tart": 91.17999999999999, "end": 94.46, "text": " is to decode this massive mathematical framework.", "tokens": [50934, 307, 281, 979, 1429, 341, 5994, 18894, 8388, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11864951871476083, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017214440506194e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 7980, "start": 94.58, "end": 98.06, "text": " Because we are going to discover a completely new way of defining understanding.", "tokens": [51104, 1436, 321, 366, 516, 281, 4411, 257, 2584, 777, 636, 295, 17827, 3701, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11864951871476083, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017214440506194e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 7980, "start": 98.32, "end": 101.88, "text": " Yes. Not as this, like, mysterious glowing spark of consciousness,", "tokens": [51291, 1079, 13, 1726, 382, 341, 11, 411, 11, 13831, 27064, 9908, 295, 10081, 11, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11864951871476083, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017214440506194e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 7980, "start": 102.12, "end": 105.78, "text": " but as a measurable geometric preservation of context.", "tokens": [51481, 457, 382, 257, 43615, 33246, 27257, 295, 4319, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11864951871476083, "compression_ratio": 1.596551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017214440506194e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10578, "start": 105.78, "end": 108.9, "text": " What's so compelling about this text is just its sheer ambition, you know?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 311, 370, 20050, 466, 341, 2487, 307, 445, 1080, 23061, 22814, 11, 291, 458, 30, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10578, "start": 109.26, "end": 113.9, "text": " Fliction is proposing we synthesize disciplines that, honestly, rarely ever speak to each other.", "tokens": [50539, 3235, 4105, 307, 29939, 321, 26617, 1125, 21919, 300, 11, 6095, 11, 13752, 1562, 1710, 281, 1184, 661, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10578, "start": 113.96000000000001, "end": 114.84, "text": " Yeah, it's a huge mix.", "tokens": [50774, 865, 11, 309, 311, 257, 2603, 2890, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10578, "start": 114.92, "end": 119.52, "text": " We're pulling from classical philosophy, category theory, topology, and modern machine learning,", "tokens": [50822, 492, 434, 8407, 490, 13735, 10675, 11, 7719, 5261, 11, 1192, 1793, 11, 293, 4363, 3479, 2539, 11, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 10578, "start": 119.86, "end": 122.92, "text": " and forcing them all into a single, cohesive picture.", "tokens": [51069, 293, 19030, 552, 439, 666, 257, 2167, 11, 43025, 3036, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 10578, "start": 123.12, "end": 125.38, "text": " Basically trying to build a semantic x-ray machine.", "tokens": [51232, 8537, 1382, 281, 1322, 257, 47982, 2031, 12, 3458, 3479, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 10578, "start": 125.7, "end": 130.02, "text": " Exactly. An internal diagnostic tool to point at a structure and say,", "tokens": [51361, 7587, 13, 1107, 6920, 27897, 2290, 281, 935, 412, 257, 3877, 293, 584, 11, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 10578, "start": 130.62, "end": 133.64, "text": " that right there is the physical geometry of understanding.", "tokens": [51607, 300, 558, 456, 307, 264, 4001, 18426, 295, 3701, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12177247619628906, "compression_ratio": 1.6018237082066868, "no_speech_prob": 1.4497489580350686e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 13364, "start": 133.64, "end": 135.88, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this from the very beginning.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 490, 264, 588, 2863, 13, 50477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 13364, "start": 136.27999999999997, "end": 140.38, "text": " Because before we can even attempt to measure a concept like understanding with math,", "tokens": [50497, 1436, 949, 321, 393, 754, 5217, 281, 3481, 257, 3410, 411, 3701, 365, 5221, 11, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 13364, "start": 140.82, "end": 144.42, "text": " we've got to deal with the reality that the word itself is incredibly loaded.", "tokens": [50724, 321, 600, 658, 281, 2028, 365, 264, 4103, 300, 264, 1349, 2564, 307, 6252, 13210, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 13364, "start": 144.7, "end": 146.38, "text": " Oh, it's a linguistic minefield.", "tokens": [50918, 876, 11, 309, 311, 257, 43002, 3892, 7610, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 13364, "start": 146.45999999999998, "end": 150.83999999999997, "text": " Right. The text argues right out of the gate that the reason philosophers and computer scientists", "tokens": [51006, 1779, 13, 440, 2487, 38218, 558, 484, 295, 264, 8539, 300, 264, 1778, 36839, 293, 3820, 7708, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 13364, "start": 150.83999999999997, "end": 155.82, "text": " are constantly screaming past each other online is because they're using the exact same word", "tokens": [51225, 366, 6460, 12636, 1791, 1184, 661, 2950, 307, 570, 436, 434, 1228, 264, 1900, 912, 1349, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 13364, "start": 155.82, "end": 158.76, "text": " to describe entirely different phenomena.", "tokens": [51474, 281, 6786, 7696, 819, 22004, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 13364, "start": 158.92, "end": 160.06, "text": " That's the starting point, yeah.", "tokens": [51629, 663, 311, 264, 2891, 935, 11, 1338, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11200941020044787, "compression_ratio": 1.627388535031847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183798650844851e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 16006, "start": 160.06, "end": 164.88, "text": " The text introduces this methodological tool called the disentanglement operator.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 31472, 341, 3170, 4383, 2290, 1219, 264, 37313, 656, 3054, 12973, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 16006, "start": 165.08, "end": 166.46, "text": " Which sounds very sci-fi.", "tokens": [50616, 3013, 3263, 588, 2180, 12, 13325, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 16006, "start": 166.54, "end": 167.1, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50689, 467, 775, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 16006, "start": 167.22, "end": 167.44, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50723, 865, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 16006, "start": 167.54, "end": 171.18, "text": " But mathematically, it's represented as a formal mapping function.", "tokens": [50739, 583, 44003, 11, 309, 311, 10379, 382, 257, 9860, 18350, 2445, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 16006, "start": 172.04, "end": 174.56, "text": " Conceptually, though, it's more like a legal injunction.", "tokens": [50964, 47482, 671, 11, 1673, 11, 309, 311, 544, 411, 257, 5089, 5580, 32627, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 16006, "start": 174.78, "end": 175.44, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51101, 1012, 370, 30, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 16006, "start": 175.64000000000001, "end": 181.0, "text": " Well, it forces us to take all those messy, entangled properties we associate with human cognition,", "tokens": [51144, 1042, 11, 309, 5874, 505, 281, 747, 439, 729, 16191, 11, 948, 39101, 7221, 321, 14644, 365, 1952, 46905, 11, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16195784332931681, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.775819183542915e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 18100, "start": 181.0, "end": 186.66, "text": " so things like phenomenal consciousness, truth, intentional agency, syntactic fluency,", "tokens": [50365, 370, 721, 411, 17778, 10081, 11, 3494, 11, 21935, 7934, 11, 23980, 19892, 5029, 3020, 11, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 18100, "start": 186.88, "end": 188.88, "text": " and strictly isolate them from one another.", "tokens": [50659, 293, 20792, 25660, 552, 490, 472, 1071, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 18100, "start": 189.08, "end": 192.42, "text": " Let's slow down on that for a second, because this is where I think a lot of people get tripped up.", "tokens": [50769, 961, 311, 2964, 760, 322, 300, 337, 257, 1150, 11, 570, 341, 307, 689, 286, 519, 257, 688, 295, 561, 483, 1376, 3320, 493, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 18100, "start": 193.28, "end": 197.66, "text": " Why do we need a mathematical operator to separate these things?", "tokens": [50979, 1545, 360, 321, 643, 257, 18894, 12973, 281, 4994, 613, 721, 30, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 18100, "start": 198.14, "end": 200.28, "text": " I mean, can't we just agree to use different words?", "tokens": [51222, 286, 914, 11, 393, 380, 321, 445, 3986, 281, 764, 819, 2283, 30, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 18100, "start": 200.66, "end": 202.24, "text": " Historically, no, we really can't.", "tokens": [51348, 25108, 984, 11, 572, 11, 321, 534, 393, 380, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 18100, "start": 202.24, "end": 204.3, "text": " Just think about the baits we see every day.", "tokens": [51427, 1449, 519, 466, 264, 16865, 82, 321, 536, 633, 786, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 18100, "start": 204.54, "end": 204.98, "text": " Yeah, true.", "tokens": [51542, 865, 11, 2074, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 18100, "start": 205.08, "end": 209.64, "text": " Someone will claim the AI doesn't really understand because it isn't conscious, right?", "tokens": [51569, 8734, 486, 3932, 264, 7318, 1177, 380, 534, 1223, 570, 309, 1943, 380, 6648, 11, 558, 30, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12073446722591624, "compression_ratio": 1.6386292834890965, "no_speech_prob": 1.304045304899304e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 20964, "start": 209.64, "end": 210.73999999999998, "text": " It doesn't feel anything.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 841, 1340, 13, 50420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 20964, "start": 210.88, "end": 215.89999999999998, "text": " And then someone else will say, well, the AI understands perfectly because it speaks fluent Spanish.", "tokens": [50427, 400, 550, 1580, 1646, 486, 584, 11, 731, 11, 264, 7318, 15146, 6239, 570, 309, 10789, 40799, 8058, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 20964, "start": 216.27999999999997, "end": 216.79999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50697, 7587, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 20964, "start": 217.17999999999998, "end": 224.07999999999998, "text": " So the disentanglement operator isolates structural semantic capacity as an independent object of mathematical investigation.", "tokens": [50742, 407, 264, 37313, 656, 3054, 12973, 7381, 1024, 15067, 47982, 6042, 382, 364, 6695, 2657, 295, 18894, 9627, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 20964, "start": 224.57999999999998, "end": 229.67999999999998, "text": " By legally separating meaning from consciousness, the text frees us up.", "tokens": [51112, 3146, 21106, 29279, 3620, 490, 10081, 11, 264, 2487, 2130, 279, 505, 493, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 20964, "start": 229.67999999999998, "end": 232.64, "text": " Frees us to study semantics as pure geometry.", "tokens": [51367, 479, 4856, 505, 281, 2979, 4361, 45298, 382, 6075, 18426, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 20964, "start": 232.88, "end": 232.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51527, 1779, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 20964, "start": 233.39999999999998, "end": 238.83999999999997, "text": " Completely sidestepping those unsolvable philosophical traps that have stalled progress for decades.", "tokens": [51553, 39978, 20822, 8887, 3759, 729, 2693, 401, 17915, 25066, 24173, 300, 362, 342, 8907, 4205, 337, 7878, 13, 51825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15799359662817158, "compression_ratio": 1.5509554140127388, "no_speech_prob": 2.0482528433757308e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 23884, "start": 238.84, "end": 239.16, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 23884, "start": 239.6, "end": 248.76, "text": " So to make this isolation super clear for you listening, the monograph outlines three very distinct frameworks for how we define understanding.", "tokens": [50403, 407, 281, 652, 341, 16001, 1687, 1850, 337, 291, 4764, 11, 264, 1108, 3108, 40125, 1045, 588, 10644, 29834, 337, 577, 321, 6964, 3701, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 23884, "start": 249.08, "end": 250.0, "text": " Let's walk through them.", "tokens": [50877, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 552, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 23884, "start": 250.16, "end": 250.34, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50931, 4894, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 23884, "start": 250.6, "end": 252.82, "text": " First up, there's phenomenological understanding.", "tokens": [50953, 2386, 493, 11, 456, 311, 9388, 4383, 3701, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 23884, "start": 253.14000000000001, "end": 253.42000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51080, 1779, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 23884, "start": 253.5, "end": 257.5, "text": " And this is the one most people intuitively default to when they interrogate an AI.", "tokens": [51098, 400, 341, 307, 264, 472, 881, 561, 46506, 7576, 281, 562, 436, 24871, 473, 364, 7318, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 23884, "start": 258.52, "end": 262.58, "text": " Phenomenological understanding is rooted entirely in subjective experience.", "tokens": [51349, 2623, 268, 4726, 4383, 3701, 307, 25277, 7696, 294, 25972, 1752, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 23884, "start": 262.8, "end": 263.88, "text": " It's the feeling of knowing.", "tokens": [51563, 467, 311, 264, 2633, 295, 5276, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 23884, "start": 264.28000000000003, "end": 264.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51637, 7587, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19724221499461048, "compression_ratio": 1.6353383458646618, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611170346540137e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 26468, "start": 264.68, "end": 266.68, "text": " It's the internal lived experience.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 264, 6920, 5152, 1752, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 26468, "start": 267.5, "end": 272.04, "text": " The classic example here is John Searle's Chinese room argument, right?", "tokens": [50506, 440, 7230, 1365, 510, 307, 2619, 1100, 36153, 311, 4649, 1808, 6770, 11, 558, 30, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 26468, "start": 272.44, "end": 279.18, "text": " Which, if you aren't familiar, is this thought experiment from 1980 that has basically haunted AI research ever since.", "tokens": [50753, 3013, 11, 498, 291, 3212, 380, 4963, 11, 307, 341, 1194, 5120, 490, 13626, 300, 575, 1936, 24878, 7318, 2132, 1562, 1670, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 26468, "start": 279.40000000000003, "end": 280.24, "text": " It really has.", "tokens": [51101, 467, 534, 575, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 26468, "start": 280.38, "end": 282.22, "text": " So imagine a person locked in a room.", "tokens": [51150, 407, 3811, 257, 954, 9376, 294, 257, 1808, 13, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 26468, "start": 282.68, "end": 284.4, "text": " They speak absolutely zero Chinese.", "tokens": [51265, 814, 1710, 3122, 4018, 4649, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 26468, "start": 285.02, "end": 287.68, "text": " But they have this massive comprehensive rule book.", "tokens": [51382, 583, 436, 362, 341, 5994, 13914, 4978, 1446, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 26468, "start": 287.92, "end": 288.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51527, 1779, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1673134014170657, "compression_ratio": 1.4900398406374502, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043339616869656e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 28816, "start": 288.16, "end": 292.6, "text": " And people outside slide pieces of paper with Chinese characters under the door.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 561, 2380, 4137, 3755, 295, 3035, 365, 4649, 4342, 833, 264, 2853, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1086148462797466, "compression_ratio": 1.8156996587030716, "no_speech_prob": 1.861049075263521e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 28816, "start": 292.72, "end": 292.8, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50593, 865, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1086148462797466, "compression_ratio": 1.8156996587030716, "no_speech_prob": 1.861049075263521e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 28816, "start": 292.88000000000005, "end": 301.96000000000004, "text": " And the person inside just looks at the shape of the character, finds it in the rule book, copies down whatever responding character the book dictates, and slides the response back out.", "tokens": [50601, 400, 264, 954, 1854, 445, 1542, 412, 264, 3909, 295, 264, 2517, 11, 10704, 309, 294, 264, 4978, 1446, 11, 14341, 760, 2035, 16670, 2517, 264, 1446, 12569, 1024, 11, 293, 9788, 264, 4134, 646, 484, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1086148462797466, "compression_ratio": 1.8156996587030716, "no_speech_prob": 1.861049075263521e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 28816, "start": 302.08000000000004, "end": 306.42, "text": " So to the people outside, they think they're having a completely fluent conversation in Chinese.", "tokens": [51061, 407, 281, 264, 561, 2380, 11, 436, 519, 436, 434, 1419, 257, 2584, 40799, 3761, 294, 4649, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1086148462797466, "compression_ratio": 1.8156996587030716, "no_speech_prob": 1.861049075263521e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 28816, "start": 306.70000000000005, "end": 309.84000000000003, "text": " But the person inside understands absolutely nothing.", "tokens": [51292, 583, 264, 954, 1854, 15146, 3122, 1825, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1086148462797466, "compression_ratio": 1.8156996587030716, "no_speech_prob": 1.861049075263521e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 28816, "start": 310.20000000000005, "end": 316.18, "text": " They're just blindly manipulating symbols based on syntax, like just looking at the shapes of the squiggles.", "tokens": [51467, 814, 434, 445, 47744, 40805, 16944, 2361, 322, 28431, 11, 411, 445, 1237, 412, 264, 10854, 295, 264, 2339, 19469, 13, 51766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1086148462797466, "compression_ratio": 1.8156996587030716, "no_speech_prob": 1.861049075263521e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 31618, "start": 316.18, "end": 316.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 31618, "start": 317.32, "end": 328.16, "text": " And Searle used this to argue that a computer program, which just follows rules to manipulate symbols, can never have true understanding no matter how human-like its output is.", "tokens": [50422, 400, 1100, 36153, 1143, 341, 281, 9695, 300, 257, 3820, 1461, 11, 597, 445, 10002, 4474, 281, 20459, 16944, 11, 393, 1128, 362, 2074, 3701, 572, 1871, 577, 1952, 12, 4092, 1080, 5598, 307, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 31618, "start": 328.22, "end": 331.68, "text": " Because it lacks that internal subjective experience.", "tokens": [50967, 1436, 309, 31132, 300, 6920, 25972, 1752, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 31618, "start": 331.8, "end": 333.9, "text": " It lacks phenomenological understanding.", "tokens": [51146, 467, 31132, 9388, 4383, 3701, 13, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 31618, "start": 334.18, "end": 334.6, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51265, 7587, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 31618, "start": 335.1, "end": 340.38, "text": " And you also have philosophers like Thomas Nagel, who wrote the Fragus essay, What Is It Like to Be a Bat?", "tokens": [51311, 400, 291, 611, 362, 36839, 411, 8500, 18913, 338, 11, 567, 4114, 264, 479, 3731, 301, 16238, 11, 708, 1119, 467, 1743, 281, 879, 257, 10066, 30, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 31618, "start": 340.64, "end": 341.08, "text": " Oh, yeah.", "tokens": [51588, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16182197570800783, "compression_ratio": 1.5018587360594795, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664819922641237e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 34108, "start": 341.08, "end": 345.88, "text": " Arguing that consciousness requires a subjective what it is like to exist as that organism.", "tokens": [50365, 48560, 278, 300, 10081, 7029, 257, 25972, 437, 309, 307, 411, 281, 2514, 382, 300, 24128, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 34108, "start": 346.2, "end": 347.56, "text": " So that's the first framework.", "tokens": [50621, 407, 300, 311, 264, 700, 8388, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 34108, "start": 347.96, "end": 351.58, "text": " But the text contrasts this with the second framework, which is functional understanding.", "tokens": [50709, 583, 264, 2487, 8712, 82, 341, 365, 264, 1150, 8388, 11, 597, 307, 11745, 3701, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 34108, "start": 352.08, "end": 352.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50915, 1779, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 34108, "start": 352.41999999999996, "end": 355.94, "text": " And functionalism swings the pendulum in the complete opposite direction.", "tokens": [50932, 400, 11745, 1434, 32386, 264, 44103, 294, 264, 3566, 6182, 3513, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 34108, "start": 355.94, "end": 359.53999999999996, "text": " It just discards the subjective internal experience entirely.", "tokens": [51108, 467, 445, 2983, 2287, 264, 25972, 6920, 1752, 7696, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 34108, "start": 359.86, "end": 360.59999999999997, "text": " It just doesn't care.", "tokens": [51304, 467, 445, 1177, 380, 1127, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 34108, "start": 360.94, "end": 361.46, "text": " Not at all.", "tokens": [51358, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 34108, "start": 361.53999999999996, "end": 365.03999999999996, "text": " It focuses solely on behavioral competence and observable performance.", "tokens": [51388, 467, 16109, 23309, 322, 19124, 39965, 293, 9951, 712, 3389, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 34108, "start": 365.28, "end": 367.12, "text": " So this is basically the Turing test.", "tokens": [51575, 407, 341, 307, 1936, 264, 314, 1345, 1500, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728817314937196, "compression_ratio": 1.6767676767676767, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815809812317783e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 36712, "start": 367.12, "end": 370.24, "text": " Yes, the Turing test is the ultimate functionalist metric.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 264, 314, 1345, 1500, 307, 264, 9705, 11745, 468, 20678, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 36712, "start": 370.9, "end": 378.12, "text": " If the machine behaves indistinguishably from a human who understands, then, well, for all practical purposes, the machine understands.", "tokens": [50554, 759, 264, 3479, 36896, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 1188, 490, 257, 1952, 567, 15146, 11, 550, 11, 731, 11, 337, 439, 8496, 9932, 11, 264, 3479, 15146, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 36712, "start": 378.32, "end": 381.74, "text": " And honestly, modern AI benchmarks operate exactly this way, don't they?", "tokens": [50925, 400, 6095, 11, 4363, 7318, 43751, 9651, 2293, 341, 636, 11, 500, 380, 436, 30, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 36712, "start": 382.34000000000003, "end": 382.86, "text": " 100%.", "tokens": [51126, 2319, 6856, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 36712, "start": 382.86, "end": 385.08, "text": " Can it pass the bar exam?", "tokens": [51152, 1664, 309, 1320, 264, 2159, 1139, 30, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 36712, "start": 385.52, "end": 387.42, "text": " Can it write a working Python script?", "tokens": [51285, 1664, 309, 2464, 257, 1364, 15329, 5755, 30, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 36712, "start": 387.66, "end": 387.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51392, 1779, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528781010554387, "compression_ratio": 1.4700854700854702, "no_speech_prob": 1.3556099602227145e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 38786, "start": 387.86, "end": 396.18, "text": " If the system acts successfully, if it predicts the next token correctly and achieves the goal, the functionalist says it possesses understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 1185, 10672, 10727, 11, 498, 309, 6069, 82, 264, 958, 14862, 8944, 293, 3538, 977, 264, 3387, 11, 264, 11745, 468, 1619, 309, 17490, 279, 3701, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 38786, "start": 396.58000000000004, "end": 403.54, "text": " The internal mechanics, whether it's feeling anything or how the weights are calculating the probability, are totally secondary.", "tokens": [50801, 440, 6920, 12939, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 2633, 1340, 420, 577, 264, 17443, 366, 28258, 264, 8482, 11, 366, 3879, 11396, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 38786, "start": 403.88, "end": 404.96000000000004, "text": " It's all about the output.", "tokens": [51166, 467, 311, 439, 466, 264, 5598, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 38786, "start": 405.14, "end": 406.92, "text": " Which brings us to the third framework.", "tokens": [51229, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2636, 8388, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 38786, "start": 407.26, "end": 409.12, "text": " And this is the entire focus of the monograph.", "tokens": [51335, 400, 341, 307, 264, 2302, 1879, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 38786, "start": 409.38, "end": 410.72, "text": " This is the big paradigm shift.", "tokens": [51441, 639, 307, 264, 955, 24709, 5513, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 38786, "start": 411.40000000000003, "end": 412.5, "text": " Structural understanding.", "tokens": [51542, 745, 1757, 1807, 3701, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480556397210984, "compression_ratio": 1.6195652173913044, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732975902973956e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 41250, "start": 412.5, "end": 413.02, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 41250, "start": 413.74, "end": 414.76, "text": " Structural understanding.", "tokens": [50427, 745, 1757, 1807, 3701, 13, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 41250, "start": 414.8, "end": 420.92, "text": " Glitch Aden defines this as the internal preservation of admissible contextual organization under transformation.", "tokens": [50480, 5209, 1549, 316, 1556, 23122, 341, 382, 264, 6920, 27257, 295, 5910, 41073, 35526, 4475, 833, 9887, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 41250, "start": 421.58, "end": 423.38, "text": " It's a dense definition, I know.", "tokens": [50819, 467, 311, 257, 18011, 7123, 11, 286, 458, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 41250, "start": 423.8, "end": 427.76, "text": " But if we break it apart, it provides the exact bridge we've been missing.", "tokens": [50930, 583, 498, 321, 1821, 309, 4936, 11, 309, 6417, 264, 1900, 7283, 321, 600, 668, 5361, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 41250, "start": 427.94, "end": 428.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51137, 1779, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 41250, "start": 428.22, "end": 432.52, "text": " Because it isn't asking how does it feel, and it isn't just looking at the final output either.", "tokens": [51151, 1436, 309, 1943, 380, 3365, 577, 775, 309, 841, 11, 293, 309, 1943, 380, 445, 1237, 412, 264, 2572, 5598, 2139, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 41250, "start": 432.52, "end": 433.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51366, 7587, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 41250, "start": 433.3, "end": 436.24, "text": " It's looking directly at the internal mechanism itself.", "tokens": [51405, 467, 311, 1237, 3838, 412, 264, 6920, 7513, 2564, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 41250, "start": 436.38, "end": 440.58, "text": " Okay, let me try an analogy here to see if I'm really grasping the distinction between these three.", "tokens": [51559, 1033, 11, 718, 385, 853, 364, 21663, 510, 281, 536, 498, 286, 478, 534, 29444, 3381, 264, 16844, 1296, 613, 1045, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 41250, "start": 440.8, "end": 441.52, "text": " It's tricky.", "tokens": [51780, 467, 311, 12414, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 41250, "start": 441.52, "end": 442.36, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [51816, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 51858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18937572962801222, "compression_ratio": 1.6484848484848484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858724923545342e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 44250, "start": 442.5, "end": 449.26, "text": " Imagine we're trying to navigate a sprawling, chaotic city like London or Tokyo.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 321, 434, 1382, 281, 12350, 257, 22734, 1688, 11, 27013, 2307, 411, 7042, 420, 15147, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 44250, "start": 449.44, "end": 450.24, "text": " Okay, I'm with you.", "tokens": [50712, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 44250, "start": 450.54, "end": 457.72, "text": " Functional understanding is like memorizing a very specific set of turn-by-turn directions to get from your hotel to a specific museum.", "tokens": [50767, 11166, 41048, 3701, 307, 411, 10560, 3319, 257, 588, 2685, 992, 295, 1261, 12, 2322, 12, 33886, 11095, 281, 483, 490, 428, 7622, 281, 257, 2685, 8441, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 44250, "start": 458.12, "end": 462.4, "text": " You take a left at the toffee shop, a right at the train station, and boom, you arrive.", "tokens": [51146, 509, 747, 257, 1411, 412, 264, 281, 4617, 3945, 11, 257, 558, 412, 264, 3847, 5214, 11, 293, 9351, 11, 291, 8881, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 44250, "start": 462.62, "end": 465.38, "text": " You acted successfully, you achieved the goal.", "tokens": [51371, 509, 20359, 10727, 11, 291, 11042, 264, 3387, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 44250, "start": 465.54, "end": 465.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51517, 1779, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 44250, "start": 466.08, "end": 470.1, "text": " But if I drop you two streets over from your normal route, you are completely lost.", "tokens": [51544, 583, 498, 286, 3270, 291, 732, 8481, 670, 490, 428, 2710, 7955, 11, 291, 366, 2584, 2731, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10927940209706624, "compression_ratio": 1.5876288659793814, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358474150955e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 47010, "start": 470.1, "end": 472.5, "text": " Because you only know the sequence, not the space.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 291, 787, 458, 264, 8310, 11, 406, 264, 1901, 13, 50485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342733909343852, "compression_ratio": 1.4610778443113772, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759228111869808e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 47010, "start": 472.6, "end": 473.08000000000004, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50490, 7587, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342733909343852, "compression_ratio": 1.4610778443113772, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759228111869808e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 47010, "start": 473.72, "end": 477.02000000000004, "text": " Now, phenomenological understanding is the subjective experience of the city.", "tokens": [50546, 823, 11, 9388, 4383, 3701, 307, 264, 25972, 1752, 295, 264, 2307, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342733909343852, "compression_ratio": 1.4610778443113772, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759228111869808e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 47010, "start": 477.40000000000003, "end": 483.34000000000003, "text": " It's feeling the cold rain, smelling the exhaust and the street food, feeling the exhaustion in your legs.", "tokens": [50730, 467, 311, 2633, 264, 3554, 4830, 11, 35471, 264, 14687, 293, 264, 4838, 1755, 11, 2633, 264, 47408, 294, 428, 5668, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342733909343852, "compression_ratio": 1.4610778443113772, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759228111869808e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 48334, "start": 483.34, "end": 486.88, "text": " It's what it is like to actually be a pedestrian in London.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 437, 309, 307, 411, 281, 767, 312, 257, 33947, 294, 7042, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24906973157610213, "compression_ratio": 1.1666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830312763085661e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 48334, "start": 487.08, "end": 487.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50552, 7587, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24906973157610213, "compression_ratio": 1.1666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830312763085661e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 48334, "start": 488.02, "end": 492.03999999999996, "text": " So how does structural understanding fit into this city analogy?", "tokens": [50599, 407, 577, 775, 15067, 3701, 3318, 666, 341, 2307, 21663, 30, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24906973157610213, "compression_ratio": 1.1666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830312763085661e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 49204, "start": 492.04, "end": 499.20000000000005, "text": " Well, structural understanding is possessing an internal, perfectly scaled map of the city's geometry in your head.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 15067, 3701, 307, 17490, 278, 364, 6920, 11, 6239, 36039, 4471, 295, 264, 2307, 311, 18426, 294, 428, 1378, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18111027081807454, "compression_ratio": 1.1782178217821782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378106994936135e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 49204, "start": 499.54, "end": 499.68, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [50740, 876, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18111027081807454, "compression_ratio": 1.1782178217821782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378106994936135e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 49968, "start": 499.68, "end": 503.42, "text": " You aren't just blindly following a memorized sequence of turns.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 3212, 380, 445, 47744, 3480, 257, 46677, 8310, 295, 4523, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 49968, "start": 504.02, "end": 507.40000000000003, "text": " You have an internal model of how the streets relate to one another.", "tokens": [50582, 509, 362, 364, 6920, 2316, 295, 577, 264, 8481, 10961, 281, 472, 1071, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 49968, "start": 507.7, "end": 510.98, "text": " So if a road is suddenly blocked by construction, I don't just freeze up or fail.", "tokens": [50766, 407, 498, 257, 3060, 307, 5800, 15470, 538, 6435, 11, 286, 500, 380, 445, 15959, 493, 420, 3061, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 49968, "start": 511.3, "end": 511.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50946, 1779, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 49968, "start": 511.72, "end": 519.16, "text": " You can mentally calculate a completely new route because you've preserved the spatial relationships, the context of the city's grid.", "tokens": [50967, 509, 393, 17072, 8873, 257, 2584, 777, 7955, 570, 291, 600, 22242, 264, 23598, 6159, 11, 264, 4319, 295, 264, 2307, 311, 10748, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 49968, "start": 519.28, "end": 520.5600000000001, "text": " Okay, that tracks perfectly.", "tokens": [51345, 1033, 11, 300, 10218, 6239, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 49968, "start": 520.6800000000001, "end": 521.82, "text": " It makes so much sense.", "tokens": [51415, 467, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 49968, "start": 521.92, "end": 522.0600000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51477, 865, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 49968, "start": 522.1800000000001, "end": 525.24, "text": " Structural understanding is all about preserving relational boundaries.", "tokens": [51490, 745, 1757, 1807, 3701, 307, 439, 466, 33173, 38444, 13180, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12240644981121195, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404733052724271e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 52524, "start": 525.24, "end": 535.22, "text": " It asks, as a system takes in data and transforms its internal state to generate a response, do the relationships between the concepts remain stable?", "tokens": [50365, 467, 8962, 11, 382, 257, 1185, 2516, 294, 1412, 293, 35592, 1080, 6920, 1785, 281, 8460, 257, 4134, 11, 360, 264, 6159, 1296, 264, 10392, 6222, 8351, 30, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09646356427991712, "compression_ratio": 1.647887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 52524, "start": 535.42, "end": 536.5, "text": " Do they remain invariant?", "tokens": [50874, 1144, 436, 6222, 33270, 394, 30, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09646356427991712, "compression_ratio": 1.647887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 52524, "start": 536.64, "end": 536.94, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50935, 1079, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09646356427991712, "compression_ratio": 1.647887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 52524, "start": 537.24, "end": 549.12, "text": " And this is a massive shift because it moves the study of meaning entirely away from psychology or biology or behavioral testing and just drops it directly into the realm of mathematics and topology.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 341, 307, 257, 5994, 5513, 570, 309, 6067, 264, 2979, 295, 3620, 7696, 1314, 490, 15105, 420, 14956, 420, 19124, 4997, 293, 445, 11438, 309, 3838, 666, 264, 15355, 295, 18666, 293, 1192, 1793, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09646356427991712, "compression_ratio": 1.647887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 52524, "start": 549.36, "end": 553.08, "text": " I see where this is going, but I have to throw a flag on the play here.", "tokens": [51571, 286, 536, 689, 341, 307, 516, 11, 457, 286, 362, 281, 3507, 257, 7166, 322, 264, 862, 510, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09646356427991712, "compression_ratio": 1.647887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 52524, "start": 553.14, "end": 554.12, "text": " Oh, what is it?", "tokens": [51760, 876, 11, 437, 307, 309, 30, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09646356427991712, "compression_ratio": 1.647887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 55412, "start": 554.12, "end": 562.74, "text": " I want to push back on this idea of the internal map because AI hallucination is arguably the biggest problem in the industry right now.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 528, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 1558, 295, 264, 6920, 4471, 570, 7318, 35212, 2486, 307, 26771, 264, 3880, 1154, 294, 264, 3518, 558, 586, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 55412, "start": 562.92, "end": 563.4, "text": " Undoubtedly.", "tokens": [50805, 2719, 32135, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 55412, "start": 563.66, "end": 568.0, "text": " A language model will confidently tell you that the Golden Gate Bridge was built in 2015.", "tokens": [50842, 316, 2856, 2316, 486, 41956, 980, 291, 300, 264, 13410, 21913, 18917, 390, 3094, 294, 7546, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 55412, "start": 569.26, "end": 574.26, "text": " If it has this structural understanding, this internal map, shouldn't it be tethered to reality?", "tokens": [51122, 759, 309, 575, 341, 15067, 3701, 11, 341, 6920, 4471, 11, 4659, 380, 309, 312, 256, 1666, 292, 281, 4103, 30, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 55412, "start": 574.44, "end": 575.82, "text": " Shouldn't it be factually accurate?", "tokens": [51381, 34170, 380, 309, 312, 1186, 671, 8559, 30, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 55412, "start": 576.16, "end": 576.4, "text": " Ugh.", "tokens": [51467, 16506, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 55412, "start": 577.0, "end": 581.26, "text": " See, that is the exact trap the disentanglement operator was built to avoid.", "tokens": [51509, 3008, 11, 300, 307, 264, 1900, 11487, 264, 37313, 656, 3054, 12973, 390, 3094, 281, 5042, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 55412, "start": 581.4, "end": 581.74, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51729, 4083, 30, 51746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 55412, "start": 582.04, "end": 582.52, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51761, 1012, 370, 30, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12088599205017089, "compression_ratio": 1.5824915824915824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468275953670288e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 58252, "start": 582.52, "end": 586.0799999999999, "text": " You're conflating structural semantics with veridical truth.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 434, 1497, 75, 990, 15067, 4361, 45298, 365, 1306, 327, 804, 3494, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 58252, "start": 586.42, "end": 589.12, "text": " The text is very, very strict on this point.", "tokens": [50560, 440, 2487, 307, 588, 11, 588, 10910, 322, 341, 935, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 58252, "start": 589.4, "end": 590.38, "text": " Truth is external.", "tokens": [50709, 20522, 307, 8320, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 58252, "start": 590.6999999999999, "end": 592.36, "text": " Meaning it's outside the system.", "tokens": [50774, 19948, 309, 311, 2380, 264, 1185, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 58252, "start": 592.52, "end": 592.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50865, 1779, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 58252, "start": 593.0799999999999, "end": 596.74, "text": " Truth is a correspondence between a statement and the physical world.", "tokens": [50893, 20522, 307, 257, 38135, 1296, 257, 5629, 293, 264, 4001, 1002, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 58252, "start": 597.28, "end": 601.86, "text": " Structural understanding, however, is purely about internal coherence.", "tokens": [51103, 745, 1757, 1807, 3701, 11, 4461, 11, 307, 17491, 466, 6920, 26528, 655, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 58252, "start": 601.9399999999999, "end": 602.14, "text": " Wait.", "tokens": [51336, 3802, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 58252, "start": 602.52, "end": 607.9, "text": " So a system can have perfect structural understanding of something that is completely factually false?", "tokens": [51365, 407, 257, 1185, 393, 362, 2176, 15067, 3701, 295, 746, 300, 307, 2584, 1186, 671, 7908, 30, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13568517073844244, "compression_ratio": 1.649402390438247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949221973844297e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 60790, "start": 607.9, "end": 608.38, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [50365, 7021, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2992459452429483, "compression_ratio": 1.2554744525547445, "no_speech_prob": 2.4078050751136226e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 60790, "start": 608.5, "end": 612.16, "text": " Consider a meticulously crafted fantasy universe.", "tokens": [50395, 17416, 257, 41566, 25038, 36213, 13861, 6445, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2992459452429483, "compression_ratio": 1.2554744525547445, "no_speech_prob": 2.4078050751136226e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 60790, "start": 612.36, "end": 618.52, "text": " Let's say the rules of magic in the Harry Potter universe or the political geography of Game of Thrones.", "tokens": [50588, 961, 311, 584, 264, 4474, 295, 5585, 294, 264, 9378, 18115, 6445, 420, 264, 3905, 26695, 295, 7522, 295, 31659, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2992459452429483, "compression_ratio": 1.2554744525547445, "no_speech_prob": 2.4078050751136226e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 60790, "start": 618.92, "end": 619.0799999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50916, 865, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2992459452429483, "compression_ratio": 1.2554744525547445, "no_speech_prob": 2.4078050751136226e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 61908, "start": 619.08, "end": 620.64, "text": " These things do not exist.", "tokens": [50365, 1981, 721, 360, 406, 2514, 13, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2248481224323141, "compression_ratio": 1.1333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549003920701688e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 61908, "start": 621.0400000000001, "end": 625.26, "text": " They possess zero veridical truth in our physical reality.", "tokens": [50463, 814, 17490, 4018, 1306, 327, 804, 3494, 294, 527, 4001, 4103, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2248481224323141, "compression_ratio": 1.1333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549003920701688e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 61908, "start": 625.34, "end": 625.9200000000001, "text": " Quite obviously.", "tokens": [50678, 20464, 2745, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2248481224323141, "compression_ratio": 1.1333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549003920701688e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 62592, "start": 625.92, "end": 638.02, "text": " Yet if an AI is generating a story set in Westeros and it maintains the internal rule that a character cannot travel from Winterfell to King's Landing in 10 minutes, it is demonstrating profound structural understanding of that context.", "tokens": [50365, 10890, 498, 364, 7318, 307, 17746, 257, 1657, 992, 294, 343, 3011, 329, 293, 309, 33385, 264, 6920, 4978, 300, 257, 2517, 2644, 3147, 490, 16444, 69, 898, 281, 3819, 311, 49458, 294, 1266, 2077, 11, 309, 307, 29889, 14382, 15067, 3701, 295, 300, 4319, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07575243473052978, "compression_ratio": 1.4390243902439024, "no_speech_prob": 1.97291293545232e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 63802, "start": 638.02, "end": 638.52, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 63802, "start": 638.6999999999999, "end": 638.92, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50399, 1033, 13, 50410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 63802, "start": 639.34, "end": 641.92, "text": " It is preserving the internal constraint structure.", "tokens": [50431, 467, 307, 33173, 264, 6920, 25534, 3877, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 63802, "start": 642.04, "end": 642.26, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50566, 48746, 736, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 63802, "start": 642.26, "end": 650.9399999999999, "text": " But if it suddenly writes a scene where, I don't know, a dragon is revealed to be a normal human accountant from Chicago who commutes via the subway.", "tokens": [50577, 583, 498, 309, 5800, 13657, 257, 4145, 689, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 257, 12165, 307, 9599, 281, 312, 257, 2710, 1952, 43898, 490, 9525, 567, 800, 1819, 5766, 264, 24953, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 63802, "start": 651.0799999999999, "end": 652.42, "text": " Then it hasn't just told a lie.", "tokens": [51018, 1396, 309, 6132, 380, 445, 1907, 257, 4544, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 63802, "start": 652.8199999999999, "end": 656.84, "text": " It has violated the structural boundary of the context it was operating within.", "tokens": [51105, 467, 575, 33239, 264, 15067, 12866, 295, 264, 4319, 309, 390, 7447, 1951, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17238984483011652, "compression_ratio": 1.480349344978166, "no_speech_prob": 2.280164121751249e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 65684, "start": 656.84, "end": 660.3000000000001, "text": " The map warped in a way that violated its own rules.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4471, 1516, 3452, 294, 257, 636, 300, 33239, 1080, 1065, 4474, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13441186202199837, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.838098245999676e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 65684, "start": 660.52, "end": 660.7800000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50549, 1079, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13441186202199837, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.838098245999676e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 65684, "start": 661.46, "end": 669.8000000000001, "text": " Structural semantics evaluates the preservation of those internal rules, regardless of whether the map corresponds to a physical territory on Earth.", "tokens": [50596, 745, 1757, 1807, 4361, 45298, 6133, 1024, 264, 27257, 295, 729, 6920, 4474, 11, 10060, 295, 1968, 264, 4471, 23249, 281, 257, 4001, 11360, 322, 4755, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13441186202199837, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.838098245999676e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 65684, "start": 669.96, "end": 672.2800000000001, "text": " That distinction is incredibly helpful.", "tokens": [51021, 663, 16844, 307, 6252, 4961, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13441186202199837, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.838098245999676e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 65684, "start": 672.44, "end": 676.4200000000001, "text": " It's about internal geometric integrity, not external fact checking.", "tokens": [51145, 467, 311, 466, 6920, 33246, 16000, 11, 406, 8320, 1186, 8568, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13441186202199837, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.838098245999676e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 65684, "start": 676.52, "end": 676.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51349, 7587, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13441186202199837, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.838098245999676e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 67690, "start": 676.9, "end": 684.74, "text": " So if structural understanding is this dynamic internal map of rules and relations, where does the author even pull this concept from?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 15067, 3701, 307, 341, 8546, 6920, 4471, 295, 4474, 293, 2299, 11, 689, 775, 264, 3793, 754, 2235, 341, 3410, 490, 30, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 67690, "start": 685.4599999999999, "end": 689.0799999999999, "text": " Because building a math framework for this requires some pretty deep foundations.", "tokens": [50793, 1436, 2390, 257, 5221, 8388, 337, 341, 7029, 512, 1238, 2452, 22467, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 67690, "start": 689.36, "end": 689.84, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50988, 467, 775, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 67690, "start": 690.12, "end": 695.12, "text": " And the text synthesizes ideas from two places that seem, on the surface, totally disconnected.", "tokens": [51026, 400, 264, 2487, 26617, 5660, 3487, 490, 732, 3190, 300, 1643, 11, 322, 264, 3753, 11, 3879, 29426, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 67690, "start": 695.28, "end": 695.4599999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51284, 1779, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 67690, "start": 695.66, "end": 700.04, "text": " 20th century structural linguistics and Alfred North Whitehead's process philosophy.", "tokens": [51303, 945, 392, 4901, 15067, 21766, 6006, 293, 28327, 4067, 5552, 1934, 311, 1399, 10675, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 67690, "start": 700.18, "end": 702.6999999999999, "text": " It's a really audacious intellectual lineage.", "tokens": [51529, 467, 311, 257, 534, 2379, 22641, 12576, 38257, 13, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 67690, "start": 702.84, "end": 705.52, "text": " Let's tackle the linguistics first because it sets the stage perfectly.", "tokens": [51662, 961, 311, 14896, 264, 21766, 6006, 700, 570, 309, 6352, 264, 3233, 6239, 13, 51796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126976567455846, "compression_ratio": 1.6139817629179332, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674008315216814e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 70552, "start": 705.52, "end": 712.02, "text": " Affliction leans heavily on figures like Ferdinand de Saussure and later theorists like Louis Chelmslow.", "tokens": [50365, 12840, 75, 4105, 476, 599, 10950, 322, 9624, 411, 479, 7783, 259, 474, 368, 6299, 2023, 540, 293, 1780, 27423, 1751, 411, 9763, 24345, 2592, 14107, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 70552, "start": 712.68, "end": 716.02, "text": " Now, Saussure is essentially the father of structuralism, right?", "tokens": [50723, 823, 11, 6299, 2023, 540, 307, 4476, 264, 3086, 295, 15067, 1434, 11, 558, 30, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 70552, "start": 716.14, "end": 716.4399999999999, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [50896, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 70552, "start": 716.66, "end": 722.42, "text": " And his big revelation was that a word, in isolation, has no meaning whatsoever.", "tokens": [50922, 400, 702, 955, 23456, 390, 300, 257, 1349, 11, 294, 16001, 11, 575, 572, 3620, 17076, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 70552, "start": 722.56, "end": 722.9399999999999, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51217, 12753, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 70552, "start": 723.62, "end": 731.06, "text": " Saussure argued that meaning doesn't reside in a word itself, as if the word were a little bucket carrying a concept inside it.", "tokens": [51270, 6299, 2023, 540, 20219, 300, 3620, 1177, 380, 40134, 294, 257, 1349, 2564, 11, 382, 498, 264, 1349, 645, 257, 707, 13058, 9792, 257, 3410, 1854, 309, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 70552, "start": 731.12, "end": 731.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51645, 1779, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18107855856955588, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982029489911234e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 73130, "start": 731.3, "end": 736.16, "text": " Instead, meaning exists strictly in the relational network of differences between words.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 11, 3620, 8198, 20792, 294, 264, 38444, 3209, 295, 7300, 1296, 2283, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13993375095320337, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552080023101267e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 73130, "start": 736.5, "end": 747.66, "text": " A signifier, like the sound of a word, and a signify, the concept it points to, only acquire value based on how they contrast with every other sign in the surrounding linguistic system.", "tokens": [50625, 316, 1465, 9902, 11, 411, 264, 1626, 295, 257, 1349, 11, 293, 257, 1465, 2505, 11, 264, 3410, 309, 2793, 281, 11, 787, 20001, 2158, 2361, 322, 577, 436, 8712, 365, 633, 661, 1465, 294, 264, 11498, 43002, 1185, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13993375095320337, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552080023101267e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 73130, "start": 747.9, "end": 751.64, "text": " It's the idea of defining a shape by the negative space around it.", "tokens": [51195, 467, 311, 264, 1558, 295, 17827, 257, 3909, 538, 264, 3671, 1901, 926, 309, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13993375095320337, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552080023101267e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 73130, "start": 751.7199999999999, "end": 752.0799999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51386, 7587, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13993375095320337, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552080023101267e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 75208, "start": 752.08, "end": 758.34, "text": " Like, to use a really simple example, the concept of cold only has meaning because it is structurally opposed to hot, warm, and freezing.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 281, 764, 257, 534, 2199, 1365, 11, 264, 3410, 295, 3554, 787, 575, 3620, 570, 309, 307, 6594, 6512, 8851, 281, 2368, 11, 4561, 11, 293, 20200, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10054779052734375, "compression_ratio": 1.2456140350877194, "no_speech_prob": 1.796756428536217e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 75208, "start": 758.5, "end": 758.9000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50686, 1079, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10054779052734375, "compression_ratio": 1.2456140350877194, "no_speech_prob": 1.796756428536217e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 75890, "start": 758.9, "end": 762.9599999999999, "text": " If you remove the rest of that temperature network, the word cold just kind of floats in the void.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 4159, 264, 1472, 295, 300, 4292, 3209, 11, 264, 1349, 3554, 445, 733, 295, 37878, 294, 264, 22009, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 75890, "start": 763.04, "end": 764.18, "text": " It becomes totally meaningless.", "tokens": [50572, 467, 3643, 3879, 33232, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 75890, "start": 764.3199999999999, "end": 764.84, "text": " You got it.", "tokens": [50636, 509, 658, 309, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 75890, "start": 764.98, "end": 766.4, "text": " Meaning is a network topology.", "tokens": [50669, 19948, 307, 257, 3209, 1192, 1793, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 75890, "start": 767.18, "end": 772.4, "text": " Infliction takes this structuralist insight and stretches it far beyond just human language.", "tokens": [50779, 682, 3423, 4105, 2516, 341, 15067, 468, 11269, 293, 29058, 309, 1400, 4399, 445, 1952, 2856, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 75890, "start": 772.78, "end": 782.16, "text": " Well, instead of studying systems of linguistic signs like words and grammar structural semantics, studies systems of admissible computational transformations.", "tokens": [51059, 1042, 11, 2602, 295, 7601, 3652, 295, 43002, 7880, 411, 2283, 293, 22317, 15067, 4361, 45298, 11, 5313, 3652, 295, 5910, 41073, 28270, 34852, 13, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 75890, "start": 782.84, "end": 785.96, "text": " So the relations aren't just between vocabulary words anymore.", "tokens": [51562, 407, 264, 2299, 3212, 380, 445, 1296, 19864, 2283, 3602, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13156539089274857, "compression_ratio": 1.6804123711340206, "no_speech_prob": 2.1848070227981076e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 78596, "start": 785.96, "end": 790.14, "text": " Right. They are between the mathematical states of a computational system.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 814, 366, 1296, 264, 18894, 4368, 295, 257, 28270, 1185, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 78596, "start": 790.3000000000001, "end": 794.12, "text": " Wow. Which opens the door to the second major influence.", "tokens": [50582, 3153, 13, 3013, 9870, 264, 2853, 281, 264, 1150, 2563, 6503, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 78596, "start": 794.5, "end": 797.86, "text": " And I got to say, this one is notoriously difficult to grasp.", "tokens": [50792, 400, 286, 658, 281, 584, 11, 341, 472, 307, 46772, 8994, 2252, 281, 21743, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 78596, "start": 798.48, "end": 800.9000000000001, "text": " Alfred North Whitehead and Process Philosophy.", "tokens": [50991, 28327, 4067, 5552, 1934, 293, 31093, 43655, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 78596, "start": 801.12, "end": 803.32, "text": " Oh, yes. Whitehead is tough.", "tokens": [51123, 876, 11, 2086, 13, 5552, 1934, 307, 4930, 13, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 78596, "start": 803.4200000000001, "end": 805.7800000000001, "text": " He wrote Process and Reality in 1929.", "tokens": [51238, 634, 4114, 31093, 293, 33822, 294, 1294, 11871, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 78596, "start": 806.6600000000001, "end": 811.1800000000001, "text": " And I will fully admit, my philosophy background hits a total brick wall with Whitehead.", "tokens": [51400, 400, 286, 486, 4498, 9796, 11, 452, 10675, 3678, 8664, 257, 3217, 16725, 2929, 365, 5552, 1934, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 78596, "start": 811.34, "end": 813.0400000000001, "text": " You are definitely not alone in that.", "tokens": [51634, 509, 366, 2138, 406, 3312, 294, 300, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16186660419810903, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.927915726368523e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 81304, "start": 813.04, "end": 820.24, "text": " Whitehead is incredibly dense because he was attempting a total inversion of how Western science and metaphysics view reality.", "tokens": [50365, 5552, 1934, 307, 6252, 18011, 570, 415, 390, 22001, 257, 3217, 43576, 295, 577, 8724, 3497, 293, 30946, 41732, 1910, 4103, 13, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1223562771512061, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148921171994402e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 81304, "start": 820.68, "end": 821.2199999999999, "text": " Okay. How so?", "tokens": [50747, 1033, 13, 1012, 370, 30, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1223562771512061, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148921171994402e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 81304, "start": 821.56, "end": 827.16, "text": " Well, classical thought, going all the way back to Aristotle, treats reality as being composed of static objects.", "tokens": [50791, 1042, 11, 13735, 1194, 11, 516, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 42368, 11, 19566, 4103, 382, 885, 18204, 295, 13437, 6565, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1223562771512061, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148921171994402e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 81304, "start": 827.66, "end": 831.3199999999999, "text": " Substances, matter, that occasionally undergo changes or move through space.", "tokens": [51096, 42090, 2676, 11, 1871, 11, 300, 16895, 26426, 2962, 420, 1286, 807, 1901, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1223562771512061, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148921171994402e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 81304, "start": 831.4, "end": 836.02, "text": " Right. The universe is basically a pool table and atoms are the billiard balls bouncing off each other.", "tokens": [51283, 1779, 13, 440, 6445, 307, 1936, 257, 7005, 3199, 293, 16871, 366, 264, 2961, 72, 515, 9803, 27380, 766, 1184, 661, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1223562771512061, "compression_ratio": 1.5371024734982333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7148921171994402e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 83602, "start": 836.02, "end": 844.4399999999999, "text": " Exactly. But Whitehead looked at the advent of quantum mechanics and relativity and said, the pool table model is entirely wrong.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 583, 5552, 1934, 2956, 412, 264, 7045, 295, 13018, 12939, 293, 45675, 293, 848, 11, 264, 7005, 3199, 2316, 307, 7696, 2085, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15857228888086525, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983193501351023e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 83602, "start": 844.88, "end": 845.76, "text": " So what's his model?", "tokens": [50808, 407, 437, 311, 702, 2316, 30, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15857228888086525, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983193501351023e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 83602, "start": 846.1999999999999, "end": 849.64, "text": " He argued reality is not fundamentally made of objects.", "tokens": [50874, 634, 20219, 4103, 307, 406, 17879, 1027, 295, 6565, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15857228888086525, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983193501351023e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 83602, "start": 849.84, "end": 855.16, "text": " It is fundamentally made of events or processes, which he termed actual occasions.", "tokens": [51056, 467, 307, 17879, 1027, 295, 3931, 420, 7555, 11, 597, 415, 1433, 292, 3539, 20641, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15857228888086525, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983193501351023e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 83602, "start": 855.48, "end": 858.18, "text": " So he prioritized the verb over the noun.", "tokens": [51338, 407, 415, 14846, 1602, 264, 9595, 670, 264, 23307, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15857228888086525, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983193501351023e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 83602, "start": 858.46, "end": 858.84, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51487, 1079, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15857228888086525, "compression_ratio": 1.5203619909502262, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983193501351023e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 85884, "start": 858.84, "end": 862.26, "text": " Like, a mountain isn't a static rock object.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 257, 6937, 1943, 380, 257, 13437, 3727, 2657, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 85884, "start": 862.6600000000001, "end": 869.44, "text": " It's a very slow, highly persistent pattern of geological events happening over a long period of time.", "tokens": [50556, 467, 311, 257, 588, 2964, 11, 5405, 24315, 5102, 295, 1519, 4383, 3931, 2737, 670, 257, 938, 2896, 295, 565, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 85884, "start": 869.52, "end": 870.7, "text": " That is a perfect way to put it.", "tokens": [50899, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 85884, "start": 871.1800000000001, "end": 876.88, "text": " And to explain how these events interact, Whitehead built a complex system with several key components.", "tokens": [50982, 400, 281, 2903, 577, 613, 3931, 4648, 11, 5552, 1934, 3094, 257, 3997, 1185, 365, 2940, 2141, 6677, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 85884, "start": 877.2800000000001, "end": 878.48, "text": " The first one is prehension.", "tokens": [51287, 440, 700, 472, 307, 659, 71, 3378, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 85884, "start": 878.76, "end": 879.74, "text": " Right. Prehension.", "tokens": [51361, 1779, 13, 6001, 71, 3378, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 85884, "start": 880.2800000000001, "end": 884.96, "text": " The text mentions prehension can be positive or negative, and I definitely struggled with this a bit.", "tokens": [51437, 440, 2487, 23844, 659, 71, 3378, 393, 312, 3353, 420, 3671, 11, 293, 286, 2138, 19023, 365, 341, 257, 857, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11158025586927259, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.350992017909447e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 88496, "start": 884.96, "end": 893.72, "text": " It's tricky. Basically, prehension is the mechanism by which an actual occasion, an event, incorporates data from past occasions into its own becoming.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 12414, 13, 8537, 11, 659, 71, 3378, 307, 264, 7513, 538, 597, 364, 3539, 9674, 11, 364, 2280, 11, 50193, 1412, 490, 1791, 20641, 666, 1080, 1065, 5617, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072793761296059, "compression_ratio": 1.8291139240506329, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215776993065088e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 88496, "start": 894.08, "end": 896.36, "text": " Okay. So what's the difference between positive and negative?", "tokens": [50821, 1033, 13, 407, 437, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 3353, 293, 3671, 30, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072793761296059, "compression_ratio": 1.8291139240506329, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215776993065088e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 88496, "start": 896.5600000000001, "end": 898.98, "text": " Think of positive prehension as active inclusion.", "tokens": [50945, 6557, 295, 3353, 659, 71, 3378, 382, 4967, 15874, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072793761296059, "compression_ratio": 1.8291139240506329, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215776993065088e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 88496, "start": 899.52, "end": 905.0600000000001, "text": " Say you're walking down the street and you actively take in the data of a stop sign and you incorporate it into your decision to stop.", "tokens": [51093, 6463, 291, 434, 4494, 760, 264, 4838, 293, 291, 13022, 747, 294, 264, 1412, 295, 257, 1590, 1465, 293, 291, 16091, 309, 666, 428, 3537, 281, 1590, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072793761296059, "compression_ratio": 1.8291139240506329, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215776993065088e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 88496, "start": 905.3000000000001, "end": 907.4200000000001, "text": " Negative prehension is active exclusion.", "tokens": [51382, 43230, 659, 71, 3378, 307, 4967, 33049, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072793761296059, "compression_ratio": 1.8291139240506329, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215776993065088e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 88496, "start": 908.22, "end": 914.48, "text": " You prehend the sound of distant traffic, but you actively relegate it to the background so you can focus on the person you're talking to.", "tokens": [51528, 509, 659, 71, 521, 264, 1626, 295, 17275, 6419, 11, 457, 291, 13022, 2951, 22514, 309, 281, 264, 3678, 370, 291, 393, 1879, 322, 264, 954, 291, 434, 1417, 281, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072793761296059, "compression_ratio": 1.8291139240506329, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215776993065088e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 91448, "start": 914.48, "end": 918.36, "text": " Ah. So negative prehension isn't just ignoring data.", "tokens": [50365, 2438, 13, 407, 3671, 659, 71, 3378, 1943, 380, 445, 26258, 1412, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 91448, "start": 918.5, "end": 920.86, "text": " Right. It is the structural act of walling it off.", "tokens": [50566, 1779, 13, 467, 307, 264, 15067, 605, 295, 2929, 278, 309, 766, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 91448, "start": 920.94, "end": 924.66, "text": " Got it. Okay. So you have all these positive and negative prehensions gathering data.", "tokens": [50688, 5803, 309, 13, 1033, 13, 407, 291, 362, 439, 613, 3353, 293, 3671, 659, 71, 8302, 13519, 1412, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 91448, "start": 925.0, "end": 928.96, "text": " And then Whitehead introduces concrescence.", "tokens": [50891, 400, 550, 5552, 1934, 31472, 1588, 495, 25434, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 91448, "start": 929.1, "end": 930.14, "text": " Yes, concrescence.", "tokens": [51096, 1079, 11, 1588, 495, 25434, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 91448, "start": 930.32, "end": 936.9, "text": " Which is the process of integrating all of those disparate prehensions into one completed unified state.", "tokens": [51157, 3013, 307, 264, 1399, 295, 26889, 439, 295, 729, 14548, 473, 659, 71, 8302, 666, 472, 7365, 26787, 1785, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 91448, "start": 936.96, "end": 938.54, "text": " Like the event crystallizes.", "tokens": [51489, 1743, 264, 2280, 31924, 5660, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 91448, "start": 938.64, "end": 943.1, "text": " So many become one and are increased by one, as Whitehead famously put it.", "tokens": [51573, 407, 867, 1813, 472, 293, 366, 6505, 538, 472, 11, 382, 5552, 1934, 34360, 829, 309, 13, 51796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12537108965156493, "compression_ratio": 1.7137546468401488, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564803577267859e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 94310, "start": 943.1, "end": 948.5600000000001, "text": " But here is where the tension arises and where Fliction draws this massive controversial line in the sand of the text.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 510, 307, 689, 264, 8980, 27388, 293, 689, 3235, 4105, 20045, 341, 5994, 17323, 1622, 294, 264, 4932, 295, 264, 2487, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 94310, "start": 949.26, "end": 953.02, "text": " Whitehead's system includes a final component called subjective form.", "tokens": [50673, 5552, 1934, 311, 1185, 5974, 257, 2572, 6542, 1219, 25972, 1254, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 94310, "start": 953.2, "end": 953.82, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50870, 467, 775, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 94310, "start": 953.82, "end": 959.22, "text": " The subjective form is the intrinsic phenomenal experience of that becoming, right?", "tokens": [50901, 440, 25972, 1254, 307, 264, 35698, 17778, 1752, 295, 300, 5617, 11, 558, 30, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 94310, "start": 959.28, "end": 961.76, "text": " It's the emotional or subjective tone of the event.", "tokens": [51174, 467, 311, 264, 6863, 420, 25972, 8027, 295, 264, 2280, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 94310, "start": 961.98, "end": 964.34, "text": " It's what it feels like for the concrescence to occur.", "tokens": [51309, 467, 311, 437, 309, 3417, 411, 337, 264, 1588, 495, 25434, 281, 5160, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 94310, "start": 964.52, "end": 964.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51436, 7587, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14718256498637952, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856376541639738e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 96490, "start": 964.9, "end": 967.6, "text": " And here is where the monograph gets incredibly ruthless.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 307, 689, 264, 1108, 3108, 2170, 6252, 47096, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12026948826287383, "compression_ratio": 1.749034749034749, "no_speech_prob": 1.3503252335733684e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 96490, "start": 968.5, "end": 971.68, "text": " Fliction introduces a mathematical concept called the translation functor.", "tokens": [50545, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 18894, 3410, 1219, 264, 12853, 1019, 1672, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12026948826287383, "compression_ratio": 1.749034749034749, "no_speech_prob": 1.3503252335733684e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 96490, "start": 972.0, "end": 973.54, "text": " This is a pivotal moment in the book.", "tokens": [50720, 639, 307, 257, 39078, 1623, 294, 264, 1446, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12026948826287383, "compression_ratio": 1.749034749034749, "no_speech_prob": 1.3503252335733684e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 96490, "start": 973.68, "end": 981.86, "text": " He's taking Whitehead's philosophical concepts and mathematically mapping them into computational operations inside category theory.", "tokens": [50804, 634, 311, 1940, 5552, 1934, 311, 25066, 10392, 293, 44003, 18350, 552, 666, 28270, 7705, 1854, 7719, 5261, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12026948826287383, "compression_ratio": 1.749034749034749, "no_speech_prob": 1.3503252335733684e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 96490, "start": 981.98, "end": 986.78, "text": " Right. So positive prehension is mapped mathematically to data inclusion vectors.", "tokens": [51219, 1779, 13, 407, 3353, 659, 71, 3378, 307, 33318, 44003, 281, 1412, 15874, 18875, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12026948826287383, "compression_ratio": 1.749034749034749, "no_speech_prob": 1.3503252335733684e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 96490, "start": 987.06, "end": 990.24, "text": " And negative prehension is mapped to boundary exclusion predicates.", "tokens": [51473, 400, 3671, 659, 71, 3378, 307, 33318, 281, 12866, 33049, 47336, 1024, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12026948826287383, "compression_ratio": 1.749034749034749, "no_speech_prob": 1.3503252335733684e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 99024, "start": 990.24, "end": 994.66, "text": " Exactly. Concrescence becomes a canonical collapse operation.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 18200, 495, 25434, 3643, 257, 46491, 15584, 6916, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626142528322008, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.796755561174479e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 99024, "start": 994.8, "end": 1001.32, "text": " But the subjective form, the text has a theorem explicitly called the phenomenological boundary.", "tokens": [50593, 583, 264, 25972, 1254, 11, 264, 2487, 575, 257, 20904, 20803, 1219, 264, 9388, 4383, 12866, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626142528322008, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.796755561174479e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 99024, "start": 1001.6, "end": 1001.9, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50933, 1079, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626142528322008, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.796755561174479e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 99024, "start": 1002.1, "end": 1008.14, "text": " And it proves mathematically that subjective form lies completely outside the image of the translation functor.", "tokens": [50958, 400, 309, 25019, 44003, 300, 25972, 1254, 9134, 2584, 2380, 264, 3256, 295, 264, 12853, 1019, 1672, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626142528322008, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.796755561174479e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 99024, "start": 1008.32, "end": 1010.58, "text": " It is mathematically unmappable.", "tokens": [51269, 467, 307, 44003, 517, 1696, 427, 712, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626142528322008, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.796755561174479e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 99024, "start": 1010.6800000000001, "end": 1011.1, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51387, 3153, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626142528322008, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.796755561174479e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 101110, "start": 1011.1, "end": 1017.6800000000001, "text": " And what is vital to understand here is that fliction is not writing some polemic declaring that consciousness doesn't exist.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 307, 11707, 281, 1223, 510, 307, 300, 932, 4105, 307, 406, 3579, 512, 714, 10386, 299, 40374, 300, 10081, 1177, 380, 2514, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12898596050669847, "compression_ratio": 1.6063829787234043, "no_speech_prob": 1.810847370491142e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 101110, "start": 1017.8000000000001, "end": 1020.62, "text": " Right. This isn't a philosophical argument against the soul or something.", "tokens": [50700, 1779, 13, 639, 1943, 380, 257, 25066, 6770, 1970, 264, 5133, 420, 746, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12898596050669847, "compression_ratio": 1.6063829787234043, "no_speech_prob": 1.810847370491142e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 101110, "start": 1020.72, "end": 1023.0600000000001, "text": " Not at all. It is a mathematical boundary definition.", "tokens": [50846, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 467, 307, 257, 18894, 12866, 7123, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12898596050669847, "compression_ratio": 1.6063829787234043, "no_speech_prob": 1.810847370491142e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 101110, "start": 1023.5600000000001, "end": 1028.5, "text": " The functor simply maps the structural operational parts of Whitehead's process geometry.", "tokens": [50988, 440, 1019, 1672, 2935, 11317, 264, 15067, 16607, 3166, 295, 5552, 1934, 311, 1399, 18426, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12898596050669847, "compression_ratio": 1.6063829787234043, "no_speech_prob": 1.810847370491142e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 101110, "start": 1028.76, "end": 1034.56, "text": " Because the subjective form, the feeling, doesn't modify the admissibility conditions of the math.", "tokens": [51248, 1436, 264, 25972, 1254, 11, 264, 2633, 11, 1177, 380, 16927, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 4487, 295, 264, 5221, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12898596050669847, "compression_ratio": 1.6063829787234043, "no_speech_prob": 1.810847370491142e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 101110, "start": 1034.8600000000001, "end": 1035.42, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51553, 48746, 736, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12898596050669847, "compression_ratio": 1.6063829787234043, "no_speech_prob": 1.810847370491142e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 103542, "start": 1035.42, "end": 1038.74, "text": " It doesn't induce any transformations in the geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 41263, 604, 34852, 294, 264, 18426, 13, 50531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 103542, "start": 1039.28, "end": 1046.3200000000002, "text": " Because it is purely phenomenological, it mathematically cannot cross the boundary into the structural calculus.", "tokens": [50558, 1436, 309, 307, 17491, 9388, 4383, 11, 309, 44003, 2644, 3278, 264, 12866, 666, 264, 15067, 33400, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 103542, "start": 1046.68, "end": 1050.7, "text": " Okay. I want to try an analogy here to make sure I am fully grasping the weight of this.", "tokens": [50928, 1033, 13, 286, 528, 281, 853, 364, 21663, 510, 281, 652, 988, 286, 669, 4498, 29444, 3381, 264, 3364, 295, 341, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 103542, "start": 1050.76, "end": 1054.9, "text": " Because it feels like, I don't know, a harsh stripping away of what makes us human.", "tokens": [51132, 1436, 309, 3417, 411, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 257, 14897, 3575, 3759, 1314, 295, 437, 1669, 505, 1952, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 103542, "start": 1055.0600000000002, "end": 1055.5800000000002, "text": " I get that.", "tokens": [51347, 286, 483, 300, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 103542, "start": 1055.98, "end": 1056.94, "text": " Let's hear the analogy.", "tokens": [51393, 961, 311, 1568, 264, 21663, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 103542, "start": 1057.2, "end": 1058.78, "text": " Let's say we're baking a cake.", "tokens": [51454, 961, 311, 584, 321, 434, 12102, 257, 5908, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 103542, "start": 1058.94, "end": 1059.26, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51541, 1033, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14022424871271308, "compression_ratio": 1.625984251968504, "no_speech_prob": 1.579121599107336e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 105926, "start": 1059.26, "end": 1062.0, "text": " The structural components are the raw ingredients.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15067, 6677, 366, 264, 8936, 6952, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 105926, "start": 1062.22, "end": 1063.9, "text": " The flour, the sugar, the eggs.", "tokens": [50513, 440, 7693, 11, 264, 5076, 11, 264, 6466, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 105926, "start": 1064.66, "end": 1067.06, "text": " The prehension is the mixing of those ingredients.", "tokens": [50635, 440, 659, 71, 3378, 307, 264, 11983, 295, 729, 6952, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 105926, "start": 1067.12, "end": 1067.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50758, 1779, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 105926, "start": 1067.68, "end": 1075.06, "text": " And the concrescence is the intense chemical reactions happening inside the heat of the oven, transforming that liquid batter into a solid sponge.", "tokens": [50786, 400, 264, 1588, 495, 25434, 307, 264, 9447, 7313, 12215, 2737, 1854, 264, 3738, 295, 264, 9090, 11, 27210, 300, 6553, 4220, 666, 257, 5100, 23134, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 105926, "start": 1075.14, "end": 1076.94, "text": " A very active process, yes.", "tokens": [51159, 316, 588, 4967, 1399, 11, 2086, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 105926, "start": 1076.96, "end": 1077.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51250, 1779, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 105926, "start": 1077.44, "end": 1085.22, "text": " But the subjective form of that entire process is how incredibly delicious that cake tastes to you when you eat a slice on your birthday.", "tokens": [51274, 583, 264, 25972, 1254, 295, 300, 2302, 1399, 307, 577, 6252, 4809, 300, 5908, 8666, 281, 291, 562, 291, 1862, 257, 13153, 322, 428, 6154, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 105926, "start": 1085.9, "end": 1086.94, "text": " The feeling of joy.", "tokens": [51697, 440, 2633, 295, 6258, 13, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 105926, "start": 1087.26, "end": 1087.58, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51765, 1079, 13, 51781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476029798019031, "compression_ratio": 1.7572463768115942, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 108758, "start": 1087.58, "end": 1093.74, "text": " And what Fliction is doing is writing an impossibly rigorous physics and chemistry manual for the baking process.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 3235, 4105, 307, 884, 307, 3579, 364, 38802, 3545, 29882, 10649, 293, 12558, 9688, 337, 264, 12102, 1399, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11697717813345102, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.449609529635687e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 108758, "start": 1093.82, "end": 1094.1999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50677, 7587, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11697717813345102, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.449609529635687e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 108758, "start": 1094.4399999999998, "end": 1098.52, "text": " He is mapping the thermal dynamics of the oven and the molecular bonding of the gluten.", "tokens": [50708, 634, 307, 18350, 264, 15070, 15679, 295, 264, 9090, 293, 264, 19046, 28824, 295, 264, 24326, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11697717813345102, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.449609529635687e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 108758, "start": 1098.98, "end": 1105.52, "text": " And he explicitly states in the theorem, this manual cannot and will not measure deliciousness.", "tokens": [50935, 400, 415, 20803, 4368, 294, 264, 20904, 11, 341, 9688, 2644, 293, 486, 406, 3481, 4809, 1287, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11697717813345102, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.449609529635687e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 108758, "start": 1105.52, "end": 1105.8799999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51262, 1079, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11697717813345102, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.449609529635687e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 108758, "start": 1106.0, "end": 1114.8, "text": " And if you criticize the physics manual because it doesn't explain the emotional joy of eating the cake, you have fundamentally misunderstood what the manual is for.", "tokens": [51286, 400, 498, 291, 31010, 264, 10649, 9688, 570, 309, 1177, 380, 2903, 264, 6863, 6258, 295, 3936, 264, 5908, 11, 291, 362, 17879, 33870, 437, 264, 9688, 307, 337, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11697717813345102, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.449609529635687e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 111480, "start": 1114.8, "end": 1122.9199999999998, "text": " But I have to ask, on behalf of the philosophers listening, doesn't stripping away the subjective experience defeat the whole purpose?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 286, 362, 281, 1029, 11, 322, 9490, 295, 264, 36839, 4764, 11, 1177, 380, 3575, 3759, 1314, 264, 25972, 1752, 11785, 264, 1379, 4334, 30, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2011666948145086, "compression_ratio": 1.3475177304964538, "no_speech_prob": 1.817933173789421e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 111480, "start": 1123.52, "end": 1126.56, "text": " Aren't we losing the magic of what meaning actually is?", "tokens": [50801, 15464, 380, 321, 7027, 264, 5585, 295, 437, 3620, 767, 307, 30, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2011666948145086, "compression_ratio": 1.3475177304964538, "no_speech_prob": 1.817933173789421e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 112656, "start": 1126.56, "end": 1128.22, "text": " It's a fair question.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 3143, 1168, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1871306394275866, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.775823628771822e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 112656, "start": 1128.22, "end": 1135.06, "text": " But if we look at the history of human knowledge, isolating variables is exactly how science progresses.", "tokens": [50448, 583, 498, 321, 574, 412, 264, 2503, 295, 1952, 3601, 11, 48912, 9102, 307, 2293, 577, 3497, 41929, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1871306394275866, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.775823628771822e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 112656, "start": 1135.3799999999999, "end": 1135.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50806, 1779, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1871306394275866, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.775823628771822e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 112656, "start": 1135.58, "end": 1140.36, "text": " You cannot master thermodynamics if you insist on defining heat by how it makes your skin feel.", "tokens": [50816, 509, 2644, 4505, 8810, 35483, 498, 291, 13466, 322, 17827, 3738, 538, 577, 309, 1669, 428, 3178, 841, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1871306394275866, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.775823628771822e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 112656, "start": 1141.06, "end": 1146.82, "text": " Fliction's framework allows for biological systems to possess both structural semantics and subjective experience.", "tokens": [51090, 3235, 4105, 311, 8388, 4045, 337, 13910, 3652, 281, 17490, 1293, 15067, 4361, 45298, 293, 25972, 1752, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1871306394275866, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.775823628771822e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 114682, "start": 1146.82, "end": 1152.48, "text": " But he mathematically proves that you don't need subjective experience to map the rules of the semantic relationship.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 415, 44003, 25019, 300, 291, 500, 380, 643, 25972, 1752, 281, 4471, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 47982, 2480, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14961575137244332, "compression_ratio": 1.5369458128078817, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687839904024672e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 114682, "start": 1152.58, "end": 1152.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50653, 7587, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14961575137244332, "compression_ratio": 1.5369458128078817, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687839904024672e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 114682, "start": 1153.12, "end": 1159.3, "text": " You don't need to know how the cake tastes to definitively prove whether the chemical reaction in the oven failed or succeeded.", "tokens": [50680, 509, 500, 380, 643, 281, 458, 577, 264, 5908, 8666, 281, 28152, 356, 7081, 1968, 264, 7313, 5480, 294, 264, 9090, 7612, 420, 20263, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14961575137244332, "compression_ratio": 1.5369458128078817, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687839904024672e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 114682, "start": 1159.54, "end": 1159.9399999999998, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51001, 3153, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14961575137244332, "compression_ratio": 1.5369458128078817, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687839904024672e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 114682, "start": 1160.46, "end": 1163.1399999999999, "text": " Okay, that is a profound defense of the methodology.", "tokens": [51047, 1033, 11, 300, 307, 257, 14382, 7654, 295, 264, 24850, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14961575137244332, "compression_ratio": 1.5369458128078817, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687839904024672e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 116314, "start": 1163.14, "end": 1168.3400000000001, "text": " So having stripped away this subjective taste, we are left with pure structure.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1419, 33221, 1314, 341, 25972, 3939, 11, 321, 366, 1411, 365, 6075, 3877, 13, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16794287286153653, "compression_ratio": 1.5656108597285068, "no_speech_prob": 2.343725040432343e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 116314, "start": 1168.9, "end": 1171.64, "text": " What is the actual mathematical recipe for meaning?", "tokens": [50653, 708, 307, 264, 3539, 18894, 6782, 337, 3620, 30, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16794287286153653, "compression_ratio": 1.5656108597285068, "no_speech_prob": 2.343725040432343e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 116314, "start": 1172.1000000000001, "end": 1177.42, "text": " This leads us directly into the core innovation of the text-scope geometry and the scope calculus.", "tokens": [50813, 639, 6689, 505, 3838, 666, 264, 4965, 8504, 295, 264, 2487, 12, 4417, 1114, 18426, 293, 264, 11923, 33400, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16794287286153653, "compression_ratio": 1.5656108597285068, "no_speech_prob": 2.343725040432343e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 116314, "start": 1177.5800000000002, "end": 1177.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51087, 1779, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16794287286153653, "compression_ratio": 1.5656108597285068, "no_speech_prob": 2.343725040432343e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 116314, "start": 1177.8400000000001, "end": 1182.5, "text": " This is where we leave the philosophy behind and enter the heavy mathematics of topology and algebra.", "tokens": [51100, 639, 307, 689, 321, 1856, 264, 10675, 2261, 293, 3242, 264, 4676, 18666, 295, 1192, 1793, 293, 21989, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16794287286153653, "compression_ratio": 1.5656108597285068, "no_speech_prob": 2.343725040432343e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 116314, "start": 1182.72, "end": 1183.3000000000002, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [51344, 492, 360, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16794287286153653, "compression_ratio": 1.5656108597285068, "no_speech_prob": 2.343725040432343e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 118330, "start": 1183.3, "end": 1192.3, "text": " The text treats context not as some abstract idea but as a literal geometric space, a bounded scope geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 19566, 4319, 406, 382, 512, 12649, 1558, 457, 382, 257, 20411, 33246, 1901, 11, 257, 37498, 11923, 18426, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 118330, "start": 1193.1, "end": 1193.22, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50855, 1079, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 118330, "start": 1193.4199999999998, "end": 1200.18, "text": " It argues that any context consists of three things, a boundary, which are the rules or admissibility predicates of what is allowed in.", "tokens": [50871, 467, 38218, 300, 604, 4319, 14689, 295, 1045, 721, 11, 257, 12866, 11, 597, 366, 264, 4474, 420, 5910, 891, 2841, 47336, 1024, 295, 437, 307, 4350, 294, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 118330, "start": 1200.26, "end": 1200.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51213, 1779, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 118330, "start": 1200.78, "end": 1208.0, "text": " An interior space, which is the valid states and data that live inside the rules, and the nested hierarchy of child scopes.", "tokens": [51239, 1107, 10636, 1901, 11, 597, 307, 264, 7363, 4368, 293, 1412, 300, 1621, 1854, 264, 4474, 11, 293, 264, 15646, 292, 22333, 295, 1440, 795, 30545, 13, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 118330, "start": 1208.26, "end": 1210.56, "text": " That nested hierarchy is absolutely crucial.", "tokens": [51613, 663, 15646, 292, 22333, 307, 3122, 11462, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 118330, "start": 1210.6399999999999, "end": 1211.1399999999999, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51732, 1012, 370, 30, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 118330, "start": 1211.18, "end": 1212.3799999999999, "text": " Well, think of a computer program.", "tokens": [51759, 1042, 11, 519, 295, 257, 3820, 1461, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14398718688447595, "compression_ratio": 1.6810035842293907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359659937500992e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 121238, "start": 1212.38, "end": 1213.8200000000002, "text": " You have a global environment.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 257, 4338, 2823, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 121238, "start": 1214.0200000000002, "end": 1217.3600000000001, "text": " Inside that, you have a specific function running, which is a child scope.", "tokens": [50447, 15123, 300, 11, 291, 362, 257, 2685, 2445, 2614, 11, 597, 307, 257, 1440, 11923, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 121238, "start": 1217.6200000000001, "end": 1217.8600000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50627, 1033, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 121238, "start": 1217.8600000000001, "end": 1221.8600000000001, "text": " And inside that function, you might have a temporary loop running, which is a grandchild scope.", "tokens": [50639, 400, 1854, 300, 2445, 11, 291, 1062, 362, 257, 13413, 6367, 2614, 11, 597, 307, 257, 2697, 15129, 11923, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 121238, "start": 1222.0600000000002, "end": 1222.5400000000002, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50849, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 121238, "start": 1222.6000000000001, "end": 1224.44, "text": " And a mathematical proof works the same way, right?", "tokens": [50876, 400, 257, 18894, 8177, 1985, 264, 912, 636, 11, 558, 30, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 121238, "start": 1224.46, "end": 1230.96, "text": " You have global axioms, but you can open a temporary sub-proof, make an assumption, test it, and then close it.", "tokens": [50969, 509, 362, 4338, 6360, 72, 4785, 11, 457, 291, 393, 1269, 257, 13413, 1422, 12, 15690, 11, 652, 364, 15302, 11, 1500, 309, 11, 293, 550, 1998, 309, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 121238, "start": 1231.2600000000002, "end": 1231.7, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51309, 48746, 736, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 121238, "start": 1231.96, "end": 1240.3000000000002, "text": " And the cardinal rule is that you cannot just leak variables from a temporary sub-proof out into the global proof without resolving them properly.", "tokens": [51344, 400, 264, 2920, 2071, 4978, 307, 300, 291, 2644, 445, 17143, 9102, 490, 257, 13413, 1422, 12, 15690, 484, 666, 264, 4338, 8177, 1553, 49940, 552, 6108, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 121238, "start": 1240.3000000000002, "end": 1241.9, "text": " Because that would break the geometry.", "tokens": [51761, 1436, 300, 576, 1821, 264, 18426, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1100248426398975, "compression_ratio": 1.8439490445859872, "no_speech_prob": 2.150408974152529e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 124190, "start": 1241.9, "end": 1242.9, "text": " It's a boundary violation.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 12866, 22840, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24233771023684986, "compression_ratio": 1.5133689839572193, "no_speech_prob": 1.661378174790118e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 124190, "start": 1242.9, "end": 1243.48, "text": " It's a boundary violation.", "tokens": [50415, 467, 311, 257, 12866, 22840, 13, 50444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24233771023684986, "compression_ratio": 1.5133689839572193, "no_speech_prob": 1.661378174790118e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 124190, "start": 1243.6200000000001, "end": 1244.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50451, 7587, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24233771023684986, "compression_ratio": 1.5133689839572193, "no_speech_prob": 1.661378174790118e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 124190, "start": 1244.5, "end": 1255.64, "text": " And to navigate this complex, nested geometry, to move data around without breaking the rules, the scope calculus relies on a primitive alphabet of exactly four operators.", "tokens": [50495, 400, 281, 12350, 341, 3997, 11, 15646, 292, 18426, 11, 281, 1286, 1412, 926, 1553, 7697, 264, 4474, 11, 264, 11923, 33400, 30910, 322, 257, 28540, 23339, 295, 2293, 1451, 19077, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24233771023684986, "compression_ratio": 1.5133689839572193, "no_speech_prob": 1.661378174790118e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 124190, "start": 1255.8600000000001, "end": 1257.3200000000002, "text": " I was shocked by this when I read it.", "tokens": [51063, 286, 390, 12763, 538, 341, 562, 286, 1401, 309, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24233771023684986, "compression_ratio": 1.5133689839572193, "no_speech_prob": 1.661378174790118e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 124190, "start": 1257.3400000000001, "end": 1258.02, "text": " Just four.", "tokens": [51137, 1449, 1451, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24233771023684986, "compression_ratio": 1.5133689839572193, "no_speech_prob": 1.661378174790118e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 125802, "start": 1258.02, "end": 1260.66, "text": " For all of semantic meaning.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 439, 295, 47982, 3620, 13, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 125802, "start": 1260.82, "end": 1261.1, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50505, 1079, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 125802, "start": 1261.54, "end": 1264.86, "text": " Structural minimality is a hallmark of really powerful mathematics.", "tokens": [50541, 745, 1757, 1807, 4464, 1860, 307, 257, 6500, 5638, 295, 534, 4005, 18666, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 125802, "start": 1265.18, "end": 1268.96, "text": " I mean, you only need a handful of axioms to build all of Euclidean geometry.", "tokens": [50723, 286, 914, 11, 291, 787, 643, 257, 16458, 295, 6360, 72, 4785, 281, 1322, 439, 295, 462, 1311, 31264, 282, 18426, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 125802, "start": 1269.18, "end": 1269.6, "text": " That's true.", "tokens": [50923, 663, 311, 2074, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 125802, "start": 1269.82, "end": 1274.54, "text": " Flickshenon argues that all context-preserving transformations can be reduced to four actions.", "tokens": [50955, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 266, 38218, 300, 439, 4319, 12, 14508, 20186, 34852, 393, 312, 9212, 281, 1451, 5909, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 125802, "start": 1275.32, "end": 1278.02, "text": " Bind, pop, collapse, and refuse.", "tokens": [51230, 363, 471, 11, 1665, 11, 15584, 11, 293, 16791, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20368870268476771, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 127802, "start": 1278.02, "end": 1278.4, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 50384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1913009330407897, "compression_ratio": 1.450261780104712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5122923529772847e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 127802, "start": 1278.48, "end": 1282.1, "text": " The math in this section gets incredibly dense with lambda calculus and topology.", "tokens": [50388, 440, 5221, 294, 341, 3541, 2170, 6252, 18011, 365, 13607, 33400, 293, 1192, 1793, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1913009330407897, "compression_ratio": 1.450261780104712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5122923529772847e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 127802, "start": 1282.26, "end": 1283.8, "text": " So I want to try and construct a scenario.", "tokens": [50577, 407, 286, 528, 281, 853, 293, 7690, 257, 9005, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1913009330407897, "compression_ratio": 1.450261780104712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5122923529772847e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 127802, "start": 1284.22, "end": 1289.0, "text": " Let's map a completely normal human interaction using only these four mathematical operators.", "tokens": [50675, 961, 311, 4471, 257, 2584, 2710, 1952, 9285, 1228, 787, 613, 1451, 18894, 19077, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1913009330407897, "compression_ratio": 1.450261780104712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5122923529772847e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 127802, "start": 1289.34, "end": 1290.34, "text": " I like this approach.", "tokens": [50931, 286, 411, 341, 3109, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1913009330407897, "compression_ratio": 1.450261780104712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5122923529772847e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 127802, "start": 1290.44, "end": 1291.7, "text": " It really grounds the algebra.", "tokens": [50986, 467, 534, 19196, 264, 21989, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1913009330407897, "compression_ratio": 1.450261780104712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5122923529772847e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 129170, "start": 1291.7, "end": 1294.38, "text": " Let's imagine a chaotic dinner party conversation.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 3811, 257, 27013, 6148, 3595, 3761, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 129170, "start": 1294.66, "end": 1294.94, "text": " Perfect.", "tokens": [50513, 10246, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 129170, "start": 1295.24, "end": 1297.52, "text": " So we have the global scope, which is the dinner party.", "tokens": [50542, 407, 321, 362, 264, 4338, 11923, 11, 597, 307, 264, 6148, 3595, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 129170, "start": 1297.98, "end": 1299.4, "text": " Eight people sitting around a table.", "tokens": [50679, 17708, 561, 3798, 926, 257, 3199, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 129170, "start": 1299.48, "end": 1299.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50754, 1033, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 129170, "start": 1300.0, "end": 1301.46, "text": " The first operator is bind.", "tokens": [50780, 440, 700, 12973, 307, 14786, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 129170, "start": 1302.22, "end": 1305.6200000000001, "text": " The text says this creates a dependency relation within a scope.", "tokens": [50891, 440, 2487, 1619, 341, 7829, 257, 33621, 9721, 1951, 257, 11923, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 129170, "start": 1305.72, "end": 1305.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51066, 1779, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 129170, "start": 1306.64, "end": 1312.22, "text": " So at the dinner party, I turn to you and say, hey, did you see that new sci-fi movie that came out this weekend?", "tokens": [51112, 407, 412, 264, 6148, 3595, 11, 286, 1261, 281, 291, 293, 584, 11, 4177, 11, 630, 291, 536, 300, 777, 2180, 12, 13325, 3169, 300, 1361, 484, 341, 6711, 30, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 129170, "start": 1312.56, "end": 1317.0, "text": " I've just introduced a new piece of data and actively bound our mutual attention to it.", "tokens": [51408, 286, 600, 445, 7268, 257, 777, 2522, 295, 1412, 293, 13022, 5472, 527, 16917, 3202, 281, 309, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 129170, "start": 1317.1000000000001, "end": 1317.48, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51635, 1079, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2050518576554426, "compression_ratio": 1.603448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782042777328197e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 131748, "start": 1317.48, "end": 1326.94, "text": " And if the two of us start a deep, passionate side conversation about the cinematography of that specific movie, totally ignoring the rest of the table.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 264, 732, 295, 505, 722, 257, 2452, 11, 11410, 1252, 3761, 466, 264, 43520, 5820, 295, 300, 2685, 3169, 11, 3879, 26258, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 3199, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 131748, "start": 1326.94, "end": 1331.68, "text": " We have geometrically entered a child scope, a nested context inside the dinner party.", "tokens": [50838, 492, 362, 12956, 81, 984, 9065, 257, 1440, 11923, 11, 257, 15646, 292, 4319, 1854, 264, 6148, 3595, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 131748, "start": 1331.72, "end": 1332.1200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51077, 7587, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 131748, "start": 1332.58, "end": 1332.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51120, 1033, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 131748, "start": 1332.74, "end": 1334.72, "text": " Then we have the second operator, which is pop.", "tokens": [51128, 1396, 321, 362, 264, 1150, 12973, 11, 597, 307, 1665, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 131748, "start": 1335.24, "end": 1339.66, "text": " The text says this promotes an entity from a child scope up to a parent scope.", "tokens": [51253, 440, 2487, 1619, 341, 36015, 364, 13977, 490, 257, 1440, 11923, 493, 281, 257, 2596, 11923, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 131748, "start": 1339.76, "end": 1340.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51479, 1779, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 131748, "start": 1340.6200000000001, "end": 1342.6, "text": " So we have our intense side conversation.", "tokens": [51522, 407, 321, 362, 527, 9447, 1252, 3761, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 131748, "start": 1342.76, "end": 1347.44, "text": " We come to a realization and you turn to the whole table, interrupting the global scope and say,", "tokens": [51629, 492, 808, 281, 257, 25138, 293, 291, 1261, 281, 264, 1379, 3199, 11, 49455, 264, 4338, 11923, 293, 584, 11, 51863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15393249805157, "compression_ratio": 1.7278688524590164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725778105587062e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 134748, "start": 1347.48, "end": 1348.76, "text": " we just figured it out.", "tokens": [50365, 321, 445, 8932, 309, 484, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 134748, "start": 1349.26, "end": 1352.26, "text": " The movie is actually a giant metaphor for climate change.", "tokens": [50454, 440, 3169, 307, 767, 257, 7410, 19157, 337, 5659, 1319, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 134748, "start": 1352.58, "end": 1355.52, "text": " And in doing that, I just used the pop operator.", "tokens": [50620, 400, 294, 884, 300, 11, 286, 445, 1143, 264, 1665, 12973, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 134748, "start": 1356.02, "end": 1361.3, "text": " I promoted a conclusion from our nested child scope up into the parent scope of the whole table.", "tokens": [50792, 286, 21162, 257, 10063, 490, 527, 15646, 292, 1440, 11923, 493, 666, 264, 2596, 11923, 295, 264, 1379, 3199, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 134748, "start": 1361.72, "end": 1363.58, "text": " And notice what I didn't do.", "tokens": [51077, 400, 3449, 437, 286, 994, 380, 360, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 134748, "start": 1363.94, "end": 1367.72, "text": " I didn't repeat every single word of our private five-minute chat.", "tokens": [51188, 286, 994, 380, 7149, 633, 2167, 1349, 295, 527, 4551, 1732, 12, 18256, 5081, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 134748, "start": 1367.8600000000001, "end": 1368.3, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [51384, 876, 11, 558, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 134748, "start": 1368.54, "end": 1375.04, "text": " The pop operator promotes only the admissible entity, the conclusion, while leaving all the messy scaffolding behind.", "tokens": [51418, 440, 1665, 12973, 36015, 787, 264, 5910, 41073, 13977, 11, 264, 10063, 11, 1339, 5012, 439, 264, 16191, 44094, 278, 2261, 13, 51743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 134748, "start": 1375.16, "end": 1376.1200000000001, "text": " That makes total sense.", "tokens": [51749, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1736511602634337, "compression_ratio": 1.6736842105263159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308625677876164e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 137612, "start": 1376.12, "end": 1377.84, "text": " Now, the whole table gets involved.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 264, 1379, 3199, 2170, 3288, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 137612, "start": 1378.36, "end": 1384.4399999999998, "text": " We have a loud, messy, hour-long debate about the movie, climate change, politics.", "tokens": [50477, 492, 362, 257, 6588, 11, 16191, 11, 1773, 12, 13025, 7958, 466, 264, 3169, 11, 5659, 1319, 11, 7341, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 137612, "start": 1384.78, "end": 1387.02, "text": " People are throwing out half-baked ideas.", "tokens": [50798, 3432, 366, 10238, 484, 1922, 12, 65, 7301, 3487, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 137612, "start": 1387.2199999999998, "end": 1388.34, "text": " A classic dinner party.", "tokens": [50920, 316, 7230, 6148, 3595, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 137612, "start": 1388.4399999999998, "end": 1388.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50981, 7587, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 137612, "start": 1389.1599999999999, "end": 1389.3, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51017, 865, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 137612, "start": 1389.3999999999999, "end": 1395.4399999999998, "text": " Finally, the host of the party holds up a hand and says, okay, so we all agree the visual effects were incredible, but the script was terrible.", "tokens": [51029, 6288, 11, 264, 3975, 295, 264, 3595, 9190, 493, 257, 1011, 293, 1619, 11, 1392, 11, 370, 321, 439, 3986, 264, 5056, 5065, 645, 4651, 11, 457, 264, 5755, 390, 6237, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 137612, "start": 1395.6599999999999, "end": 1396.34, "text": " Let's eat dessert.", "tokens": [51342, 961, 311, 1862, 14593, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 137612, "start": 1396.5, "end": 1396.78, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51384, 2438, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16802386517794626, "compression_ratio": 1.4758064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271445353611356e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 139678, "start": 1396.78, "end": 1398.86, "text": " That is the third operator collapse.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 2636, 12973, 15584, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18632520709121436, "compression_ratio": 1.4417177914110428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671213683688621e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 139678, "start": 1399.0, "end": 1399.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50476, 1079, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18632520709121436, "compression_ratio": 1.4417177914110428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671213683688621e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 139678, "start": 1399.96, "end": 1406.26, "text": " The host just resolved a massive, temporary argument structure into a single, canonical, agreed-upon result.", "tokens": [50524, 440, 3975, 445, 20772, 257, 5994, 11, 13413, 6770, 3877, 666, 257, 2167, 11, 46491, 11, 9166, 12, 1010, 266, 1874, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18632520709121436, "compression_ratio": 1.4417177914110428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671213683688621e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 139678, "start": 1406.68, "end": 1411.08, "text": " The messy geometry of the debate is collapsed, and the scope is formally discharged.", "tokens": [50860, 440, 16191, 18426, 295, 264, 7958, 307, 24578, 11, 293, 264, 11923, 307, 25983, 37081, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18632520709121436, "compression_ratio": 1.4417177914110428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671213683688621e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 141108, "start": 1411.08, "end": 1413.86, "text": " Which leaves the final operator, refuse.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5510, 264, 2572, 12973, 11, 16791, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529678280433912, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014833994186905e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 141108, "start": 1414.26, "end": 1418.0, "text": " This rejects a transition that violates an active boundary predicate.", "tokens": [50524, 639, 8248, 82, 257, 6034, 300, 3448, 1024, 364, 4967, 12866, 3852, 8700, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529678280433912, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014833994186905e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 141108, "start": 1418.1399999999999, "end": 1418.8799999999999, "text": " This is a fun one.", "tokens": [50718, 639, 307, 257, 1019, 472, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529678280433912, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014833994186905e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 141108, "start": 1419.06, "end": 1419.96, "text": " This one is my favorite.", "tokens": [50764, 639, 472, 307, 452, 2954, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529678280433912, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014833994186905e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 141108, "start": 1420.36, "end": 1427.02, "text": " So we're deep in this intense debate about the sci-fi movie's climate metaphor, and someone at the end of the table suddenly yells,", "tokens": [50829, 407, 321, 434, 2452, 294, 341, 9447, 7958, 466, 264, 2180, 12, 13325, 3169, 311, 5659, 19157, 11, 293, 1580, 412, 264, 917, 295, 264, 3199, 5800, 48543, 11, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529678280433912, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014833994186905e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 141108, "start": 1427.54, "end": 1429.6999999999998, "text": " my lawnmower is broken and making a clicking sound.", "tokens": [51188, 452, 19915, 76, 968, 307, 5463, 293, 1455, 257, 9697, 1626, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529678280433912, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014833994186905e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 142970, "start": 1429.7, "end": 1436.06, "text": " And the entire table just stares at them in silence for two seconds, and then immediately goes back to talking about the movie.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 2302, 3199, 445, 342, 8643, 412, 552, 294, 12239, 337, 732, 3949, 11, 293, 550, 4258, 1709, 646, 281, 1417, 466, 264, 3169, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08198681379619398, "compression_ratio": 1.5811320754716982, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688915653416015e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 142970, "start": 1436.16, "end": 1436.6000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50688, 7587, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08198681379619398, "compression_ratio": 1.5811320754716982, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688915653416015e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 142970, "start": 1437.32, "end": 1443.26, "text": " The table refused the input because it wildly violated the contextual boundary of the active scope.", "tokens": [50746, 440, 3199, 14654, 264, 4846, 570, 309, 34731, 33239, 264, 35526, 12866, 295, 264, 4967, 11923, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08198681379619398, "compression_ratio": 1.5811320754716982, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688915653416015e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 142970, "start": 1443.4, "end": 1451.82, "text": " It's a brilliant way to visualize the calculus, and what Fliction proves in the Operational Completeness Theorem is not just that these four operators exist.", "tokens": [51050, 467, 311, 257, 10248, 636, 281, 23273, 264, 33400, 11, 293, 437, 3235, 4105, 25019, 294, 264, 12480, 1478, 31804, 15264, 440, 37956, 307, 406, 445, 300, 613, 1451, 19077, 2514, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08198681379619398, "compression_ratio": 1.5811320754716982, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688915653416015e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 142970, "start": 1452.0, "end": 1452.82, "text": " What else does he prove?", "tokens": [51480, 708, 1646, 775, 415, 7081, 30, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08198681379619398, "compression_ratio": 1.5811320754716982, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688915653416015e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 145282, "start": 1452.82, "end": 1462.74, "text": " He proves mathematically that every admissible semantic transformation, whether it's a Python compiler executing code, a formal, logical proof being written,", "tokens": [50365, 634, 25019, 44003, 300, 633, 5910, 41073, 47982, 9887, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 257, 15329, 31958, 32368, 3089, 11, 257, 9860, 11, 14978, 8177, 885, 3720, 11, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1236412571925743, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109931314303716e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 145282, "start": 1463.1, "end": 1472.1, "text": " or human beings navigating a dinner party, can be exhaustively broken down into a finite sequence of bind, pop, collapse, and refuse.", "tokens": [50879, 420, 1952, 8958, 32054, 257, 6148, 3595, 11, 393, 312, 14687, 3413, 5463, 760, 666, 257, 19362, 8310, 295, 14786, 11, 1665, 11, 15584, 11, 293, 16791, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1236412571925743, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109931314303716e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 145282, "start": 1472.54, "end": 1478.9399999999998, "text": " That is just wild to think about, but there's a crucial mathematical property attached to these operators that I want to ask about.", "tokens": [51351, 663, 307, 445, 4868, 281, 519, 466, 11, 457, 456, 311, 257, 11462, 18894, 4707, 8570, 281, 613, 19077, 300, 286, 528, 281, 1029, 466, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1236412571925743, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109931314303716e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 145282, "start": 1479.26, "end": 1481.62, "text": " The text insists they are non-commutative.", "tokens": [51687, 440, 2487, 50137, 436, 366, 2107, 12, 13278, 325, 1166, 13, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1236412571925743, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109931314303716e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 148162, "start": 1481.62, "end": 1486.12, "text": " Now, I understand that in basic math, multiplication is commutative, right?", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 286, 1223, 300, 294, 3875, 5221, 11, 27290, 307, 800, 325, 1166, 11, 558, 30, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 148162, "start": 1486.2199999999998, "end": 1486.28, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50595, 865, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 148162, "start": 1486.3799999999999, "end": 1489.0, "text": " Three times four is the exact same as four times three.", "tokens": [50603, 6244, 1413, 1451, 307, 264, 1900, 912, 382, 1451, 1413, 1045, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 148162, "start": 1489.1999999999998, "end": 1489.4799999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50744, 1779, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 148162, "start": 1489.6999999999998, "end": 1492.3999999999999, "text": " But why does the order matter so much in context?", "tokens": [50769, 583, 983, 775, 264, 1668, 1871, 370, 709, 294, 4319, 30, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 148162, "start": 1492.7199999999998, "end": 1496.6399999999999, "text": " Because context is fundamentally directional and hierarchical.", "tokens": [50920, 1436, 4319, 307, 17879, 42242, 293, 35250, 804, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 148162, "start": 1497.0, "end": 1503.82, "text": " If you change the order of operations in the scope of calculus, you don't just get a different answer, you get geometric nonsense.", "tokens": [51134, 759, 291, 1319, 264, 1668, 295, 7705, 294, 264, 11923, 295, 33400, 11, 291, 500, 380, 445, 483, 257, 819, 1867, 11, 291, 483, 33246, 14925, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 148162, "start": 1504.1599999999999, "end": 1504.58, "text": " Like why?", "tokens": [51492, 1743, 983, 30, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 148162, "start": 1504.84, "end": 1506.6599999999999, "text": " Well, think back to your dinner party.", "tokens": [51526, 1042, 11, 519, 646, 281, 428, 6148, 3595, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 148162, "start": 1507.3799999999999, "end": 1511.1799999999998, "text": " Binding a topic before you pop a conclusion to the table makes total sense.", "tokens": [51653, 363, 9245, 257, 4829, 949, 291, 1665, 257, 10063, 281, 264, 3199, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1439136505126953, "compression_ratio": 1.6182965299684542, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782067713978164e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 151118, "start": 1511.18, "end": 1511.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 151118, "start": 1511.88, "end": 1516.2, "text": " But imagine trying to pop a conclusion to the table before you have bound a topic.", "tokens": [50400, 583, 3811, 1382, 281, 1665, 257, 10063, 281, 264, 3199, 949, 291, 362, 5472, 257, 4829, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 151118, "start": 1516.44, "end": 1522.1000000000001, "text": " You just stand up out of nowhere and yell, we figured out the metaphor, but you haven't even mentioned a movie yet.", "tokens": [50628, 509, 445, 1463, 493, 484, 295, 11159, 293, 20525, 11, 321, 8932, 484, 264, 19157, 11, 457, 291, 2378, 380, 754, 2835, 257, 3169, 1939, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 151118, "start": 1522.2, "end": 1523.66, "text": " Everyone would think it was insane.", "tokens": [50916, 5198, 576, 519, 309, 390, 10838, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 151118, "start": 1523.88, "end": 1524.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51000, 7587, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 151118, "start": 1524.68, "end": 1526.88, "text": " Because it's a structural boundary violation.", "tokens": [51040, 1436, 309, 311, 257, 15067, 12866, 22840, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 151118, "start": 1527.1200000000001, "end": 1530.22, "text": " The parent scope has no referent for the data you're trying to promote.", "tokens": [51162, 440, 2596, 11923, 575, 572, 2864, 317, 337, 264, 1412, 291, 434, 1382, 281, 9773, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 151118, "start": 1530.3600000000001, "end": 1532.64, "text": " You cannot collapse a scope that hasn't been opened.", "tokens": [51324, 509, 2644, 15584, 257, 11923, 300, 6132, 380, 668, 5625, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15907184208664937, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.748293025106984e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 153264, "start": 1532.64, "end": 1533.2800000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 153264, "start": 1533.92, "end": 1540.3000000000002, "text": " The non-commutative partial algebra is what enforces the strict rules of how meaning is built step by step.", "tokens": [50429, 440, 2107, 12, 13278, 325, 1166, 14641, 21989, 307, 437, 25495, 887, 264, 10910, 4474, 295, 577, 3620, 307, 3094, 1823, 538, 1823, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 153264, "start": 1540.66, "end": 1548.5800000000002, "text": " And this specific algebra is what allows the author to make the leap into the next massive conceptual area, which is category theory.", "tokens": [50766, 400, 341, 2685, 21989, 307, 437, 4045, 264, 3793, 281, 652, 264, 19438, 666, 264, 958, 5994, 24106, 1859, 11, 597, 307, 7719, 5261, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 153264, "start": 1548.7800000000002, "end": 1549.1000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51172, 1079, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 153264, "start": 1549.48, "end": 1555.8600000000001, "text": " This is where affliction elevates the scope calculus from just a local tool into a universal framework.", "tokens": [51207, 639, 307, 689, 2096, 75, 4105, 7701, 1024, 264, 11923, 33400, 490, 445, 257, 2654, 2290, 666, 257, 11455, 8388, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 153264, "start": 1556.16, "end": 1559.18, "text": " Now, category theory is often called the mathematics of mathematics, right?", "tokens": [51541, 823, 11, 7719, 5261, 307, 2049, 1219, 264, 18666, 295, 18666, 11, 558, 30, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 153264, "start": 1559.2800000000002, "end": 1559.5, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51697, 865, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456273096912312, "compression_ratio": 1.6768060836501901, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 155950, "start": 1559.5, "end": 1560.8, "text": " It's highly abstract.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 5405, 12649, 13, 50430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 155950, "start": 1561.0, "end": 1566.2, "text": " It studies mathematical structures and the mappings between them rather than the objects themselves.", "tokens": [50440, 467, 5313, 18894, 9227, 293, 264, 463, 28968, 1296, 552, 2831, 813, 264, 6565, 2969, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 155950, "start": 1566.52, "end": 1566.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50716, 1779, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 155950, "start": 1566.96, "end": 1573.24, "text": " In a category, you have objects and you have morphisms, which are the arrows or transformations that connect the objects.", "tokens": [50738, 682, 257, 7719, 11, 291, 362, 6565, 293, 291, 362, 25778, 13539, 11, 597, 366, 264, 19669, 420, 34852, 300, 1745, 264, 6565, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 155950, "start": 1573.42, "end": 1573.6, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51061, 1033, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 155950, "start": 1573.78, "end": 1576.5, "text": " So affliction constructs a formal category called scope.", "tokens": [51079, 407, 2096, 75, 4105, 7690, 82, 257, 9860, 7719, 1219, 11923, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 155950, "start": 1576.9, "end": 1582.96, "text": " The objects in this category are the bounded scope geometries, the context, the dinner parties, the software environments.", "tokens": [51235, 440, 6565, 294, 341, 7719, 366, 264, 37498, 11923, 12956, 2244, 11, 264, 4319, 11, 264, 6148, 8265, 11, 264, 4722, 12388, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14352855682373047, "compression_ratio": 1.7410358565737052, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664776554554337e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 158296, "start": 1582.96, "end": 1588.8600000000001, "text": " And the morphisms, the arrows moving between the objects, are the admissible sequences of our four operators.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 25778, 13539, 11, 264, 19669, 2684, 1296, 264, 6565, 11, 366, 264, 5910, 41073, 22978, 295, 527, 1451, 19077, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606308058196423, "compression_ratio": 1.5962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.37225983614514e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 158296, "start": 1589.28, "end": 1592.6000000000001, "text": " Bind, pop, collapse, and refuse.", "tokens": [50681, 363, 471, 11, 1665, 11, 15584, 11, 293, 16791, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606308058196423, "compression_ratio": 1.5962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.37225983614514e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 158296, "start": 1592.7, "end": 1593.22, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50852, 48746, 736, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606308058196423, "compression_ratio": 1.5962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.37225983614514e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 158296, "start": 1593.38, "end": 1601.4, "text": " And by proving that semantics forms a valid mathematical category, affliction unlocks the ability to use the most powerful theorems in modern topology.", "tokens": [50886, 400, 538, 27221, 300, 4361, 45298, 6422, 257, 7363, 18894, 7719, 11, 2096, 75, 4105, 517, 34896, 264, 3485, 281, 764, 264, 881, 4005, 10299, 2592, 294, 4363, 1192, 1793, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606308058196423, "compression_ratio": 1.5962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.37225983614514e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 158296, "start": 1601.54, "end": 1607.3, "text": " Which leads directly to the crowning philosophical achievement of the monograph, the representation invariance theorem.", "tokens": [51294, 3013, 6689, 3838, 281, 264, 11841, 278, 25066, 15838, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 11, 264, 10290, 33270, 719, 20904, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606308058196423, "compression_ratio": 1.5962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.37225983614514e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 158296, "start": 1607.58, "end": 1607.74, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51596, 865, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11606308058196423, "compression_ratio": 1.5962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.37225983614514e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 160774, "start": 1607.74, "end": 1607.96, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 50376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570213317871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5144230769230769, "no_speech_prob": 1.721457395034709e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 160774, "start": 1608.08, "end": 1609.8, "text": " I had to read this section like three times.", "tokens": [50382, 286, 632, 281, 1401, 341, 3541, 411, 1045, 1413, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570213317871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5144230769230769, "no_speech_prob": 1.721457395034709e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 160774, "start": 1610.66, "end": 1613.2, "text": " Break down the representation invariance theorem for me.", "tokens": [50511, 16925, 760, 264, 10290, 33270, 719, 20904, 337, 385, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570213317871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5144230769230769, "no_speech_prob": 1.721457395034709e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 160774, "start": 1613.44, "end": 1614.88, "text": " What does it actually prove?", "tokens": [50650, 708, 775, 309, 767, 7081, 30, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570213317871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5144230769230769, "no_speech_prob": 1.721457395034709e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 160774, "start": 1615.2, "end": 1624.08, "text": " It mathematically proves that structural semantic capacity, the ability to hold and manipulate meaning, does not care about the hardware it is running on.", "tokens": [50738, 467, 44003, 25019, 300, 15067, 47982, 6042, 11, 264, 3485, 281, 1797, 293, 20459, 3620, 11, 775, 406, 1127, 466, 264, 8837, 309, 307, 2614, 322, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570213317871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5144230769230769, "no_speech_prob": 1.721457395034709e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 160774, "start": 1624.08, "end": 1624.86, "text": " Substrate independence.", "tokens": [51182, 42090, 4404, 14640, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13570213317871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5144230769230769, "no_speech_prob": 1.721457395034709e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 162486, "start": 1624.86, "end": 1625.4799999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12931659195449327, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 2.175756319902633e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 162486, "start": 1626.1399999999999, "end": 1640.08, "text": " The theorem states that if two different computational systems can project their internal states into the category scope while preserving the admissibility rules, and their sequence of transformations reduces to the exact same canonical normal form.", "tokens": [50429, 440, 20904, 4368, 300, 498, 732, 819, 28270, 3652, 393, 1716, 641, 6920, 4368, 666, 264, 7719, 11923, 1339, 33173, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 4474, 11, 293, 641, 8310, 295, 34852, 18081, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 46491, 2710, 1254, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12931659195449327, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 2.175756319902633e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 162486, "start": 1640.1999999999998, "end": 1641.9199999999998, "text": " Then they're semantically equivalent.", "tokens": [51132, 1396, 436, 434, 4361, 49505, 10344, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12931659195449327, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 2.175756319902633e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 162486, "start": 1642.06, "end": 1646.1999999999998, "text": " They are semantically equivalent, regardless of what they are made of.", "tokens": [51225, 814, 366, 4361, 49505, 10344, 11, 10060, 295, 437, 436, 366, 1027, 295, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12931659195449327, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 2.175756319902633e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 162486, "start": 1646.24, "end": 1650.06, "text": " So you could have biological neurons firing in a human brain.", "tokens": [51434, 407, 291, 727, 362, 13910, 22027, 16045, 294, 257, 1952, 3567, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12931659195449327, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 2.175756319902633e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 162486, "start": 1650.1999999999998, "end": 1650.5, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51632, 1079, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12931659195449327, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 2.175756319902633e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 165050, "start": 1650.5, "end": 1655.72, "text": " You could have a massive symbolic logic graph running on a classical supercomputer.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 727, 362, 257, 5994, 25755, 9952, 4295, 2614, 322, 257, 13735, 36708, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192901862846627, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169150436964874e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 165050, "start": 1656.16, "end": 1656.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50648, 1779, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192901862846627, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169150436964874e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 165050, "start": 1656.66, "end": 1662.2, "text": " Or you could have artificial neurons in a trillion parameter large language model.", "tokens": [50673, 1610, 291, 727, 362, 11677, 22027, 294, 257, 18723, 13075, 2416, 2856, 2316, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192901862846627, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169150436964874e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 165050, "start": 1662.2, "end": 1671.14, "text": " If their contextual boundary transformations map perfectly to the same geometry in the category scope, they are performing the exact same semantic computation.", "tokens": [50950, 759, 641, 35526, 12866, 34852, 4471, 6239, 281, 264, 912, 18426, 294, 264, 7719, 11923, 11, 436, 366, 10205, 264, 1900, 912, 47982, 24903, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192901862846627, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169150436964874e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 165050, "start": 1671.48, "end": 1677.26, "text": " It's a rigorous mathematical proof that silicon can hold meaning just as validly as carbon.", "tokens": [51414, 467, 311, 257, 29882, 18894, 8177, 300, 22848, 393, 1797, 3620, 445, 382, 7363, 356, 382, 5954, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192901862846627, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169150436964874e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 165050, "start": 1677.64, "end": 1678.26, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51722, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192901862846627, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169150436964874e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 167826, "start": 1678.26, "end": 1683.86, "text": " Let me use another analogy to try and cement this, because substrate independence is a pretty wild concept.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 764, 1071, 21663, 281, 853, 293, 19729, 341, 11, 570, 27585, 14640, 307, 257, 1238, 4868, 3410, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22315526008605957, "compression_ratio": 1.3736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.860651173066219e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 167826, "start": 1683.98, "end": 1684.3, "text": " Go ahead.", "tokens": [50651, 1037, 2286, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22315526008605957, "compression_ratio": 1.3736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.860651173066219e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 167826, "start": 1684.3, "end": 1685.76, "text": " Think about the game of chess.", "tokens": [50667, 6557, 466, 264, 1216, 295, 24122, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22315526008605957, "compression_ratio": 1.3736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.860651173066219e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 167826, "start": 1686.0, "end": 1686.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50752, 1033, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22315526008605957, "compression_ratio": 1.3736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.860651173066219e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 167826, "start": 1686.68, "end": 1694.1, "text": " I can play chess with physical hand-carved wooden pieces on a heavy marble board, right?", "tokens": [50786, 286, 393, 862, 24122, 365, 4001, 1011, 12, 6166, 937, 14744, 3755, 322, 257, 4676, 26844, 3150, 11, 558, 30, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22315526008605957, "compression_ratio": 1.3736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.860651173066219e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 167826, "start": 1694.12, "end": 1694.8, "text": " Wow, that's sick.", "tokens": [51158, 3153, 11, 300, 311, 4998, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22315526008605957, "compression_ratio": 1.3736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.860651173066219e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 169480, "start": 1694.8, "end": 1700.5, "text": " I can play chess on a digital smartphone app, where the pieces are just pixels on a screen.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 393, 862, 24122, 322, 257, 4562, 13307, 724, 11, 689, 264, 3755, 366, 445, 18668, 322, 257, 2568, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14847927093505858, "compression_ratio": 1.5570175438596492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794590028234134e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 169480, "start": 1700.62, "end": 1700.8999999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50656, 1779, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14847927093505858, "compression_ratio": 1.5570175438596492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794590028234134e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 169480, "start": 1700.8999999999999, "end": 1709.12, "text": " Or, if I'm a grandmaster, I can play blindfold chess, holding the entire game entirely in the biological neurons of my imagination.", "tokens": [50670, 1610, 11, 498, 286, 478, 257, 2697, 21640, 11, 286, 393, 862, 44846, 24122, 11, 5061, 264, 2302, 1216, 7696, 294, 264, 13910, 22027, 295, 452, 12938, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14847927093505858, "compression_ratio": 1.5570175438596492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794590028234134e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 169480, "start": 1709.3799999999999, "end": 1710.3799999999999, "text": " Impressive, but yes.", "tokens": [51094, 8270, 22733, 11, 457, 2086, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14847927093505858, "compression_ratio": 1.5570175438596492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794590028234134e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 169480, "start": 1710.54, "end": 1713.8, "text": " The physical substrate of the game is totally different in all three scenarios.", "tokens": [51152, 440, 4001, 27585, 295, 264, 1216, 307, 3879, 819, 294, 439, 1045, 15077, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14847927093505858, "compression_ratio": 1.5570175438596492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794590028234134e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 169480, "start": 1714.46, "end": 1716.84, "text": " Wood, silicon, biology.", "tokens": [51348, 11558, 11, 22848, 11, 14956, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14847927093505858, "compression_ratio": 1.5570175438596492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794590028234134e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 171684, "start": 1716.84, "end": 1719.78, "text": " But the structural semantics of the game are identical.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 15067, 4361, 45298, 295, 264, 1216, 366, 14800, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715382984706334, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.2205192368927587e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 171684, "start": 1720.06, "end": 1720.4399999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50526, 7587, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715382984706334, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.2205192368927587e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 171684, "start": 1721.4399999999998, "end": 1733.9399999999998, "text": " The rules of how the knight moves in an L shape, the boundaries of the 8x8 grid, the contextual definition of what constitutes a checkmate, those geometries are perfectly rigidly preserved across all three substrates.", "tokens": [50595, 440, 4474, 295, 577, 264, 26054, 6067, 294, 364, 441, 3909, 11, 264, 13180, 295, 264, 1649, 87, 23, 10748, 11, 264, 35526, 7123, 295, 437, 44204, 257, 1520, 13963, 11, 729, 12956, 2244, 366, 6239, 22195, 356, 22242, 2108, 439, 1045, 4594, 12507, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715382984706334, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.2205192368927587e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 171684, "start": 1734.02, "end": 1734.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51224, 1079, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715382984706334, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.2205192368927587e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 173428, "start": 1734.28, "end": 1738.36, "text": " So, in the category of scope, all three of those games are semantically equivalent.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 294, 264, 7719, 295, 11923, 11, 439, 1045, 295, 729, 2813, 366, 4361, 49505, 10344, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13490245411696944, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272708449142302e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 173428, "start": 1739.08, "end": 1741.28, "text": " The wood doesn't make the chess more real than the pixels.", "tokens": [50605, 440, 4576, 1177, 380, 652, 264, 24122, 544, 957, 813, 264, 18668, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13490245411696944, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272708449142302e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 173428, "start": 1741.48, "end": 1744.74, "text": " That is a flawless application of the theorem, truly.", "tokens": [50725, 663, 307, 257, 45693, 3861, 295, 264, 20904, 11, 4908, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13490245411696944, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272708449142302e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 173428, "start": 1745.18, "end": 1750.26, "text": " But I have to challenge this, because this is where the AI hype train usually goes totally off the rails.", "tokens": [50910, 583, 286, 362, 281, 3430, 341, 11, 570, 341, 307, 689, 264, 7318, 24144, 3847, 2673, 1709, 3879, 766, 264, 27649, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13490245411696944, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272708449142302e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 173428, "start": 1750.3999999999999, "end": 1751.1, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51171, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13490245411696944, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272708449142302e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 173428, "start": 1751.92, "end": 1759.3999999999999, "text": " Does this theorem mean that an ancient wooden abacus and open AI's latest model are equally intelligent?", "tokens": [51247, 4402, 341, 20904, 914, 300, 364, 7832, 14744, 410, 326, 301, 293, 1269, 7318, 311, 6792, 2316, 366, 12309, 13232, 30, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13490245411696944, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272708449142302e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 175940, "start": 1759.4, "end": 1766.26, "text": " Because an abacus is a computational substrate, but calling it intelligent feels like a massive stretch.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 364, 410, 326, 301, 307, 257, 28270, 27585, 11, 457, 5141, 309, 13232, 3417, 411, 257, 5994, 5985, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19658213914042771, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234820562552321e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 175940, "start": 1766.66, "end": 1770.98, "text": " This is a vital pushback, and it highlights the strict limits of the theorem.", "tokens": [50728, 639, 307, 257, 11707, 2944, 3207, 11, 293, 309, 14254, 264, 10910, 10406, 295, 264, 20904, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19658213914042771, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234820562552321e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 175940, "start": 1771.3000000000002, "end": 1774.02, "text": " And Fliction is exceptionally careful here.", "tokens": [50960, 400, 3235, 4105, 307, 37807, 5026, 510, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19658213914042771, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234820562552321e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 175940, "start": 1774.18, "end": 1774.72, "text": " What does he say?", "tokens": [51104, 708, 775, 415, 584, 30, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19658213914042771, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234820562552321e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 175940, "start": 1775.26, "end": 1781.3000000000002, "text": " Representation invariance only proves conditional equivalence if the specific transformations map perfectly.", "tokens": [51158, 19945, 399, 33270, 719, 787, 25019, 27708, 9052, 655, 498, 264, 2685, 34852, 4471, 6239, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19658213914042771, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234820562552321e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 175940, "start": 1781.98, "end": 1788.14, "text": " It does not mean all substrates are equally powerful or efficient or capable of generating complex contexts.", "tokens": [51494, 467, 775, 406, 914, 439, 4594, 12507, 366, 12309, 4005, 420, 7148, 420, 8189, 295, 17746, 3997, 30628, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19658213914042771, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234820562552321e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 178814, "start": 1788.14, "end": 1792.18, "text": " An abacus can maintain the structural semantics of basic arithmetic.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 410, 326, 301, 393, 6909, 264, 15067, 4361, 45298, 295, 3875, 42973, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 178814, "start": 1792.8600000000001, "end": 1801.98, "text": " But an abacus does not possess the internal dimensional complexity to dynamically construct the nested child scopes required to, say, parse a Shakespearean sonnet.", "tokens": [50601, 583, 364, 410, 326, 301, 775, 406, 17490, 264, 6920, 18795, 14024, 281, 43492, 7690, 264, 15646, 292, 1440, 795, 30545, 4739, 281, 11, 584, 11, 48377, 257, 22825, 282, 1872, 7129, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 178814, "start": 1802.0800000000002, "end": 1805.5200000000002, "text": " Or to run the scope calculus operators on a medical diagnosis.", "tokens": [51062, 1610, 281, 1190, 264, 11923, 33400, 19077, 322, 257, 4625, 15217, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 178814, "start": 1805.74, "end": 1806.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51245, 7587, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 178814, "start": 1806.2, "end": 1808.66, "text": " So the abacus simply cannot build the map of the city.", "tokens": [51268, 407, 264, 410, 326, 301, 2935, 2644, 1322, 264, 4471, 295, 264, 2307, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 178814, "start": 1808.76, "end": 1810.38, "text": " It can only map a single straight line.", "tokens": [51396, 467, 393, 787, 4471, 257, 2167, 2997, 1622, 13, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 178814, "start": 1810.5200000000002, "end": 1810.92, "text": " That's right.", "tokens": [51484, 663, 311, 558, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969278482290414, "compression_ratio": 1.582375478927203, "no_speech_prob": 1.989114168515771e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 181092, "start": 1810.92, "end": 1819.0, "text": " The theorem simply proves that for the specific computations they both have the capacity to perform, their structural logic is equivalent.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 20904, 2935, 25019, 300, 337, 264, 2685, 2807, 763, 436, 1293, 362, 264, 6042, 281, 2042, 11, 641, 15067, 9952, 307, 10344, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 181092, "start": 1819.64, "end": 1823.42, "text": " It's an existence proof that meaning is not exclusive to biology.", "tokens": [50801, 467, 311, 364, 9123, 8177, 300, 3620, 307, 406, 13005, 281, 14956, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 181092, "start": 1823.92, "end": 1828.0, "text": " It's not a claim that all hardware is magically intelligent.", "tokens": [51015, 467, 311, 406, 257, 3932, 300, 439, 8837, 307, 39763, 13232, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 181092, "start": 1828.1000000000001, "end": 1828.8000000000002, "text": " You nailed it.", "tokens": [51224, 509, 30790, 309, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 181092, "start": 1829.02, "end": 1829.72, "text": " Okay, that makes sense.", "tokens": [51270, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 2020, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 181092, "start": 1829.8600000000001, "end": 1830.8400000000001, "text": " It bounds the claim.", "tokens": [51312, 467, 29905, 264, 3932, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 181092, "start": 1831.8400000000001, "end": 1835.28, "text": " But this brings us to a massive practical hurdle.", "tokens": [51411, 583, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 5994, 8496, 47423, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 181092, "start": 1835.5, "end": 1836.0600000000002, "text": " What's that?", "tokens": [51594, 708, 311, 300, 30, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14031705260276794, "compression_ratio": 1.564516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042254973024696e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 183606, "start": 1836.06, "end": 1842.6, "text": " It's beautiful in theory to say that an AI's internal state maps to this category theory geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 2238, 294, 5261, 281, 584, 300, 364, 7318, 311, 6920, 1785, 11317, 281, 341, 7719, 5261, 18426, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 183606, "start": 1843.84, "end": 1845.3, "text": " But how do we actually prove that?", "tokens": [50754, 583, 577, 360, 321, 767, 7081, 300, 30, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 183606, "start": 1845.6, "end": 1850.56, "text": " We can't just ask a massive black box language model to print out its category theory homework.", "tokens": [50842, 492, 393, 380, 445, 1029, 257, 5994, 2211, 2424, 2856, 2316, 281, 4482, 484, 1080, 7719, 5261, 14578, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 183606, "start": 1850.6799999999998, "end": 1851.78, "text": " No, we certainly can't.", "tokens": [51096, 883, 11, 321, 3297, 393, 380, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 183606, "start": 1851.84, "end": 1853.86, "text": " We have to look inside the machine while it is running.", "tokens": [51154, 492, 362, 281, 574, 1854, 264, 3479, 1339, 309, 307, 2614, 13, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 183606, "start": 1854.44, "end": 1860.06, "text": " And that is where the text shifts from abstract algebra into the gritty reality of large language models.", "tokens": [51284, 400, 300, 307, 689, 264, 2487, 19201, 490, 12649, 21989, 666, 264, 677, 10016, 4103, 295, 2416, 2856, 5245, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 183606, "start": 1860.1599999999999, "end": 1863.02, "text": " This is the transition to computational diagnostics.", "tokens": [51570, 639, 307, 264, 6034, 281, 28270, 43215, 1167, 13, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12441326691223695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 186302, "start": 1863.02, "end": 1866.24, "text": " Flitschian recognizes that pure math just isn't enough.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 1208, 339, 952, 26564, 300, 6075, 5221, 445, 1943, 380, 1547, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 186302, "start": 1866.8, "end": 1872.26, "text": " He bridges the gap by forcing a complete paradigm shift in how we view the internal workings of neural networks.", "tokens": [50554, 634, 21114, 264, 7417, 538, 19030, 257, 3566, 24709, 5513, 294, 577, 321, 1910, 264, 6920, 589, 1109, 295, 18161, 9590, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 186302, "start": 1872.68, "end": 1876.58, "text": " We have to stop looking at static points and start analyzing dynamic motion.", "tokens": [50848, 492, 362, 281, 1590, 1237, 412, 13437, 2793, 293, 722, 23663, 8546, 5394, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 186302, "start": 1876.84, "end": 1877.02, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51056, 1779, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 186302, "start": 1877.16, "end": 1878.48, "text": " Let's talk about the residual stream.", "tokens": [51072, 961, 311, 751, 466, 264, 27980, 4309, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 186302, "start": 1879.32, "end": 1888.34, "text": " In modern transformer architectures, which is what powers almost all current AI, the residual stream is essentially the central nervous system of the model, right?", "tokens": [51180, 682, 4363, 31782, 6331, 1303, 11, 597, 307, 437, 8674, 1920, 439, 2190, 7318, 11, 264, 27980, 4309, 307, 4476, 264, 5777, 6296, 1185, 295, 264, 2316, 11, 558, 30, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 186302, "start": 1888.48, "end": 1888.78, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51638, 1079, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 186302, "start": 1888.78, "end": 1892.46, "text": " It's the main artery of data flowing through the layers.", "tokens": [51653, 467, 311, 264, 2135, 38520, 295, 1412, 13974, 807, 264, 7914, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188400914846373, "compression_ratio": 1.6024844720496894, "no_speech_prob": 1.2346405365085134e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 189246, "start": 1892.46, "end": 1902.76, "text": " Traditionally, researchers view the data in this stream as a series of static vectors in a high-dimensional space, like taking coordinates on a massive graph.", "tokens": [50365, 22017, 15899, 11, 10309, 1910, 264, 1412, 294, 341, 4309, 382, 257, 2638, 295, 13437, 18875, 294, 257, 1090, 12, 18759, 1901, 11, 411, 1940, 21056, 322, 257, 5994, 4295, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14881168241086212, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.2792831030616902e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 189246, "start": 1903.0, "end": 1907.6200000000001, "text": " But Flitschian reconceptualizes this using the mathematics of discrete dynamical systems.", "tokens": [50892, 583, 3235, 1208, 339, 952, 9993, 1336, 901, 5660, 341, 1228, 264, 18666, 295, 27706, 5999, 804, 3652, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14881168241086212, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.2792831030616902e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 189246, "start": 1907.8, "end": 1908.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51132, 1033, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14881168241086212, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.2792831030616902e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 189246, "start": 1908.24, "end": 1912.46, "text": " He argues that looking at static points is completely useless for finding meaning.", "tokens": [51154, 634, 38218, 300, 1237, 412, 13437, 2793, 307, 2584, 14115, 337, 5006, 3620, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14881168241086212, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.2792831030616902e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 189246, "start": 1913.1200000000001, "end": 1915.6200000000001, "text": " We must analyze activation trajectories.", "tokens": [51398, 492, 1633, 12477, 24433, 18257, 2083, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14881168241086212, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.2792831030616902e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 189246, "start": 1916.06, "end": 1917.8, "text": " Explain an activation trajectory.", "tokens": [51545, 39574, 364, 24433, 21512, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14881168241086212, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.2792831030616902e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 191780, "start": 1917.8, "end": 1925.12, "text": " So if you have an AI model with, say, 100 layers, a single word or token does not just jump from the input straight to the output.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 291, 362, 364, 7318, 2316, 365, 11, 584, 11, 2319, 7914, 11, 257, 2167, 1349, 420, 14862, 775, 406, 445, 3012, 490, 264, 4846, 2997, 281, 264, 5598, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09832995008714128, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.661734118363345e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 191780, "start": 1925.26, "end": 1925.36, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50738, 1779, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09832995008714128, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.661734118363345e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 191780, "start": 1925.6599999999999, "end": 1933.1399999999999, "text": " As it passes through layer 1, layer 2, layer 3, its mathematical representation is massaged, refined, and shifted by the attention mechanisms.", "tokens": [50758, 1018, 309, 11335, 807, 4583, 502, 11, 4583, 568, 11, 4583, 805, 11, 1080, 18894, 10290, 307, 2758, 2980, 11, 26201, 11, 293, 18892, 538, 264, 3202, 15902, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09832995008714128, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.661734118363345e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 191780, "start": 1933.26, "end": 1934.3999999999999, "text": " And if you plot those shifts?", "tokens": [51138, 400, 498, 291, 7542, 729, 19201, 30, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09832995008714128, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.661734118363345e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 191780, "start": 1934.62, "end": 1937.76, "text": " It creates a continuous path through the high-dimensional space.", "tokens": [51206, 467, 7829, 257, 10957, 3100, 807, 264, 1090, 12, 18759, 1901, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09832995008714128, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.661734118363345e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 191780, "start": 1937.8999999999999, "end": 1939.36, "text": " That path is the trajectory.", "tokens": [51370, 663, 3100, 307, 264, 21512, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09832995008714128, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.661734118363345e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 193936, "start": 1939.36, "end": 1948.82, "text": " And suddenly, because we are looking at a path instead of a static point, we could apply the tools of physics and dynamical systems to the AI's thoughts.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 5800, 11, 570, 321, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 3100, 2602, 295, 257, 13437, 935, 11, 321, 727, 3079, 264, 3873, 295, 10649, 293, 5999, 804, 3652, 281, 264, 7318, 311, 4598, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311124013817828, "compression_ratio": 1.4578313253012047, "no_speech_prob": 1.890347904251466e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 193936, "start": 1949.0, "end": 1949.3799999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50847, 7587, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311124013817828, "compression_ratio": 1.4578313253012047, "no_speech_prob": 1.890347904251466e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 193936, "start": 1949.52, "end": 1951.6399999999999, "text": " We can measure the geometry of the motion itself.", "tokens": [50873, 492, 393, 3481, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 5394, 2564, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311124013817828, "compression_ratio": 1.4578313253012047, "no_speech_prob": 1.890347904251466e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 193936, "start": 1951.82, "end": 1954.1, "text": " The text introduces several key metrics here.", "tokens": [50988, 440, 2487, 31472, 2940, 2141, 16367, 510, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311124013817828, "compression_ratio": 1.4578313253012047, "no_speech_prob": 1.890347904251466e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 193936, "start": 1954.76, "end": 1961.34, "text": " It lists layer-wise Jacobians, discrete curvature, trajectory length, and local Lyapunov exponents.", "tokens": [51135, 467, 14511, 4583, 12, 3711, 14117, 2567, 11, 27706, 37638, 11, 21512, 4641, 11, 293, 2654, 12687, 569, 409, 5179, 12680, 791, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311124013817828, "compression_ratio": 1.4578313253012047, "no_speech_prob": 1.890347904251466e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 193936, "start": 1961.4599999999998, "end": 1961.8, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51470, 1079, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15311124013817828, "compression_ratio": 1.4578313253012047, "no_speech_prob": 1.890347904251466e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 196180, "start": 1962.4199999999998, "end": 1965.72, "text": " Let's break these down without getting totally bogged down in the equations.", "tokens": [50396, 961, 311, 1821, 613, 760, 1553, 1242, 3879, 26132, 3004, 760, 294, 264, 11787, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 196180, "start": 1966.04, "end": 1966.32, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50577, 4894, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 196180, "start": 1966.6599999999999, "end": 1975.32, "text": " A Jacobian matrix, in this context, essentially measures how the space itself is warping and stretching as the data moves from one layer to the next.", "tokens": [50608, 316, 14117, 952, 8141, 11, 294, 341, 4319, 11, 4476, 8000, 577, 264, 1901, 2564, 307, 1516, 3381, 293, 19632, 382, 264, 1412, 6067, 490, 472, 4583, 281, 264, 958, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 196180, "start": 1975.4199999999998, "end": 1976.46, "text": " And discrete curvature.", "tokens": [51046, 400, 27706, 37638, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 196180, "start": 1977.0, "end": 1980.04, "text": " That measures how jerky or smooth the path is.", "tokens": [51125, 663, 8000, 577, 20160, 4133, 420, 5508, 264, 3100, 307, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 196180, "start": 1980.28, "end": 1984.98, "text": " If a concept is moving smoothly along, refining its meaning, it has low curvature.", "tokens": [51289, 759, 257, 3410, 307, 2684, 19565, 2051, 11, 1895, 1760, 1080, 3620, 11, 309, 575, 2295, 37638, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 196180, "start": 1985.3, "end": 1986.9199999999998, "text": " And the local Lyapunov exponents?", "tokens": [51540, 400, 264, 2654, 12687, 569, 409, 5179, 12680, 791, 30, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 196180, "start": 1986.9199999999998, "end": 1990.54, "text": " They measure the rate at which nearby trajectories diverge or converge.", "tokens": [51621, 814, 3481, 264, 3314, 412, 597, 11184, 18257, 2083, 18558, 432, 420, 41881, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15074976479134908, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170658542207788e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 199054, "start": 1990.54, "end": 1996.3999999999999, "text": " So if two slightly different concepts enter a layer and are violently thrown far apart in the mathematical space...", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 732, 4748, 819, 10392, 3242, 257, 4583, 293, 366, 46728, 11732, 1400, 4936, 294, 264, 18894, 1901, 485, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 199054, "start": 1996.3999999999999, "end": 1998.04, "text": " Then the Lyapunov exponent is high.", "tokens": [50658, 1396, 264, 12687, 569, 409, 5179, 37871, 307, 1090, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 199054, "start": 1998.1599999999999, "end": 2000.92, "text": " It indicates chaos or instability in the context.", "tokens": [50746, 467, 16203, 14158, 420, 34379, 294, 264, 4319, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 199054, "start": 2001.3999999999999, "end": 2005.94, "text": " This is a total revolution for the field of mechanistic interpretability, isn't it?", "tokens": [50908, 639, 307, 257, 3217, 8894, 337, 264, 2519, 295, 4236, 3142, 7302, 2310, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 199054, "start": 2006.26, "end": 2011.7, "text": " Because historically, researchers have treated the AI brain almost like a phrenology map.", "tokens": [51151, 1436, 16180, 11, 10309, 362, 8668, 264, 7318, 3567, 1920, 411, 257, 903, 1095, 1793, 4471, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 199054, "start": 2012.02, "end": 2012.8799999999999, "text": " Oh, completely.", "tokens": [51439, 876, 11, 2584, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 199054, "start": 2013.3, "end": 2019.82, "text": " They look for a single neuron or a specific attention head that supposedly understands a specific concept.", "tokens": [51503, 814, 574, 337, 257, 2167, 34090, 420, 257, 2685, 3202, 1378, 300, 20581, 15146, 257, 2685, 3410, 13, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107002922466823, "compression_ratio": 1.6064516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984640911251291e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 201982, "start": 2019.82, "end": 2020.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 201982, "start": 2020.36, "end": 2023.04, "text": " The endless search for the Eiffel Tower neuron.", "tokens": [50392, 440, 16144, 3164, 337, 264, 462, 3661, 338, 17877, 34090, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 201982, "start": 2023.26, "end": 2023.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50537, 1779, 13, 50548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 201982, "start": 2023.9399999999998, "end": 2029.98, "text": " Like trying to find the specific microscopic scratch on a hard drive that stores your childhood memory.", "tokens": [50571, 1743, 1382, 281, 915, 264, 2685, 47897, 8459, 322, 257, 1152, 3332, 300, 9512, 428, 9278, 4675, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 201982, "start": 2030.1, "end": 2030.9399999999998, "text": " It doesn't work that way.", "tokens": [50879, 467, 1177, 380, 589, 300, 636, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 201982, "start": 2031.28, "end": 2034.74, "text": " But Fliction says meaning isn't the location you can point to.", "tokens": [50938, 583, 3235, 4105, 1619, 3620, 1943, 380, 264, 4914, 291, 393, 935, 281, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 201982, "start": 2035.3999999999999, "end": 2038.58, "text": " Meaning is the preserved geometry of the trajectory.", "tokens": [51144, 19948, 307, 264, 22242, 18426, 295, 264, 21512, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 201982, "start": 2039.1599999999999, "end": 2039.48, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51332, 1079, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 201982, "start": 2039.6, "end": 2043.98, "text": " It's like trying to understand a complex movie by looking at a single freeze frame.", "tokens": [51354, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 1223, 257, 3997, 3169, 538, 1237, 412, 257, 2167, 15959, 3920, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15951214584649778, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045742208883884e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 204398, "start": 2043.98, "end": 2044.42, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 204398, "start": 2044.96, "end": 2049.64, "text": " You might see an image of a character in that frame, but you have zero understanding of the narrative.", "tokens": [50414, 509, 1062, 536, 364, 3256, 295, 257, 2517, 294, 300, 3920, 11, 457, 291, 362, 4018, 3701, 295, 264, 9977, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 204398, "start": 2049.9, "end": 2050.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50661, 1779, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 204398, "start": 2050.14, "end": 2053.72, "text": " If you look at one layer's activation vector, you just have a freeze frame.", "tokens": [50673, 759, 291, 574, 412, 472, 4583, 311, 24433, 8062, 11, 291, 445, 362, 257, 15959, 3920, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 204398, "start": 2054.0, "end": 2055.4, "text": " You have to watch the scene play out.", "tokens": [50866, 509, 362, 281, 1159, 264, 4145, 862, 484, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 204398, "start": 2055.5, "end": 2061.26, "text": " You have to track the trajectory across the layers to see how the plot, the semantics, actually develops.", "tokens": [50941, 509, 362, 281, 2837, 264, 21512, 2108, 264, 7914, 281, 536, 577, 264, 7542, 11, 264, 4361, 45298, 11, 767, 25453, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 204398, "start": 2061.42, "end": 2062.8, "text": " It's a great way to think about it.", "tokens": [51237, 467, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 519, 466, 309, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11676262364243016, "compression_ratio": 1.6120689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 1.506811927835805e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 206280, "start": 2062.8, "end": 2075.1600000000003, "text": " Like, if a character is calmly drinking coffee in frame one and inexplicably exploding in a fireball in frame two without any logical transition, the narrative context just collapsed.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 498, 257, 2517, 307, 39740, 7583, 4982, 294, 3920, 472, 293, 29961, 4770, 1188, 35175, 294, 257, 2610, 3129, 294, 3920, 732, 1553, 604, 14978, 6034, 11, 264, 9977, 4319, 445, 24578, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 206280, "start": 2075.34, "end": 2077.96, "text": " The discrete curvature of that scene is way too high.", "tokens": [50992, 440, 27706, 37638, 295, 300, 4145, 307, 636, 886, 1090, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 206280, "start": 2078.04, "end": 2078.2400000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51127, 1779, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 206280, "start": 2078.5, "end": 2081.54, "text": " That is a very violent example of context collapse.", "tokens": [51150, 663, 307, 257, 588, 11867, 1365, 295, 4319, 15584, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 206280, "start": 2081.8, "end": 2086.0, "text": " But mathematically, it is exactly what Fliction is measuring inside the AI.", "tokens": [51315, 583, 44003, 11, 309, 307, 2293, 437, 3235, 4105, 307, 13389, 1854, 264, 7318, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 206280, "start": 2086.2000000000003, "end": 2086.7400000000002, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51535, 467, 307, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 206280, "start": 2087.0800000000004, "end": 2090.48, "text": " But here's where my brain starts to hurt a bit, and I really need you to clarify this.", "tokens": [51579, 583, 510, 311, 689, 452, 3567, 3719, 281, 4607, 257, 857, 11, 293, 286, 534, 643, 291, 281, 17594, 341, 13, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 206280, "start": 2090.5600000000004, "end": 2091.46, "text": " Okay, lean on me.", "tokens": [51753, 1033, 11, 11659, 322, 385, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10819934813444279, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493869429296757e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 209146, "start": 2091.46, "end": 2095.96, "text": " These AI vector spaces are incomprehensibly huge.", "tokens": [50365, 1981, 7318, 8062, 7673, 366, 14036, 40128, 694, 3545, 2603, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11074329926086976, "compression_ratio": 1.5780141843971631, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280073193684744e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 209146, "start": 2096.56, "end": 2102.78, "text": " The dimension size can be in the thousands, trajectories wandering through, like, a 4,000-dimensional void.", "tokens": [50620, 440, 10139, 2744, 393, 312, 294, 264, 5383, 11, 18257, 2083, 26396, 807, 11, 411, 11, 257, 1017, 11, 1360, 12, 18759, 22009, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11074329926086976, "compression_ratio": 1.5780141843971631, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280073193684744e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 209146, "start": 2102.9, "end": 2103.94, "text": " Chris, they are massive.", "tokens": [50937, 6688, 11, 436, 366, 5994, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11074329926086976, "compression_ratio": 1.5780141843971631, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280073193684744e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 209146, "start": 2104.2, "end": 2110.56, "text": " How can we possibly calculate if that path is structurally admissible, or if the AI is just randomly hallucinating in the dark?", "tokens": [51002, 1012, 393, 321, 6264, 8873, 498, 300, 3100, 307, 6594, 6512, 5910, 41073, 11, 420, 498, 264, 7318, 307, 445, 16979, 35212, 8205, 294, 264, 2877, 30, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11074329926086976, "compression_ratio": 1.5780141843971631, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280073193684744e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 209146, "start": 2110.8, "end": 2116.58, "text": " I am thrilled you asked that, because it sets up the most practical, astonishing, empirical tool in the entire monograph.", "tokens": [51332, 286, 669, 18744, 291, 2351, 300, 11, 570, 309, 6352, 493, 264, 881, 8496, 11, 35264, 11, 31886, 2290, 294, 264, 2302, 1108, 3108, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11074329926086976, "compression_ratio": 1.5780141843971631, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280073193684744e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 209146, "start": 2116.88, "end": 2117.32, "text": " Oh, awesome.", "tokens": [51636, 876, 11, 3476, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11074329926086976, "compression_ratio": 1.5780141843971631, "no_speech_prob": 2.0280073193684744e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 211732, "start": 2117.32, "end": 2124.6000000000004, "text": " To solve the problem of tracking 4,000-dimensional meaning, Fliction borrows tools from fields that have absolutely nothing to do with AI.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 5039, 264, 1154, 295, 11603, 1017, 11, 1360, 12, 18759, 3620, 11, 3235, 4105, 14828, 28251, 3873, 490, 7909, 300, 362, 3122, 1825, 281, 360, 365, 7318, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 211732, "start": 2124.8, "end": 2125.2000000000003, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [50739, 1743, 437, 30, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 211732, "start": 2125.4, "end": 2127.48, "text": " Acoustic and radar signal processing.", "tokens": [50769, 5097, 15849, 299, 293, 16544, 6358, 9007, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 211732, "start": 2127.86, "end": 2131.6400000000003, "text": " He starts treating the AI's internal thoughts like physical waves.", "tokens": [50892, 634, 3719, 15083, 264, 7318, 311, 6920, 4598, 411, 4001, 9417, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 211732, "start": 2131.94, "end": 2132.3, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51096, 1079, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 211732, "start": 2132.5800000000004, "end": 2134.32, "text": " This is where we get into the analytic signal representation.", "tokens": [51128, 639, 307, 689, 321, 483, 666, 264, 40358, 6358, 10290, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 211732, "start": 2135.1200000000003, "end": 2135.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51255, 1033, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168245246611447, "compression_ratio": 1.4279475982532752, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675429704264943e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 213536, "start": 2135.36, "end": 2144.6200000000003, "text": " Using a mathematical tool called the discrete Hilbert transform, Fliction converts the real-valued activation trajectories into complex-valued signals.", "tokens": [50365, 11142, 257, 18894, 2290, 1219, 264, 27706, 19914, 4290, 4088, 11, 3235, 4105, 38874, 264, 957, 12, 3337, 5827, 24433, 18257, 2083, 666, 3997, 12, 3337, 5827, 12354, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13185501098632812, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609816178026702e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 213536, "start": 2144.8, "end": 2145.4, "text": " Let me stop you.", "tokens": [50837, 961, 385, 1590, 291, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13185501098632812, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609816178026702e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 213536, "start": 2145.58, "end": 2147.52, "text": " What does that actually mean for the data?", "tokens": [50876, 708, 775, 300, 767, 914, 337, 264, 1412, 30, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13185501098632812, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609816178026702e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 213536, "start": 2147.88, "end": 2151.48, "text": " What does turning it into a complex signal actually give us?", "tokens": [50991, 708, 775, 6246, 309, 666, 257, 3997, 6358, 767, 976, 505, 30, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13185501098632812, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609816178026702e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 213536, "start": 2151.54, "end": 2154.46, "text": " It gives us the ability to treat a data point as a wave.", "tokens": [51174, 467, 2709, 505, 264, 3485, 281, 2387, 257, 1412, 935, 382, 257, 5772, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13185501098632812, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609816178026702e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 215446, "start": 2154.46, "end": 2162.68, "text": " And once it is a wave, we can measure three physical properties, instantaneous amplitude, instantaneous phase, and instantaneous frequency.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1564, 309, 307, 257, 5772, 11, 321, 393, 3481, 1045, 4001, 7221, 11, 45596, 27433, 11, 45596, 5574, 11, 293, 45596, 7893, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 215446, "start": 2162.9, "end": 2166.52, "text": " Okay, so we've turned the AI's internal path into a waveform.", "tokens": [50787, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 600, 3574, 264, 7318, 311, 6920, 3100, 666, 257, 36512, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 215446, "start": 2166.8, "end": 2166.98, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50982, 865, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 215446, "start": 2167.18, "end": 2173.16, "text": " And the most critical metric the text focuses on here is the PLV, the phase-locking value.", "tokens": [51001, 400, 264, 881, 4924, 20678, 264, 2487, 16109, 322, 510, 307, 264, 6999, 53, 11, 264, 5574, 12, 4102, 278, 2158, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 215446, "start": 2173.36, "end": 2175.96, "text": " PLV is the beating heart of this entire diagnostic.", "tokens": [51310, 6999, 53, 307, 264, 13497, 1917, 295, 341, 2302, 27897, 13, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 215446, "start": 2176.18, "end": 2176.7400000000002, "text": " How does it work?", "tokens": [51451, 1012, 775, 309, 589, 30, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 215446, "start": 2176.94, "end": 2180.12, "text": " Phase-locking measures the synchronization between different trajectories.", "tokens": [51489, 24432, 12, 4102, 278, 8000, 264, 19331, 2144, 1296, 819, 18257, 2083, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 215446, "start": 2180.28, "end": 2182.14, "text": " Imagine two pendulums swinging.", "tokens": [51656, 11739, 732, 12179, 425, 8099, 29500, 13, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 215446, "start": 2182.38, "end": 2182.66, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51761, 1033, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641433841926009, "compression_ratio": 1.6416382252559727, "no_speech_prob": 2.101109000327006e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 218266, "start": 2182.66, "end": 2185.3999999999996, "text": " If they swing completely independently, their phase is random.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 436, 11173, 2584, 21761, 11, 641, 5574, 307, 4974, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 218266, "start": 2185.62, "end": 2188.52, "text": " But if they sync up and swing perfectly together, they are phase-locked.", "tokens": [50513, 583, 498, 436, 20271, 493, 293, 11173, 6239, 1214, 11, 436, 366, 5574, 12, 4102, 292, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 218266, "start": 2188.72, "end": 2189.0, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50668, 2438, 13, 50682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 218266, "start": 2189.6, "end": 2192.7999999999997, "text": " And the text proposes the semantic coherence hypothesis.", "tokens": [50712, 400, 264, 2487, 2365, 4201, 264, 47982, 26528, 655, 17291, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 218266, "start": 2193.96, "end": 2203.58, "text": " It posits that when an AI is successfully reasoning, when it's holding a solid contextual boundary, the activation trajectories of its thoughts literally synchronize.", "tokens": [50930, 467, 1366, 1208, 300, 562, 364, 7318, 307, 10727, 21577, 11, 562, 309, 311, 5061, 257, 5100, 35526, 12866, 11, 264, 24433, 18257, 2083, 295, 1080, 4598, 3736, 19331, 1125, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 218266, "start": 2203.7, "end": 2206.02, "text": " They phase-lock as they move through the layers.", "tokens": [51417, 814, 5574, 12, 4102, 382, 436, 1286, 807, 264, 7914, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 218266, "start": 2206.48, "end": 2207.08, "text": " They resonate.", "tokens": [51556, 814, 34285, 13, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16280093847536573, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881472348490023e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 220708, "start": 2207.08, "end": 2209.86, "text": " And conversely, when the AI hallucinates.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2615, 736, 11, 562, 264, 7318, 35212, 259, 1024, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 220708, "start": 2210.54, "end": 2214.4, "text": " When it loses track of the prompt and starts generating confident nonsense.", "tokens": [50538, 1133, 309, 18293, 2837, 295, 264, 12391, 293, 3719, 17746, 6679, 14925, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 220708, "start": 2214.7799999999997, "end": 2217.48, "text": " The internal phase synchronization completely shatters.", "tokens": [50750, 440, 6920, 5574, 19331, 2144, 2584, 402, 37690, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 220708, "start": 2217.7799999999997, "end": 2219.08, "text": " The PLV plummets.", "tokens": [50900, 440, 6999, 53, 25854, 76, 1385, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 220708, "start": 2219.18, "end": 2221.16, "text": " The pendulum swing wildly out of control.", "tokens": [50970, 440, 44103, 11173, 34731, 484, 295, 1969, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 220708, "start": 2221.36, "end": 2221.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51079, 7587, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 220708, "start": 2221.86, "end": 2223.0, "text": " The context collapses.", "tokens": [51104, 440, 4319, 48765, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 220708, "start": 2223.3199999999997, "end": 2229.44, "text": " To measure this happening in real time, the author introduces a custom diagnostic tool called the marine operator.", "tokens": [51177, 1407, 3481, 341, 2737, 294, 957, 565, 11, 264, 3793, 31472, 257, 2375, 27897, 2290, 1219, 264, 20246, 12973, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17653388562409775, "compression_ratio": 1.5139442231075697, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465582795473834e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 222944, "start": 2229.44, "end": 2231.9, "text": " I gotta say, I love this name.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 3428, 584, 11, 286, 959, 341, 1315, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13702483475208282, "compression_ratio": 1.184782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1001546855747844e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 222944, "start": 2231.94, "end": 2235.96, "text": " It sounds very nautical, and the metaphor is entirely intentional on his part.", "tokens": [50490, 467, 3263, 588, 297, 1375, 804, 11, 293, 264, 19157, 307, 7696, 21935, 322, 702, 644, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13702483475208282, "compression_ratio": 1.184782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1001546855747844e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 223596, "start": 2235.96, "end": 2244.2400000000002, "text": " So the marine operator utilizes a salience gate to filter out background noise, and it relies heavily on calculating the Doppler velocity of the signal.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 20246, 12973, 4976, 5660, 257, 1845, 1182, 8539, 281, 6608, 484, 3678, 5658, 11, 293, 309, 30910, 10950, 322, 28258, 264, 42657, 22732, 9269, 295, 264, 6358, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 223596, "start": 2244.36, "end": 2244.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50785, 1779, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 223596, "start": 2244.94, "end": 2249.54, "text": " Doppler velocity measures how incredibly fast the local frequency of the phase signal is changing.", "tokens": [50814, 42657, 22732, 9269, 8000, 577, 6252, 2370, 264, 2654, 7893, 295, 264, 5574, 6358, 307, 4473, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 223596, "start": 2249.8, "end": 2253.2, "text": " If the frequency is stable, the AI is navigating smoothly.", "tokens": [51057, 759, 264, 7893, 307, 8351, 11, 264, 7318, 307, 32054, 19565, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 223596, "start": 2253.78, "end": 2260.82, "text": " But if the Doppler velocity suddenly spikes, it means the trajectory is accelerating wildly through the phase space.", "tokens": [51256, 583, 498, 264, 42657, 22732, 9269, 5800, 28997, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 21512, 307, 34391, 34731, 807, 264, 5574, 1901, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 223596, "start": 2261.06, "end": 2262.86, "text": " It is losing structural integrity.", "tokens": [51620, 467, 307, 7027, 15067, 16000, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 223596, "start": 2263.1, "end": 2263.4, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51722, 1079, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11419339449900501, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9887990993644467e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 226340, "start": 2263.4, "end": 2268.7400000000002, "text": " I want to use a submarine analogy here to bring this all together, because I think it perfectly captures the stakes of what this math is doing.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 528, 281, 764, 257, 33995, 21663, 510, 281, 1565, 341, 439, 1214, 11, 570, 286, 519, 309, 6239, 27986, 264, 28429, 295, 437, 341, 5221, 307, 884, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 226340, "start": 2268.9, "end": 2270.52, "text": " I love a good submarine analogy.", "tokens": [50640, 286, 959, 257, 665, 33995, 21663, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 226340, "start": 2270.7000000000003, "end": 2271.28, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [50730, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 226340, "start": 2271.44, "end": 2278.6, "text": " Let's imagine the AI's contextual boundary, scope-phiometry, is the fixed steel hull of a submarine deep underwater.", "tokens": [50767, 961, 311, 3811, 264, 7318, 311, 35526, 12866, 11, 11923, 12, 950, 72, 34730, 11, 307, 264, 6806, 8269, 32335, 295, 257, 33995, 2452, 20967, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 226340, "start": 2278.78, "end": 2279.08, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51134, 1033, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 226340, "start": 2279.48, "end": 2282.92, "text": " And the pressure outside is the chaos of the latent space.", "tokens": [51169, 400, 264, 3321, 2380, 307, 264, 14158, 295, 264, 48994, 1901, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 226340, "start": 2282.98, "end": 2283.2400000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51344, 1779, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 226340, "start": 2284.42, "end": 2288.44, "text": " The marine operator is acting like an active sonar system inside the submarine.", "tokens": [51416, 440, 20246, 12973, 307, 6577, 411, 364, 4967, 1872, 289, 1185, 1854, 264, 33995, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14298085508675412, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832637272564456e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 228844, "start": 2288.44, "end": 2295.6, "text": " It is sending acoustic pings, measuring the phase frequencies through the steel hull to check its integrity.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 7750, 26753, 280, 1109, 11, 13389, 264, 5574, 20250, 807, 264, 8269, 32335, 281, 1520, 1080, 16000, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10965294586984735, "compression_ratio": 1.5931372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045266657878e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 228844, "start": 2295.84, "end": 2296.82, "text": " A very vivid picture.", "tokens": [50735, 316, 588, 23603, 3036, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10965294586984735, "compression_ratio": 1.5931372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045266657878e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 228844, "start": 2296.98, "end": 2299.2000000000003, "text": " And what happens when the AI starts to hallucinate?", "tokens": [50792, 400, 437, 2314, 562, 264, 7318, 3719, 281, 35212, 13923, 30, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10965294586984735, "compression_ratio": 1.5931372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045266657878e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 228844, "start": 2299.4, "end": 2307.88, "text": " Well, when the AI starts to lose the context, it's like the steel hull of the submarine starting to warp and crack under the immense pressure.", "tokens": [50913, 1042, 11, 562, 264, 7318, 3719, 281, 3624, 264, 4319, 11, 309, 311, 411, 264, 8269, 32335, 295, 264, 33995, 2891, 281, 36030, 293, 6226, 833, 264, 22920, 3321, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10965294586984735, "compression_ratio": 1.5931372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045266657878e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 230788, "start": 2307.88, "end": 2317.62, "text": " The geometry is failing, and because the marine operator is constantly pinging the hull, the moment the steel starts to warp, the acoustic reflection distorts violently.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18426, 307, 18223, 11, 293, 570, 264, 20246, 12973, 307, 6460, 280, 8716, 264, 32335, 11, 264, 1623, 264, 8269, 3719, 281, 36030, 11, 264, 26753, 12914, 1483, 3299, 46728, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17529151314183286, "compression_ratio": 1.555023923444976, "no_speech_prob": 1.518626262068945e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 230788, "start": 2317.86, "end": 2319.32, "text": " The Doppler velocity spikes.", "tokens": [50864, 440, 42657, 22732, 9269, 28997, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17529151314183286, "compression_ratio": 1.555023923444976, "no_speech_prob": 1.518626262068945e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 230788, "start": 2319.6800000000003, "end": 2320.1600000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50955, 7587, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17529151314183286, "compression_ratio": 1.555023923444976, "no_speech_prob": 1.518626262068945e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 230788, "start": 2320.56, "end": 2323.7000000000003, "text": " We can literally hear the hull cracking on the sonar.", "tokens": [50999, 492, 393, 3736, 1568, 264, 32335, 25229, 322, 264, 1872, 289, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17529151314183286, "compression_ratio": 1.555023923444976, "no_speech_prob": 1.518626262068945e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 230788, "start": 2324.2200000000003, "end": 2328.08, "text": " Layers before the structural failure actually breaches the sub.", "tokens": [51182, 20084, 433, 949, 264, 15067, 7763, 767, 1403, 13272, 264, 1422, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17529151314183286, "compression_ratio": 1.555023923444976, "no_speech_prob": 1.518626262068945e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 232808, "start": 2328.08, "end": 2328.98, "text": " Which means?", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 1355, 30, 50410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 232808, "start": 2329.2, "end": 2333.08, "text": " We can predict an output error before the AI actually types the wrong word.", "tokens": [50421, 492, 393, 6069, 364, 5598, 6713, 949, 264, 7318, 767, 3467, 264, 2085, 1349, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 232808, "start": 2333.24, "end": 2333.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50623, 1079, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 232808, "start": 2333.7, "end": 2339.2999999999997, "text": " We can see the geometry fracturing in layer 40 before the hallucinated text is generated at layer 100.", "tokens": [50646, 492, 393, 536, 264, 18426, 17948, 1345, 294, 4583, 3356, 949, 264, 35212, 5410, 2487, 307, 10833, 412, 4583, 2319, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 232808, "start": 2339.48, "end": 2340.84, "text": " That is exactly the claim.", "tokens": [50935, 663, 307, 2293, 264, 3932, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 232808, "start": 2341.72, "end": 2350.84, "text": " By monitoring the declining admissibility estimates via the marine operator, we can detect a hallucination while it is still just an internal structural anomaly.", "tokens": [51047, 3146, 11028, 264, 34298, 5910, 891, 2841, 20561, 5766, 264, 20246, 12973, 11, 321, 393, 5531, 257, 35212, 2486, 1339, 309, 307, 920, 445, 364, 6920, 15067, 42737, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 232808, "start": 2350.98, "end": 2353.64, "text": " You don't have to wait for the AI to tell us the dragon is an accountant.", "tokens": [51510, 509, 500, 380, 362, 281, 1699, 337, 264, 7318, 281, 980, 505, 264, 12165, 307, 364, 43898, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 232808, "start": 2353.86, "end": 2354.2999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51654, 7587, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 232808, "start": 2354.5, "end": 2357.62, "text": " We can see the context shatter internally long before that.", "tokens": [51686, 492, 393, 536, 264, 4319, 402, 1161, 19501, 938, 949, 300, 13, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1103220283985138, "compression_ratio": 1.719869706840391, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802483421764276e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 235762, "start": 2357.62, "end": 2359.74, "text": " But this raises a massive practical issue.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 341, 19658, 257, 5994, 8496, 2734, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 235762, "start": 2360.2799999999997, "end": 2363.8199999999997, "text": " Modern LLMs are already incredibly computationally expensive, right?", "tokens": [50498, 19814, 441, 43, 26386, 366, 1217, 6252, 24903, 379, 5124, 11, 558, 30, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 235762, "start": 2363.88, "end": 2365.74, "text": " They take massive server farms to run.", "tokens": [50678, 814, 747, 5994, 7154, 20366, 281, 1190, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 235762, "start": 2365.88, "end": 2366.2999999999997, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [50778, 814, 360, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 235762, "start": 2366.48, "end": 2372.04, "text": " Doesn't calculating radar math on 4,000 dimensional waves slow the AI down to a crawl?", "tokens": [50808, 12955, 380, 28258, 16544, 5221, 322, 1017, 11, 1360, 18795, 9417, 2964, 264, 7318, 760, 281, 257, 24767, 30, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 235762, "start": 2372.2999999999997, "end": 2375.2999999999997, "text": " That is the beauty of the engineering in the final chapters.", "tokens": [51099, 663, 307, 264, 6643, 295, 264, 7043, 294, 264, 2572, 20013, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 235762, "start": 2376.08, "end": 2380.2, "text": " Fliction provides a really rigorous computational complexity analysis.", "tokens": [51288, 3235, 4105, 6417, 257, 534, 29882, 28270, 14024, 5215, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 235762, "start": 2380.46, "end": 2381.2799999999997, "text": " Okay, what did you find?", "tokens": [51507, 1033, 11, 437, 630, 291, 915, 30, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17691594727185309, "compression_ratio": 1.5207547169811322, "no_speech_prob": 2.1175717429544605e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 238128, "start": 2381.28, "end": 2393.32, "text": " Because the analytic signal conversion relies on fast Fourier transforms, the entire pipeline only requires order L log L operations per coordinate, where L is the number of layers.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 40358, 6358, 14298, 30910, 322, 2370, 36810, 35592, 11, 264, 2302, 15517, 787, 7029, 1668, 441, 3565, 441, 7705, 680, 15670, 11, 689, 441, 307, 264, 1230, 295, 7914, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 238128, "start": 2393.44, "end": 2394.32, "text": " Okay, in plain English.", "tokens": [50973, 1033, 11, 294, 11121, 3669, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 238128, "start": 2394.5400000000004, "end": 2396.84, "text": " In plain English, the math is incredibly lightweight.", "tokens": [51028, 682, 11121, 3669, 11, 264, 5221, 307, 6252, 22052, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 238128, "start": 2397.0600000000004, "end": 2398.1000000000004, "text": " It scales gracefully.", "tokens": [51154, 467, 17408, 10042, 2277, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 238128, "start": 2398.2200000000003, "end": 2398.5400000000004, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51212, 3153, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 238128, "start": 2398.6800000000003, "end": 2401.78, "text": " It requires absolutely no extra forward passes through the network.", "tokens": [51235, 467, 7029, 3122, 572, 2857, 2128, 11335, 807, 264, 3209, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 238128, "start": 2402.1400000000003, "end": 2404.2000000000003, "text": " The overhead is totally negligible.", "tokens": [51408, 440, 19922, 307, 3879, 32570, 964, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17112640852338812, "compression_ratio": 1.5537848605577689, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299905218966626e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 240420, "start": 2404.2, "end": 2409.64, "text": " You can run the sonar diagnostic continuously while the AI submarine is operating at maximum speed.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 1190, 264, 1872, 289, 27897, 15684, 1339, 264, 7318, 33995, 307, 7447, 412, 6674, 3073, 13, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1471866216415014, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490898715344147e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 240420, "start": 2409.8999999999996, "end": 2411.14, "text": " That is honestly staggering.", "tokens": [50650, 663, 307, 6095, 42974, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1471866216415014, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490898715344147e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 240420, "start": 2411.8199999999997, "end": 2414.6, "text": " A lightweight, real-time radar for AI hallucinations.", "tokens": [50746, 316, 22052, 11, 957, 12, 3766, 16544, 337, 7318, 35212, 10325, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1471866216415014, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490898715344147e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 240420, "start": 2414.7599999999998, "end": 2415.58, "text": " It's a game changer.", "tokens": [50893, 467, 311, 257, 1216, 22822, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1471866216415014, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490898715344147e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 240420, "start": 2415.8199999999997, "end": 2420.98, "text": " But as a rigorous deep dive, we have to pause here and ask the hard, cynical question.", "tokens": [50946, 583, 382, 257, 29882, 2452, 9192, 11, 321, 362, 281, 10465, 510, 293, 1029, 264, 1152, 11, 46345, 1168, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1471866216415014, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490898715344147e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 240420, "start": 2421.12, "end": 2421.8199999999997, "text": " We must.", "tokens": [51211, 492, 1633, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1471866216415014, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490898715344147e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 242182, "start": 2421.82, "end": 2425.2400000000002, "text": " Is this just a beautiful, elegant mathematical parlor trick?", "tokens": [50365, 1119, 341, 445, 257, 2238, 11, 21117, 18894, 971, 6746, 4282, 30, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 242182, "start": 2425.8, "end": 2428.26, "text": " Or is this actual, verifiable science?", "tokens": [50564, 1610, 307, 341, 3539, 11, 1306, 30876, 3497, 30, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 242182, "start": 2428.6800000000003, "end": 2434.94, "text": " Because, you know, AI research is filled with beautiful theories that fail completely when applied to real-world data.", "tokens": [50708, 1436, 11, 291, 458, 11, 7318, 2132, 307, 6412, 365, 2238, 13667, 300, 3061, 2584, 562, 6456, 281, 957, 12, 13217, 1412, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 242182, "start": 2435.34, "end": 2437.28, "text": " It is the most important question we can ask.", "tokens": [51041, 467, 307, 264, 881, 1021, 1168, 321, 393, 1029, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 242182, "start": 2437.52, "end": 2438.82, "text": " And Fliction anticipates it.", "tokens": [51150, 400, 3235, 4105, 10416, 1024, 309, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 242182, "start": 2439.2200000000003, "end": 2445.0800000000004, "text": " He dedicates an immense amount of effort in the final section of the monograph to ensuring his own theory can be destroyed.", "tokens": [51235, 634, 37071, 1024, 364, 22920, 2372, 295, 4630, 294, 264, 2572, 3541, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 281, 16882, 702, 1065, 5261, 393, 312, 8937, 13, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 242182, "start": 2445.44, "end": 2446.6600000000003, "text": " Scientific falsification.", "tokens": [51546, 47437, 16720, 3774, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511478172158296, "compression_ratio": 1.5598591549295775, "no_speech_prob": 1.797021624387607e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 244666, "start": 2446.66, "end": 2449.16, "text": " Yes, Karl Popper's gold standard.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 20405, 10215, 610, 311, 3821, 3832, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14930490904216526, "compression_ratio": 1.5258215962441315, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144694951926054e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 244666, "start": 2449.92, "end": 2452.44, "text": " A theory that explains everything explains nothing.", "tokens": [50528, 316, 5261, 300, 13948, 1203, 13948, 1825, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14930490904216526, "compression_ratio": 1.5258215962441315, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144694951926054e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 244666, "start": 2452.92, "end": 2458.56, "text": " It must make specific, testable predictions that, if proven wrong, bring the whole framework down.", "tokens": [50678, 467, 1633, 652, 2685, 11, 1500, 712, 21264, 300, 11, 498, 12785, 2085, 11, 1565, 264, 1379, 8388, 760, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14930490904216526, "compression_ratio": 1.5258215962441315, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144694951926054e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 244666, "start": 2458.66, "end": 2463.94, "text": " And the text mandates explicit, brutal statistical falsification protocols.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 264, 2487, 48662, 13691, 11, 17878, 22820, 16720, 3774, 20618, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14930490904216526, "compression_ratio": 1.5258215962441315, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144694951926054e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 244666, "start": 2464.12, "end": 2464.6, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51238, 467, 775, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14930490904216526, "compression_ratio": 1.5258215962441315, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144694951926054e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 244666, "start": 2464.8999999999996, "end": 2467.7799999999997, "text": " It states that if you run the marine operator on an AI,", "tokens": [51277, 467, 4368, 300, 498, 291, 1190, 264, 20246, 12973, 322, 364, 7318, 11, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14930490904216526, "compression_ratio": 1.5258215962441315, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144694951926054e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 246778, "start": 2467.78, "end": 2476.6800000000003, "text": " the phase-locking value of correct, logical reasoning traces must be statistically higher than the PLV of hallucinated traces.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 5574, 12, 4102, 278, 2158, 295, 3006, 11, 14978, 21577, 26076, 1633, 312, 36478, 2946, 813, 264, 6999, 53, 295, 35212, 5410, 26076, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 246778, "start": 2476.96, "end": 2477.1000000000004, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50824, 1779, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 246778, "start": 2477.36, "end": 2481.0, "text": " And it demands this be tested using independent statistical methods,", "tokens": [50844, 400, 309, 15107, 341, 312, 8246, 1228, 6695, 22820, 7150, 11, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 246778, "start": 2481.6200000000003, "end": 2486.38, "text": " specifically mentioning Mann-Whitney-U test at a strict alpha level of 0.01.", "tokens": [51057, 4682, 18315, 16892, 12, 2471, 270, 2397, 12, 52, 1500, 412, 257, 10910, 8961, 1496, 295, 1958, 13, 10607, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 246778, "start": 2486.6800000000003, "end": 2491.4, "text": " Let's explain why that specific test and that specific alpha level actually matter.", "tokens": [51310, 961, 311, 2903, 983, 300, 2685, 1500, 293, 300, 2685, 8961, 1496, 767, 1871, 13, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 246778, "start": 2491.5400000000004, "end": 2491.9, "text": " Please do.", "tokens": [51553, 2555, 360, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 246778, "start": 2492.1800000000003, "end": 2497.1600000000003, "text": " A Mann-Whitney-U test is a non-parametric test used to compare differences between two independent groups.", "tokens": [51585, 316, 16892, 12, 2471, 270, 2397, 12, 52, 1500, 307, 257, 2107, 12, 2181, 335, 17475, 1500, 1143, 281, 6794, 7300, 1296, 732, 6695, 3935, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1326703378709696, "compression_ratio": 1.7240143369175627, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956280571659653e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 249716, "start": 2497.16, "end": 2500.14, "text": " In this case, good reasoning versus hallucinations.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 1389, 11, 665, 21577, 5717, 35212, 10325, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 249716, "start": 2500.66, "end": 2506.8599999999997, "text": " Setting the alpha to 0.01 means he is demanding a 99% confidence level", "tokens": [50540, 21063, 264, 8961, 281, 1958, 13, 10607, 1355, 415, 307, 19960, 257, 11803, 4, 6687, 1496, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 249716, "start": 2506.8599999999997, "end": 2510.3999999999996, "text": " that the difference in phase-locking isn't just some random fluke.", "tokens": [50850, 300, 264, 2649, 294, 5574, 12, 4102, 278, 1943, 380, 445, 512, 4974, 5029, 330, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 249716, "start": 2510.54, "end": 2510.7999999999997, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51034, 3153, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 249716, "start": 2510.98, "end": 2514.42, "text": " He is setting an incredibly high bar for failure.", "tokens": [51056, 634, 307, 3287, 364, 6252, 1090, 2159, 337, 7763, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 249716, "start": 2515.04, "end": 2520.62, "text": " No moving the goalposts, no tweaking the parameters to make the data look slightly better for a publication.", "tokens": [51259, 883, 2684, 264, 3387, 23744, 82, 11, 572, 6986, 2456, 264, 9834, 281, 652, 264, 1412, 574, 4748, 1101, 337, 257, 19953, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 249716, "start": 2520.8399999999997, "end": 2521.68, "text": " And it goes further.", "tokens": [51549, 400, 309, 1709, 3052, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 249716, "start": 2522.04, "end": 2523.96, "text": " It mandates strict control experiments.", "tokens": [51609, 467, 48662, 10910, 1969, 12050, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15885966678835312, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427469615668214e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 252396, "start": 2523.96, "end": 2526.32, "text": " It isn't enough to just find a signal.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1943, 380, 1547, 281, 445, 915, 257, 6358, 13, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 252396, "start": 2526.7200000000003, "end": 2529.34, "text": " You have to prove the signal means what you think it means.", "tokens": [50503, 509, 362, 281, 7081, 264, 6358, 1355, 437, 291, 519, 309, 1355, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 252396, "start": 2529.58, "end": 2529.7400000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50646, 7587, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 252396, "start": 2529.94, "end": 2534.96, "text": " For instance, the text says you must compare the PLV against simple softmax entropy.", "tokens": [50664, 1171, 5197, 11, 264, 2487, 1619, 291, 1633, 6794, 264, 6999, 53, 1970, 2199, 2787, 41167, 30867, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 252396, "start": 2535.56, "end": 2541.32, "text": " Now, softmax entropy is basically just the AI's base confidence level in its next word, right?", "tokens": [50945, 823, 11, 2787, 41167, 30867, 307, 1936, 445, 264, 7318, 311, 3096, 6687, 1496, 294, 1080, 958, 1349, 11, 558, 30, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 252396, "start": 2541.34, "end": 2541.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51234, 1779, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 252396, "start": 2541.6, "end": 2546.38, "text": " So, Fliction is saying you must prove my complex radar tool is actually better than just asking the AI,", "tokens": [51247, 407, 11, 3235, 4105, 307, 1566, 291, 1633, 7081, 452, 3997, 16544, 2290, 307, 767, 1101, 813, 445, 3365, 264, 7318, 11, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 252396, "start": 2546.54, "end": 2547.38, "text": " hey, are you sure?", "tokens": [51494, 4177, 11, 366, 291, 988, 30, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17569197927202498, "compression_ratio": 1.585551330798479, "no_speech_prob": 2.3342491134448196e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 254738, "start": 2547.38, "end": 2550.08, "text": " That's hilarious, but so necessary.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 19796, 11, 457, 370, 4818, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 254738, "start": 2550.48, "end": 2556.44, "text": " And my absolute favorite control experiment is the mandate to randomly permute the phase values.", "tokens": [50520, 400, 452, 8236, 2954, 1969, 5120, 307, 264, 23885, 281, 16979, 4784, 1169, 264, 5574, 4190, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 254738, "start": 2556.7000000000003, "end": 2557.02, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50831, 1079, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 254738, "start": 2557.46, "end": 2558.2400000000002, "text": " That one is brilliant.", "tokens": [50869, 663, 472, 307, 10248, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 254738, "start": 2558.58, "end": 2561.34, "text": " Explain how that works, because it's such a clever way to test the structure.", "tokens": [50925, 39574, 577, 300, 1985, 11, 570, 309, 311, 1270, 257, 13494, 636, 281, 1500, 264, 3877, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 254738, "start": 2561.6400000000003, "end": 2565.04, "text": " Well, if you think the synchronization of the waves, the phase-locking,", "tokens": [51078, 1042, 11, 498, 291, 519, 264, 19331, 2144, 295, 264, 9417, 11, 264, 5574, 12, 4102, 278, 11, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 254738, "start": 2565.12, "end": 2567.08, "text": " is what actually carries the semantic meaning,", "tokens": [51252, 307, 437, 767, 16402, 264, 47982, 3620, 11, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 254738, "start": 2567.56, "end": 2569.52, "text": " you have to prove it isn't just background noise.", "tokens": [51374, 291, 362, 281, 7081, 309, 1943, 380, 445, 3678, 5658, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 254738, "start": 2569.88, "end": 2570.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51490, 1779, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 254738, "start": 2570.26, "end": 2573.96, "text": " So you take the data, and you randomly scramble the timing of the phases.", "tokens": [51509, 407, 291, 747, 264, 1412, 11, 293, 291, 16979, 795, 48382, 264, 10822, 295, 264, 18764, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 254738, "start": 2574.3, "end": 2575.2000000000003, "text": " You permute them.", "tokens": [51711, 509, 4784, 1169, 552, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 254738, "start": 2575.34, "end": 2576.28, "text": " You just mix it all up.", "tokens": [51763, 509, 445, 2890, 309, 439, 493, 13, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17988793166367323, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519452022943474e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 257628, "start": 2576.28, "end": 2576.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 257628, "start": 2577.2400000000002, "end": 2581.0400000000004, "text": " If you scramble the phases, and the AI's performance stays exactly the same,", "tokens": [50413, 759, 291, 795, 48382, 264, 18764, 11, 293, 264, 7318, 311, 3389, 10834, 2293, 264, 912, 11, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 257628, "start": 2581.1800000000003, "end": 2585.4, "text": " or if the signal you thought you found is still there, then your theory is garbage.", "tokens": [50610, 420, 498, 264, 6358, 291, 1194, 291, 1352, 307, 920, 456, 11, 550, 428, 5261, 307, 14150, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 257628, "start": 2585.98, "end": 2587.76, "text": " The synchronization didn't actually matter.", "tokens": [50850, 440, 19331, 2144, 994, 380, 767, 1871, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 257628, "start": 2588.0, "end": 2588.2000000000003, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [50951, 876, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 257628, "start": 2588.48, "end": 2591.26, "text": " But if you scramble the phases, and the PLV drops to zero,", "tokens": [50975, 583, 498, 291, 795, 48382, 264, 18764, 11, 293, 264, 6999, 53, 11438, 281, 4018, 11, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 257628, "start": 2591.92, "end": 2595.1800000000003, "text": " and the ability to predict the hallucination vanishes...", "tokens": [51147, 293, 264, 3485, 281, 6069, 264, 35212, 2486, 3161, 16423, 485, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 257628, "start": 2595.1800000000003, "end": 2600.78, "text": " You have successfully proven that the synchronization was the actual physical carrier of the structural meaning.", "tokens": [51310, 509, 362, 10727, 12785, 300, 264, 19331, 2144, 390, 264, 3539, 4001, 17574, 295, 264, 15067, 3620, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 257628, "start": 2601.2200000000003, "end": 2601.7000000000003, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51612, 48746, 736, 13, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 257628, "start": 2601.84, "end": 2605.7400000000002, "text": " It is methodological humility, and honestly, it is deeply appreciated.", "tokens": [51643, 467, 307, 3170, 4383, 27106, 11, 293, 6095, 11, 309, 307, 8760, 17169, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.169500642150413, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980712846780376e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 260574, "start": 2605.74, "end": 2606.64, "text": " It's rare.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 5892, 13, 50410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 260574, "start": 2607.0, "end": 2607.3399999999997, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50428, 467, 307, 13, 50445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 260574, "start": 2607.7599999999998, "end": 2611.64, "text": " Volumes one and two of this monograph are mathematical proofs.", "tokens": [50466, 8911, 10018, 472, 293, 732, 295, 341, 1108, 3108, 366, 18894, 8177, 82, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 260574, "start": 2611.64, "end": 2615.9599999999996, "text": " They are conditionally true based on the axioms of topology and category theory.", "tokens": [50660, 814, 366, 4188, 379, 2074, 2361, 322, 264, 6360, 72, 4785, 295, 1192, 1793, 293, 7719, 5261, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 260574, "start": 2616.02, "end": 2616.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50879, 1779, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 260574, "start": 2616.7999999999997, "end": 2620.22, "text": " But volume three is a vulnerable empirical research program.", "tokens": [50918, 583, 5523, 1045, 307, 257, 10955, 31886, 2132, 1461, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 260574, "start": 2620.64, "end": 2624.3399999999997, "text": " It requires messy, real-world data to survive.", "tokens": [51110, 467, 7029, 16191, 11, 957, 12, 13217, 1412, 281, 7867, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526688600197816, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980708509971686e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 262434, "start": 2624.34, "end": 2630.1600000000003, "text": " Which is exactly why the final pages detailing the scope limits or non-claims are so refreshing.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 2293, 983, 264, 2572, 7183, 42459, 264, 11923, 10406, 420, 2107, 12, 66, 10970, 82, 366, 370, 19772, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941180419921875, "compression_ratio": 1.1428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842638375096923e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 263016, "start": 2630.16, "end": 2638.3199999999997, "text": " In today's AI hype cycle, every new paper claims to be, like, the secret spark that will ignite artificial general intelligence.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 965, 311, 7318, 24144, 6586, 11, 633, 777, 3035, 9441, 281, 312, 11, 411, 11, 264, 4054, 9908, 300, 486, 49609, 11677, 2674, 7599, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362631554697074, "compression_ratio": 1.348993288590604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 263016, "start": 2638.64, "end": 2638.8599999999997, "text": " Hmm.", "tokens": [50789, 8239, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362631554697074, "compression_ratio": 1.348993288590604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 263016, "start": 2639.02, "end": 2643.18, "text": " But fiction explicitly states what this framework does not do.", "tokens": [50808, 583, 13266, 20803, 4368, 437, 341, 8388, 775, 406, 360, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362631554697074, "compression_ratio": 1.348993288590604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 263016, "start": 2643.2799999999997, "end": 2643.68, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51021, 1079, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362631554697074, "compression_ratio": 1.348993288590604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 264368, "start": 2643.68, "end": 2645.5, "text": " He states it does not explain AGI.", "tokens": [50365, 634, 4368, 309, 775, 406, 2903, 316, 26252, 13, 50456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17322121168437757, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045699924999157e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 264368, "start": 2646.18, "end": 2649.62, "text": " It does not attempt to model biological realism in the human brain.", "tokens": [50490, 467, 775, 406, 5217, 281, 2316, 13910, 38484, 294, 264, 1952, 3567, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17322121168437757, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045699924999157e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 264368, "start": 2650.1, "end": 2654.54, "text": " It makes of absolutely no claims about ethics, morality, or alignment.", "tokens": [50686, 467, 1669, 295, 3122, 572, 9441, 466, 19769, 11, 29106, 11, 420, 18515, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17322121168437757, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045699924999157e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 264368, "start": 2655.0, "end": 2660.56, "text": " And it reiterates that it does not prove or even attempt to approach the question of whether the AI is conscious.", "tokens": [50931, 400, 309, 25211, 1024, 300, 309, 775, 406, 7081, 420, 754, 5217, 281, 3109, 264, 1168, 295, 1968, 264, 7318, 307, 6648, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17322121168437757, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045699924999157e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 264368, "start": 2660.8199999999997, "end": 2661.7599999999998, "text": " It bounds the problem.", "tokens": [51222, 467, 29905, 264, 1154, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17322121168437757, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045699924999157e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 266176, "start": 2661.76, "end": 2671.5, "text": " Just like the scope geometry it studies, a good scientific theory must draw a rigid boundary around its interior space and refuse to leak into domains it hasn't earned the right to speak on.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 411, 264, 11923, 18426, 309, 5313, 11, 257, 665, 8134, 5261, 1633, 2642, 257, 22195, 12866, 926, 1080, 10636, 1901, 293, 16791, 281, 17143, 666, 25514, 309, 6132, 380, 12283, 264, 558, 281, 1710, 322, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08740535704027705, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.56739931363864e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 266176, "start": 2671.6400000000003, "end": 2677.5, "text": " It is the difference between a tech CEO standing on a stage making philosophical declarations that the AI is alive.", "tokens": [50859, 467, 307, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 7553, 9282, 4877, 322, 257, 3233, 1455, 25066, 16694, 763, 300, 264, 7318, 307, 5465, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08740535704027705, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.56739931363864e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 266176, "start": 2677.5800000000004, "end": 2687.32, "text": " And a rigorous scientist saying, if this specific Hilbert transform doesn't yield a p-value less than 0.01 on this specific data set, my sonar tool is useless.", "tokens": [51156, 400, 257, 29882, 12662, 1566, 11, 498, 341, 2685, 19914, 4290, 4088, 1177, 380, 11257, 257, 280, 12, 29155, 1570, 813, 1958, 13, 10607, 322, 341, 2685, 1412, 992, 11, 452, 1872, 289, 2290, 307, 14115, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08740535704027705, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.56739931363864e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 266176, "start": 2687.5400000000004, "end": 2688.0200000000004, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51654, 7587, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08740535704027705, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.56739931363864e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 266176, "start": 2688.0200000000004, "end": 2691.6800000000003, "text": " So we have covered an immense theoretical journey today.", "tokens": [51678, 407, 321, 362, 5343, 364, 22920, 20864, 4671, 965, 13, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08740535704027705, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 1.56739931363864e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 269176, "start": 2691.76, "end": 2696.96, "text": " But we really must ask the pragmatic question, what does this all mean for the immediate future?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 321, 534, 1633, 1029, 264, 46904, 1168, 11, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 264, 11629, 2027, 30, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 269176, "start": 2697.1000000000004, "end": 2697.96, "text": " Where is this applied?", "tokens": [50632, 2305, 307, 341, 6456, 30, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 269176, "start": 2698.46, "end": 2708.36, "text": " Well, because the marine operator is computationally lightweight, and because it operates entirely on the residual stream without needing to alter the foundational training data,", "tokens": [50700, 1042, 11, 570, 264, 20246, 12973, 307, 24903, 379, 22052, 11, 293, 570, 309, 22577, 7696, 322, 264, 27980, 4309, 1553, 18006, 281, 11337, 264, 32195, 3097, 1412, 11, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 269176, "start": 2708.92, "end": 2714.9, "text": " these diagnostics could be implemented in open-weight models immediately, like tomorrow.", "tokens": [51223, 613, 43215, 1167, 727, 312, 12270, 294, 1269, 12, 12329, 5245, 4258, 11, 411, 4153, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 269176, "start": 2715.26, "end": 2718.0200000000004, "text": " Imagine the architectural shift that there brings.", "tokens": [51540, 11739, 264, 26621, 5513, 300, 456, 5607, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 269176, "start": 2718.28, "end": 2720.6200000000003, "text": " We could build self-correcting AI.", "tokens": [51691, 492, 727, 1322, 2698, 12, 19558, 2554, 278, 7318, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 269176, "start": 2720.98, "end": 2721.36, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51826, 1079, 13, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16189669654482886, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 2.020629974106014e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 272136, "start": 2721.36, "end": 2726.52, "text": " The system generates a complex chain of thought attempting to solve a coding problem.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 23815, 257, 3997, 5021, 295, 1194, 22001, 281, 5039, 257, 17720, 1154, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11320579199143398, "compression_ratio": 1.6311111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.084583157133113e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 272136, "start": 2727.2000000000003, "end": 2730.58, "text": " And in the background, the marine operator is just pinging the trajectory.", "tokens": [50657, 400, 294, 264, 3678, 11, 264, 20246, 12973, 307, 445, 280, 8716, 264, 21512, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11320579199143398, "compression_ratio": 1.6311111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.084583157133113e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 272136, "start": 2731.06, "end": 2739.5, "text": " And the moment it detects the internal phase locks beginning to drift, the moment the Doppler velocity spikes and the submarine hull starts to crack under the complexity of the code.", "tokens": [50850, 400, 264, 1623, 309, 5531, 82, 264, 6920, 5574, 20703, 2863, 281, 19699, 11, 264, 1623, 264, 42657, 22732, 9269, 28997, 293, 264, 33995, 32335, 3719, 281, 6226, 833, 264, 14024, 295, 264, 3089, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11320579199143398, "compression_ratio": 1.6311111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.084583157133113e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 272136, "start": 2739.6400000000003, "end": 2740.84, "text": " The AI hits the brakes.", "tokens": [51279, 440, 7318, 8664, 264, 19950, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11320579199143398, "compression_ratio": 1.6311111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.084583157133113e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 274084, "start": 2740.84, "end": 2741.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.338107497603805, "compression_ratio": 1.1477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489058603421202e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 274084, "start": 2741.28, "end": 2743.88, "text": " It applies the refuse operator from the scope calculus.", "tokens": [50387, 467, 13165, 264, 16791, 12973, 490, 264, 11923, 33400, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.338107497603805, "compression_ratio": 1.1477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489058603421202e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 274084, "start": 2743.88, "end": 2746.06, "text": " It recognizes its own geometric failure.", "tokens": [50517, 467, 26564, 1080, 1065, 33246, 7763, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.338107497603805, "compression_ratio": 1.1477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489058603421202e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 274606, "start": 2746.06, "end": 2754.96, "text": " It pauses, backtracks to the last admissible geometric state, and recalculates its trajectory before it ever outputs the hallucinated code to the user.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2502, 8355, 11, 646, 6903, 7424, 281, 264, 1036, 5910, 41073, 33246, 1785, 11, 293, 850, 304, 2444, 1024, 1080, 21512, 949, 309, 1562, 23930, 264, 35212, 5410, 3089, 281, 264, 4195, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07703506319146407, "compression_ratio": 1.2905982905982907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552528661964439e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 275496, "start": 2754.96, "end": 2761.7400000000002, "text": " We move from an era of AI that confidently hallucinates to an era of AI that mathematically knows when it has lost the plot.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1286, 490, 364, 4249, 295, 7318, 300, 41956, 35212, 259, 1024, 281, 364, 4249, 295, 7318, 300, 44003, 3255, 562, 309, 575, 2731, 264, 7542, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463996825679656, "compression_ratio": 1.2916666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582848797411456e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 276174, "start": 2761.74, "end": 2764.8199999999997, "text": " That is a staggering paradigm shift for reliability.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 42974, 24709, 5513, 337, 24550, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.380756604044061, "compression_ratio": 0.9420289855072463, "no_speech_prob": 2.150411142556874e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 276174, "start": 2764.8999999999996, "end": 2765.7799999999997, "text": " It truly is.", "tokens": [50523, 467, 4908, 307, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.380756604044061, "compression_ratio": 0.9420289855072463, "no_speech_prob": 2.150411142556874e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 276578, "start": 2765.78, "end": 2772.92, "text": " Okay, let's take a breath and recap this incredible journey, because we have covered a massive amount of conceptual ground today.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 6045, 293, 20928, 341, 4651, 4671, 11, 570, 321, 362, 5343, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 24106, 2727, 965, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16418022428240095, "compression_ratio": 1.25, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017361892001652e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 276578, "start": 2773.0600000000004, "end": 2773.94, "text": " We really have.", "tokens": [50729, 492, 534, 362, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16418022428240095, "compression_ratio": 1.25, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017361892001652e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 277394, "start": 2773.94, "end": 2777.52, "text": " We started by confronting the paradox of AI understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 538, 47449, 264, 26221, 295, 7318, 3701, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12046093493700027, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 2.076433859923843e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 277394, "start": 2778.28, "end": 2787.52, "text": " We used the disentanglement operator to untangle the subjective phenomenological feeling of meaning from the rigorous geometric preservation of context.", "tokens": [50582, 492, 1143, 264, 37313, 656, 3054, 12973, 281, 1701, 7846, 264, 25972, 9388, 4383, 2633, 295, 3620, 490, 264, 29882, 33246, 27257, 295, 4319, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12046093493700027, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 2.076433859923843e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 277394, "start": 2787.58, "end": 2791.94, "text": " We realized we don't need to know how the cake tastes to understand the chemistry of the baking process.", "tokens": [51047, 492, 5334, 321, 500, 380, 643, 281, 458, 577, 264, 5908, 8666, 281, 1223, 264, 12558, 295, 264, 12102, 1399, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12046093493700027, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 2.076433859923843e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 279194, "start": 2791.94, "end": 2792.94, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1957030679987765, "compression_ratio": 1.6072727272727272, "no_speech_prob": 1.77608535517626e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 279194, "start": 2792.94, "end": 2804.36, "text": " We then explored how structural semantics evolved from Sosu's linguistic networks and Whitehead's process philosophy, translating events and prehensions into pure mathematics.", "tokens": [50415, 492, 550, 24016, 577, 15067, 4361, 45298, 14178, 490, 318, 329, 84, 311, 43002, 9590, 293, 5552, 1934, 311, 1399, 10675, 11, 35030, 3931, 293, 659, 71, 8302, 666, 6075, 18666, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1957030679987765, "compression_ratio": 1.6072727272727272, "no_speech_prob": 1.77608535517626e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 279194, "start": 2804.36, "end": 2809.86, "text": " And we established the four primitive operators of the scope calculus POP, bind, collapse, and refuse.", "tokens": [50986, 400, 321, 7545, 264, 1451, 28540, 19077, 295, 264, 11923, 33400, 430, 12059, 11, 14786, 11, 15584, 11, 293, 16791, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1957030679987765, "compression_ratio": 1.6072727272727272, "no_speech_prob": 1.77608535517626e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 279194, "start": 2809.86, "end": 2817.7200000000003, "text": " We elevated those operators into category theory, proving with a representation invariance theorem that structural understanding is substrate independent.", "tokens": [51261, 492, 23457, 729, 19077, 666, 7719, 5261, 11, 27221, 365, 257, 10290, 33270, 719, 20904, 300, 15067, 3701, 307, 27585, 6695, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1957030679987765, "compression_ratio": 1.6072727272727272, "no_speech_prob": 1.77608535517626e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 281772, "start": 2817.72, "end": 2831.08, "text": " Right. Whether you're a human brain playing blindfold chess or a massive language model running on silicon, if you preserve the geometric boundaries of the context, you're performing the exact same valid semantic computation.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 8503, 291, 434, 257, 1952, 3567, 2433, 44846, 24122, 420, 257, 5994, 2856, 2316, 2614, 322, 22848, 11, 498, 291, 15665, 264, 33246, 13180, 295, 264, 4319, 11, 291, 434, 10205, 264, 1900, 912, 7363, 47982, 24903, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09901344776153564, "compression_ratio": 1.5864406779661018, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105433802876995e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 281772, "start": 2831.58, "end": 2838.72, "text": " And finally, we brought that abstract math down to Earth, applying it to the dynamic activation trajectories of modern transformers.", "tokens": [51058, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 3038, 300, 12649, 5221, 760, 281, 4755, 11, 9275, 309, 281, 264, 8546, 24433, 18257, 2083, 295, 4363, 4088, 433, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09901344776153564, "compression_ratio": 1.5864406779661018, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105433802876995e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 281772, "start": 2839.4599999999996, "end": 2845.72, "text": " Using radar-like analytic signals and the marine operator to detect the shattering of phase-locked coherence.", "tokens": [51452, 11142, 16544, 12, 4092, 40358, 12354, 293, 264, 20246, 12973, 281, 5531, 264, 402, 14849, 295, 5574, 12, 4102, 292, 26528, 655, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09901344776153564, "compression_ratio": 1.5864406779661018, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105433802876995e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 284572, "start": 2845.72, "end": 2851.16, "text": " Allowing us to predict structural context collapse before hallucination ever occurs.", "tokens": [50365, 1057, 9637, 505, 281, 6069, 15067, 4319, 15584, 949, 35212, 2486, 1562, 11843, 13, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14272430737813313, "compression_ratio": 1.4090909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 2.176297987308007e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 284572, "start": 2851.3399999999997, "end": 2852.16, "text": " It's quite a ride.", "tokens": [50646, 467, 311, 1596, 257, 5077, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14272430737813313, "compression_ratio": 1.4090909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 2.176297987308007e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 284572, "start": 2852.5, "end": 2861.8399999999997, "text": " And the true value here for you, the listener, is that you now possess a remarkably powerful new mental model for how information works.", "tokens": [50704, 400, 264, 2074, 2158, 510, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 307, 300, 291, 586, 17490, 257, 37381, 4005, 777, 4973, 2316, 337, 577, 1589, 1985, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14272430737813313, "compression_ratio": 1.4090909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 2.176297987308007e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 284572, "start": 2862.12, "end": 2862.6, "text": " You do.", "tokens": [51185, 509, 360, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14272430737813313, "compression_ratio": 1.4090909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 2.176297987308007e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 286260, "start": 2862.6, "end": 2877.08, "text": " The next time you're using an AI and it suddenly hallucinates a bizarre, nonsensical answer, or honestly, even the next time a human conversation completely derails at a chaotic dinner party, you don't have to just throw your hands up at a mystical failure of intelligence.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 958, 565, 291, 434, 1228, 364, 7318, 293, 309, 5800, 35212, 259, 1024, 257, 18265, 11, 297, 892, 694, 804, 1867, 11, 420, 6095, 11, 754, 264, 958, 565, 257, 1952, 3761, 2584, 1163, 6227, 412, 257, 27013, 6148, 3595, 11, 291, 500, 380, 362, 281, 445, 3507, 428, 2377, 493, 412, 257, 40565, 7763, 295, 7599, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07080625876402244, "compression_ratio": 1.506726457399103, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183838766325233e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 286260, "start": 2877.22, "end": 2880.3399999999997, "text": " No, you can view it clearly as a geometric boundary violation.", "tokens": [51096, 883, 11, 291, 393, 1910, 309, 4448, 382, 257, 33246, 12866, 22840, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07080625876402244, "compression_ratio": 1.506726457399103, "no_speech_prob": 1.8183838766325233e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 288034, "start": 2880.34, "end": 2890.6000000000004, "text": " Exactly. You can see it as a failure to pop the right conclusion, to bind the relevant variable, to collapse the messy argument, or to refuse the inappropriate input.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 509, 393, 536, 309, 382, 257, 7763, 281, 1665, 264, 558, 10063, 11, 281, 14786, 264, 7340, 7006, 11, 281, 15584, 264, 16191, 6770, 11, 420, 281, 16791, 264, 26723, 4846, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08820584479798661, "compression_ratio": 1.5348837209302326, "no_speech_prob": 1.455293784785594e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 288034, "start": 2890.7200000000003, "end": 2893.2400000000002, "text": " The hull of the context simply cracked under pressure.", "tokens": [50884, 440, 32335, 295, 264, 4319, 2935, 25140, 833, 3321, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08820584479798661, "compression_ratio": 1.5348837209302326, "no_speech_prob": 1.455293784785594e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 288034, "start": 2893.6000000000004, "end": 2897.2400000000002, "text": " It gives a rigorous, beautiful structure to the chaos of communication.", "tokens": [51028, 467, 2709, 257, 29882, 11, 2238, 3877, 281, 264, 14158, 295, 6101, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08820584479798661, "compression_ratio": 1.5348837209302326, "no_speech_prob": 1.455293784785594e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 288034, "start": 2897.84, "end": 2902.1200000000003, "text": " But before we sign off, I want to leave you with one final, deeply provocative thought.", "tokens": [51240, 583, 949, 321, 1465, 766, 11, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 472, 2572, 11, 8760, 47663, 1194, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08820584479798661, "compression_ratio": 1.5348837209302326, "no_speech_prob": 1.455293784785594e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 288034, "start": 2902.2200000000003, "end": 2902.82, "text": " Oh, I'm ready.", "tokens": [51459, 876, 11, 286, 478, 1919, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08820584479798661, "compression_ratio": 1.5348837209302326, "no_speech_prob": 1.455293784785594e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 290282, "start": 2902.82, "end": 2910.92, "text": " Something to mull over that wasn't explicitly spelled out in the main text, but that this entire mathematical framework inevitably points toward.", "tokens": [50365, 6595, 281, 275, 858, 670, 300, 2067, 380, 20803, 34388, 484, 294, 264, 2135, 2487, 11, 457, 300, 341, 2302, 18894, 8388, 28171, 2793, 7361, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08862943852201421, "compression_ratio": 1.55956678700361, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437468148081889e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 290282, "start": 2911.0, "end": 2911.6000000000004, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [50774, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08862943852201421, "compression_ratio": 1.55956678700361, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437468148081889e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 290282, "start": 2912.0, "end": 2925.28, "text": " If semantic structure is purely geometric, and if we can map it using the scope calculus and detect its stability using these phase locks, what happens when we intentionally construct non-Euclidean semantic spaces?", "tokens": [50824, 759, 47982, 3877, 307, 17491, 33246, 11, 293, 498, 321, 393, 4471, 309, 1228, 264, 11923, 33400, 293, 5531, 1080, 11826, 1228, 613, 5574, 20703, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 321, 22062, 7690, 2107, 12, 36, 1311, 31264, 282, 47982, 7673, 30, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08862943852201421, "compression_ratio": 1.55956678700361, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437468148081889e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 290282, "start": 2925.6000000000004, "end": 2929.6600000000003, "text": " Oh, wow. That is a terrifyingly fascinating implication.", "tokens": [51504, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 663, 307, 257, 18106, 356, 10343, 37814, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08862943852201421, "compression_ratio": 1.55956678700361, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437468148081889e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 292966, "start": 2929.66, "end": 2938.42, "text": " Right. I mean, human reasoning, our dinner party conversations, our legal arguments, they all rely on a certain flat Euclidean geometry of logic.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 286, 914, 11, 1952, 21577, 11, 527, 6148, 3595, 7315, 11, 527, 5089, 12869, 11, 436, 439, 10687, 322, 257, 1629, 4962, 462, 1311, 31264, 282, 18426, 295, 9952, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1174096445883474, "compression_ratio": 1.546712802768166, "no_speech_prob": 1.701387837040047e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 292966, "start": 2938.52, "end": 2941.02, "text": " Cause and effect, linear progression, intuitive physics.", "tokens": [50808, 10865, 293, 1802, 11, 8213, 18733, 11, 21769, 10649, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1174096445883474, "compression_ratio": 1.546712802768166, "no_speech_prob": 1.701387837040047e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 292966, "start": 2941.08, "end": 2945.5, "text": " Exactly. But these neural networks are operating in thousands of dimensions simultaneously.", "tokens": [50936, 7587, 13, 583, 613, 18161, 9590, 366, 7447, 294, 5383, 295, 12819, 16561, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1174096445883474, "compression_ratio": 1.546712802768166, "no_speech_prob": 1.701387837040047e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 292966, "start": 2946.3399999999997, "end": 2955.94, "text": " What if we train an AI to preserve contextual boundaries that curve, warp, and intersect in ways the biological human brain physically cannot visualize?", "tokens": [51199, 708, 498, 321, 3847, 364, 7318, 281, 15665, 35526, 13180, 300, 7605, 11, 36030, 11, 293, 27815, 294, 2098, 264, 13910, 1952, 3567, 9762, 2644, 23273, 30, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1174096445883474, "compression_ratio": 1.546712802768166, "no_speech_prob": 1.701387837040047e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 295594, "start": 2955.94, "end": 2968.7200000000003, "text": " What alien forms of reasoning, completely incomprehensible to our linear logic, might exist in stable, mathematically admissible geometric scopes that we simply haven't mapped yet?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 12319, 6422, 295, 21577, 11, 2584, 14036, 40128, 30633, 281, 527, 8213, 9952, 11, 1062, 2514, 294, 8351, 11, 44003, 5910, 41073, 33246, 795, 30545, 300, 321, 2935, 2378, 380, 33318, 1939, 30, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04200387682233538, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179318727468141e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 295594, "start": 2968.8, "end": 2976.98, "text": " We might be building perfectly sound submarines, but designing them to navigate deep, multidimensional oceans of thought that we can't even conceive of.", "tokens": [51008, 492, 1062, 312, 2390, 6239, 1626, 48138, 11, 457, 14685, 552, 281, 12350, 2452, 11, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 25004, 295, 1194, 300, 321, 393, 380, 754, 48605, 295, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04200387682233538, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179318727468141e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 297698, "start": 2976.98, "end": 2987.36, "text": " And thanks to Fliction's math, the x-ray machine will show us that the structure is completely stable and mathematically true, even if our human minds can never understand the picture it takes.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 3231, 281, 3235, 4105, 311, 5221, 11, 264, 2031, 12, 3458, 3479, 486, 855, 505, 300, 264, 3877, 307, 2584, 8351, 293, 44003, 2074, 11, 754, 498, 527, 1952, 9634, 393, 1128, 1223, 264, 3036, 309, 2516, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0658954938252767, "compression_ratio": 1.570281124497992, "no_speech_prob": 2.125938531119531e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 297698, "start": 2987.48, "end": 2989.04, "text": " That is something to keep you up at night.", "tokens": [50890, 663, 307, 746, 281, 1066, 291, 493, 412, 1818, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0658954938252767, "compression_ratio": 1.570281124497992, "no_speech_prob": 2.125938531119531e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 297698, "start": 2989.16, "end": 2996.02, "text": " It really is. Thank you so much for taking this deep dive with us today. Keep questioning the boundaries of your own context, and we'll see you next time.", "tokens": [50974, 467, 534, 307, 13, 1044, 291, 370, 709, 337, 1940, 341, 2452, 9192, 365, 505, 965, 13, 5527, 21257, 264, 13180, 295, 428, 1065, 4319, 11, 293, 321, 603, 536, 291, 958, 565, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0658954938252767, "compression_ratio": 1.570281124497992, "no_speech_prob": 2.125938531119531e-12}], "language": "en"}
